body:
[Prop 20 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] Assume that $\bbQ$ satisfies the $\alpha$-mixing condition~\eqref{eq:AlphaMixingCondition} with $\alpha > d(d-1)/2$. Then, for every $\varepsilon >0$ there exists $q>0$ that for $\bbQ$-a.e.\ $\omega \in \Omega_{\lambda,\Lambda}$
    \begin{equation}

        \lim_{N \to \infty} \inf_{z \in \cC_N}\frac{1}{|B_z|}\sum_{y \in B_z} \IND_{\{ g^\omega_{U_z}(y,y) \geq \overline{g} - \varepsilon \}} \geq q \,.
    \end{equation}

