body:
[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2609.02283, 'The game chromatic number of generalized Mycielski graphs of paths and cycles'] For $k\geq2$, the following statements hold for generalized Mycielski graphs of paths:

\begin{enumerate}[label={\upshape(\arabic*)},
                  nosep,
                  leftmargin=*]
\item $\chi_g(M_k(P_2))=3$;
\item $\chi_g(M_k(P_3))=3$;
\item $\chi_g(M_k(P_4))=3$;
\item $\chi_g(M_k(P_n))\geq4$ for $n\geq5$.
\end{enumerate}

