{"artifact_digest":"sha256:46685268b7ab5e7a8a4ce0ad857fb9b9fbed3d8933729a3d99cf7a0d6d824671","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/46/46685268b7ab5e7a8a4ce0ad857fb9b9fbed3d8933729a3d99cf7a0d6d824671.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:a8fd0654cdbae2fb1d03c55b4f268f73601fd4c73b06af111aa096738c24916a","bundle_entry_key":"2605-14149-lemma-24-sigma-moments","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_048","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_048.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-14149-lemma-24-sigma-moments","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: For the first part, recall that $\bm{\sigma}^n(k) = \varepsilon^n(k) \bm{Z}^n(k) - \bm{b}^n(k-1)$ and $\bm{b}^n(k-1) = {\mathbb E}[\varepsilon^n(k)\bm{Z}^n(k)\,|\,{\mathcal G}^n(k)]$. Thus,
	\begin{align*}
		\mathrm{Cov}(\bm{\sigma}^n(k)\,|\,{\mathcal G}^n(k-1)) &= {\mathbb E}\big[\varepsilon^n(k)^2 \bm{Z}^n(k)\bm{Z}^n(k)^\top\,\big|\,{\mathcal G}^n(k-1)\big] - \bm{b}^n(k-1)\bm{b}^n(k-1)^\top \\
	&= \frac{1}{n} I_n - \bm{b}^n(k-1)\bm{b}^n(k-1)^\top.
	\end{align*}
