[Definition def:gamma:summing of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] An operator \( A \in \mathcal{L}(H,X) \) is \emph{\( \gamma \)-summing} if
    \begin{equation} 
        \sup_{(h_k)_{k=1}^n \in \mathcal{F}(H)} \int_\Omega \left\| \sum_{k=1}^n \xi_k(\omega) A h_k \right\|^2 \mu(d\omega) < \infty.
