[Theorem 79 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $U_1, U_2, \ldots, U_m$ be independent $U[0, 1]$ variables, and denote by $U(1), U(2), \ldots , U(m)$ the order statistics, i.e.\ $U(1) \leq U(2) \leq \ldots \leq U(m)$. If $X_1, X_2, \ldots, X_{m+1}$  are $(m + 1)$ independent standard exponentials (also independent of the $U_i$, $1 \leq i \leq m$), then
\begin{equation*}
    \big( U(1), U(2), \ldots, U(m) \big) \stackrel{(d)}{=} \Big( \frac{X_1}{\sum_{i=1}^{m+1} X_i}, \frac{X_1 + X_2}{\sum_{i=1}^{m+1} X_i}, \ldots, \frac{\sum_{i=1}^m X_i}{\sum_{i=1}^{m+1} X_i}\Big).
\end{equation*}

