for a.e. $x\in\R^{N}$ and all $n\ge1$. Since $c + l|u|$ belongs to $L^{2}(\R^{N})$, the dominated convergence theorem implies \eqref{conv-fn}. Observe that for any $n\ge 1$, the mapping $F_{n}$ satisfies the Lipschitz condition 
