[Definition 2 of arXiv:2607.17177, '2607.17177'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1)$ and $T>0$. We say that equation \eqref{control equation} is $\alpha$-null controllable in time $T$ if there exists a constant $C>0$ such that, for any $y\in H$, there exists $h\in L^2(0,T;U)$ satisfying
\begin{equation*}
    \|Y_T\|\leq \alpha\|y\|,\qquad\|h\|_{L^2(0,T;U)}\leq C\|y\|.
