along with its analytic dependence on the complex parameter $z$,
can be obtained by expanding the arguments used in the proof of Theorem \ref{Thm-spectral-gap}. 
This adaptation is analogous to the standard treatment of group actions on function spaces; for a detailed reference, see \cite[Lemma 11.16]{BQ16b}. 


 To establish the spectral gap property, we introduce a $z$-dependent deformation of the original bundle action. 
For each $z \in \bb C$, we define a new action of $G$ on the total space $E$ by setting,
