body:
[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.15616, '\textbf{Compact Support Property of Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift}'] For any $T>0$ we have 
		\begin{equation}
			\sup_{n\geq 1} \E_f[R^n_T] \leq \E_f[R^0_T] +T^{1/2} \sqrt{2\pi b_1 \constFromEq{c}{eq:est_v_infty_1}}\sqrt{\E_f[R^0_T]}+ \sqrt{\E_f[R_T^0]} \sum_{i=1}^\infty a_i(T) <\infty, 
		\end{equation}
		where 
		\begin{equation}
			a_i(T):=   \sqrt{\frac{4\pi \constFromEq{c}{eq:est_v_infty_1}}{3} \constFromEq{c}{eq:est_W_time_int}^ib_1^{i+1} \Big( \prod_{k = 2}^i w_{k+2} \Big)T^\frac{i+2}{2}},
		\end{equation}
    with the convention that $\prod_{k=2}^1w_{k+2} =1$.

