[Corollary 8 (High-noise decay of the smoothed likelihood force) of arXiv:2608.21709, 'Posterior Information Dynamics of Diffusion Models for Linear Inverse Problems'] Under the assumptions of Lemma~\ref{thm:posterior-tweedie}, the force
\(g_t\) satisfies, under the joint law of \((X_t,R)\),
\begin{equation}

\E\|g_t(X_t,R)\|^2
=
\frac{a_t^2}{\Delta_t^2}
\E\big\|\E[X_0\mid X_t,R]-\E[X_0\mid X_t]\big\|^2.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}

\E\|g_t(X_t,R)\|^2
\le
\frac{a_t^2}{\Delta_t^2}\Tr\Cov(X_0).
\end{equation}
Consequently, along any dimension sequence for which
\(d^{-1}\Tr\Cov(X_0)=O(1)\), and on any high-noise window where
\(\Delta_t\ge \Delta_0>0\),
\begin{equation}

\frac1d\E\|g_t(X_t,R)\|^2=O(a_t^2).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

