body:
[Lemma tiling slope of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] For all $ x \in X$, 
    \begin{equation}  
    \limsup_{r \rightarrow \infty} \frac{D(c_{\mathcal{R}}(x, re_i), e)}{r} \leq 2
    \end{equation} 
    for $ i =1,2$.

[Corollary of arXiv:2609.00840, 'Kählerity of complete almost-Kähler gradient shrinking Ricci solitons'] Let $(M^4,g,J,\omega,f)$ be a four-dimensional complete almost-K\"ahler gradient shrinking Ricci soliton. Then $(M^4,g,J,\omega,f)$ is, biholomorphic-isometric, one of the following:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item [(a)] a closed del Pezzo surface with its unique K\"ahler--Einstein or K\"ahler--Ricci shrinker metric;

		\item [(b)] the Gaussian shrinker $(\mathbb C^2,g_E)$;

		\item [(c)] the FIK shrinker on the blow-up of $\mathbb C^2$ at the origin;

		\item [(d)] the standard product shrinker $(\mathbb{CP}^1\times\mathbb C,g_c)$;

		\item [(e)] the BCCD shrinker on the one-point blow-up of $\mathbb{CP}^1\times\mathbb C$.
	\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 6 (Parabolic Moment Estimates) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumption \ref{ass:coefficients} hold. For any real exponent $m\ge2$, there exists a constant $K_m > 0$ such that the mild solution $X(\cdot; t, x)$ introduced in Definition \ref{def:mild_solution} satisfies the inequality:
\begin{equation} 

    \E \left[ \sup_{s \in [t, T]} \|X(s; t, x)\|_H^m \right] \le K_m \left( 1 + \|x\|_H^m \right),
\end{equation}
for all initial conditions $(t, x) \in [0, T] \times H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

