[Prop planarity of arXiv:2609.02346, 'Regularised double shuffle relations for planar \AZVs{}'] Let $(S,T)\in\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}^{\rm conv} \times \mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}^{\rm conv}$ (resp. $(S,T)\in\mathcal{PT}_{\{x,y\}}^{\rm conv} \times \mathcal{PT}_{\{x,y\}}^{\rm conv}$). Then
    \begin{equation*}
        F_{\N^*}(S)=F_{\N^*}(T)~\Longrightarrow~\zeta^T(S)=\zeta^T(T)\quad\left(\text{\normalfont{resp. } }F_{\{x,y\}}(S)=F_{\{x,y\}}(T)~\Longrightarrow~\zeta_\shuffle^T(S)=\zeta_\shuffle^T(T)~\right).
    \end{equation*}
    We call these relations the \emph{planarity relations}.

[Prop EHI:p:SbmCounterex of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t \geq 0} = (B_{S_t})_{t \geq 0}$ be a subordinate Brownian motion. For all $s>0$, let $T^{\{s\}} := \inf\{ t : \Delta S(t) > s \}$. Suppose there exist sequences $(s_n)$ and $(r_n)$ of positive numbers such that
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $s_n \ll r_n^2$.
        \item $1 \gg \mathbb{P}_0(\tau_{B(0, r_n)} < T^{\{s_n\}}) \gg \mathbb{P}_0 (|\Delta X(T^{\{s_n\}})| \leq 36 r_n)$.
    \end{itemize}
    Then $X$ does not satisfy $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}$. Furthermore, if $r_n \to 0$ along a subsequence then $X$ does not satisfy $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}(r \leq 1)$, and if $r_n \to \infty$ along a subsequence then $X$ does not satisfy $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}(r \geq 1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

