[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2605.31088, 'On couplings for kinetic Langevin diffusions'] Let $(Z_k,\tilde Z_k)_{k\in \N}$ be given by the iterated one-shot coupling defined in Section~\ref{sssec: iterated one-shot} applied to the Markov chains~\eqref{eq: linear Markov chain}. For $k\in \N$ consider the event $\{Z_{k-1}\neq\tilde Z_{k-1}\}$, i.e.\ the event that the chains have not met before the $k^{\text{th}}$ step. On this event we have that
     \begin{equation*}
         e_{k}=\frac{B_{k}^{-1}
         \Pi_{k}\Delta z}{\l|B_{k}^{-1}\Pi_{k}\Delta z\r|},
     \end{equation*}
    where $\Pi_{k}\coloneqq A_{k}A_{k-1}\dots A_1$.

