body:
[Lemma lem3.4 of arXiv:2411.06089, '{\Large \bf Averaging principle for semilinear slow-fast rough partial differential equati'] For any given $x,x_1,x_2,y\in \mathcal{H}$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that
\begin{align}
	&\sup_{t\geq0}\widetilde{\mathbb E}\|Y_t^{x_1,y}-Y_t^{x_2,y}\|_{\mathcal{H}}^2\leq C\|x_1-x_2\|_{\mathcal{H} }^2, \\
	&\sup_{t\geq0}\widetilde{\mathbb E}\|Y^{x,y}_t\|_{\mathcal{H}}^2\leq C(1+\|x\|_{\mathcal{H} }^2+\|y\|_{\mathcal{H}}^2).
\end{align}

