body:
[Lemma 56 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] For~$q'\in \{q_0,q_\infty\}$ and~$p'\in \{p_0,p_\infty\}$, the~$1$-forms~$\omega_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}$ and~$\omega_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}$ are meromorphic~$1$-forms with simple poles at~$q'$ and~$p'$ and no other poles. Moreover, their residues are given by
\begin{equation*}
\int_{\mathcal C_{q'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}=-\int_{\mathcal C_{p'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}=c_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
\int_{\mathcal C_{q'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}=-\int_{\mathcal C_{p'}}\omega_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}=c_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{equation*}
c_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z}=
\begin{footnotesize}
\begin{cases}
a\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_0, p'=p_0, \\
\i\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_0, p'=p_\infty, \\
-\i\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_0, \\
-a\sqrt{a^2+1}, & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_\infty, \\
\end{cases}
\end{footnotesize}
\quad 
c_{q',p'}^{\vartheta}=
\begin{footnotesize}
\begin{cases}
-a(a+\i), & q'=q_0, p'=p_0, \\
\i(a+\i), & q'=q_0, p'=p_\infty, \\
\i(a+\i), & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_0, \\
-a(a+\i), & q'=q_\infty, p'=p_\infty, \\
\end{cases}
\end{footnotesize}
\end{equation*}
and~$\mathcal C_{q'}$ and~$\mathcal C_{p'}$ are positively oriented small circles in~$\mathcal R$ around~$q'$ and~$p'$, respectively.

