body:
[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2512.05340, 'The rate of convergence of the critical mean-field $O(N)$ magnetization via multivariate n'] Let $V$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{assumption: assumptions on V} and let $P_t$ denote the semigroup corresponding to~\eqref{eq: overdamped langevin}.  
  Fix $h \in\smoothlip$, and define
  \begin{equation}
    f(x):=-\int_{0}^{\infty}[P_{t}h(x) - \mu(h)]\, \dt.
  \end{equation}
  Then $f \in C^2(\RR^{d})$, and for all $x,u,v\in\RR^d$ 
    \begin{equation}
      D_{u}f(x) = -\int_{0}^{\infty}D P_{t}h(x)[u]\, \dt,
    \end{equation}
    and 
    \begin{equation}
        D_{v} D_{u}f(x) = -\int_{0}^{\infty}D^{2} P_{t}h(x)[u, v] \, \dt.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, $f$ is a solution to the corresponding Stein equation~\eqref{eq: Stein equation}.

