[Lm of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] Define 
    \begin{equation*}
        G(A,x):=F(A,P_0(A)x,P_1(A)x,\dots,P_k(A) x),
    \end{equation*}
    and also 
    \begin{equation*}
        \Tilde{G}(A,x) := G\left(\frac{\min(100,||A||)}{||A||}A,\frac{\min(100,||x||)}{||x||}x\right). 
    \end{equation*}
    Then $\Tilde{G}(A,x)$ is Lipschitz on $\mathbb{R}^{n^2+n}$ with $||\Tilde{G}||_{Lip} \lesssim 1$.

