is compact, because it is the intersection of the compact set \(\mathscr{P}_+(K,d)\) with the closed condition \(\rank(\mathbf P)\le d\), and every element of \(\mathscr{P}_+(K,d)\) has rank at least \(d\).  Thus, each local rank-\(d\) infimum is attained.  Lemma~(lem:Pk-rank-common-noise of the paper) gives the common-noise representation (equation eq:restricted.theorem.P of the paper), and the completed-square identity in the proof of Proposition~(prop:FG-restricted-barycenter of ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:308df2d192cfbbd1a8acd91f4f4747b888bb0722ff3a01b505c2bc045ecf1b1d","revision_digest":"sha256:61fc107c1046f19a2528bdbb79c1af17cbcb48f632f9c5244191b7d04409f620","source_id":"arxiv:2604.22453","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

