{"artifact_digest":"sha256:8685630749fa3838e2ba24ce76e83f3e6ae8efea76640e81fbb273dadcaefbc7","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/86/8685630749fa3838e2ba24ce76e83f3e6ae8efea76640e81fbb273dadcaefbc7.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:d8dd534652a7ca4bdcb837c5b9daa5b89dd0c39751ec6395878801785ea57dfb","bundle_entry_key":"2607-15140-lemma-45-compactness-on-the-half-line","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_110","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_110.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2607-15140-lemma-45-compactness-on-the-half-line","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Note that $\mathscr{Y}$ is a Banach space. Next, we prove that, for all $M_0\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}

\{v\in \mathscr{Y}\,:\, \|v\|_{\mathscr{Y}}\leq M_0\} \ \text{ is pre-compact in }\ \mathscr{X}.
\end{equation}
To this end, it suffices to prove that for each sequence $(f_n)_{n}\subseteq \mathscr{Y}$ such that $\sup_n\|f_n\|_{\mathscr{Y}}\leq M_0$ there exists a subsequence $(f_{n_j})_j$ that converges in $\mathscr{X}$.  

