[Definition def:zon sec of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] For every admissible random field $\mathcal{X}\randin \mathscr{F}\subset C^\infty(M,\mathbb{R}^k)$ and every $x\in M$, we let:
  \begin{equation}
    \zeta_\mathcal{X}(x):=\frac{1}{\|ev_x^1\wedge\cdots\wedge ev_x^k\|}\int_{\mathscr{F}_x} \quad \underline{D_xf^1\wedge \cdots\wedge D_xf^k}\quad \rho_\mathcal{X}(f) \,\mathrm{d} f
  \end{equation}
  where $ev_x:=(ev_x^1,\ldots,ev_x^k)\in (\mathscr{F}^*)^k$ is the evaluation at a point, i.e. $ev_x(f):=f(x)$ for all $f \in \mathscr{F}$, $D_xf^i$ denotes the differential of the function $f^i$ at the point $x\in M$ and where $\mathrm{d} f$ denotes the integration with respect to the Lebesgue measure on the subspace $\mathscr{F}_x$.

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.02319, 'Averaging Principle for Ordinary Differential Equations in a Multiscale Random Environment'] Let $n\geq1$ and $z\in\mathbb R^d$, then for all $0<t<T$, if \eqref{hyp:Fbound} and \eqref{hyp:Lip} are satisfied we have
\begin{align*}
\lvert\mathbf Z_t^{n,z}\rvert\leq\big(\lvert z\rvert+T\,M_T^n)\,e^{TL_T^n},
\end{align*}
where for all $t>0$ and $n\geq1$
\begin{align*}
M_t^n:=\sup_{s\in[0,t]}M_{\mathbf I_s^n}.
\end{align*}

