[Thm 5 of arXiv:2609.03054, 'The classes of bivariate Schur and Herglotz matrix-valued rational functions: realizations'] Let $F:\DD^2\to\Cmats{m}{n}$ be a rational matrix function satisfying
Theorem~\ref{thm:kneseDD}~{\rm(i)}. Then the following conditions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[\rm(i)]
\item function $F$ is symmetric;
\item the matrices $A,B,C,D,P_1,P_2$ from Theorem~\ref{thm:kneseDD} {\rm (ii)}
can be chosen such that
\begin{equation}
 CU=C,\quad UB=B,\quad UAU=A, \quad UP_1U=P_2, 
\end{equation}
for some $U\in\Cmats{k}{k}$  satisfyig $U=U^*=U^{-1}$.
\end{enumerate}
Additionally, if $F\in\mathbb R^{m\times n}(z_1,z_2)$ then the matrices $A,B,C,D,P_1,P_2,U$ in {\rm (ii)} may be chosen as real matrices.

[Pro 5.2 of arXiv:2608.00420, '{Weighted $L^p$ solutions of scalar BSDEs with general unbounded stochastic coefficients}\'] Let $(h_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ be an $(\mathcal{F}_t)$-progressively measurable nonnegative real-valued process satisfying $\int_0^\tau h_t {\rm d}t\leq C_1$ and let the generator $g$ satisfy that
\begin{align}
|g(t,y,z)|\leq h_t+C_1|z|^2, \ \ \  (t,y,z)\in[0,\tau]\times[-C_2,C_2]\times{\mathbb R}^d,
\end{align}
where $C_i~(i=1,2)$ are two nonnegative constants. Assume that $(y_t,z_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ is an adapted solution of BSDE (equation BSDE1.1 of the paper) such that $|y_\cdot|\leq C_2$. Then $z_\cdot\in M_\tau^2(0;{\mathbb R}^d)$.\vspace{0.2cm} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

