body:
[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2607.04193, 'Onsager--Machlup Functionals for Generalized Newtonian Equations of Motion with Time-Varyi'] Let $f$ be a non-negative, convex, symmetric, and measurable function on the Wiener space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$. Let $A \in \mathcal{F}$ be a symmetric convex set with $\mathbb{P}(A) > 0$. Then the following inequality holds:
\begin{equation*}
    \mathbb{E}\bigl[f \mid A\bigr] \le \mathbb{E}\bigl[f\bigr].
\end{equation*}

