body:
[Definition def:limiting_fairness of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] For any $\epsilon>0$, define the $\epsilon$-shifted fairness process as 
    \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{S}_\epsilon\eta^{\pi,n}(t)(\mathbb{A}) = \begin{cases}
        \eta^{\pi,n}(t)(\mathbb{A}) &\mbox{if }t\geq \tau_{\epsilon}^{\pi,n}\\
        \delta_0(\mathbb{A}) &\mbox{if }t<\tau_\epsilon^{\pi,n}.
    \end{cases}
    \end{equation}
    A probability measure-valued process $\eta^\pi \in \mathbb{G}_{\mathcal{M}_f}[0,\infty)$ is said to be the limiting fairness process for $(\eta^{\pi,n}:n\in \mathbb{N})$, if for all $\epsilon>0$, $\tau_\epsilon^{\pi,n}\Rightarrow \tau_\epsilon^\pi$ and $\mathcal{S}_\epsilon\eta^{\pi,n}\Rightarrow \mathcal{S}_\epsilon\eta^\pi$ as $n\to\infty$, where $\mathcal{S}_\epsilon\eta^\pi$ is defined by replacing $\tau^{\pi,n}_\epsilon$ with $\tau_\epsilon^\pi$ in (equation eq:shifted_process_definition of the paper). We denote this mode of convergence by $\eta^{\pi,n} \stackrel{f}{\rightarrow} \eta^\pi$.

[Defn 13 of arXiv:2609.02173, 'Bounding Selmer Groups of Superelliptic Jacobians via Class Groups'] Define

	\[
	\mathcal U_v
	=
	\left\{
	\left[1+\pi^p\beta\right]|
	\beta\in \mathcal O_{L_v}
	\right\}
	\subset \HOv.
	\]

