body:
[Lemma L:sojourn:UB of arXiv:2604.08129, 'Polarity of points for Gaussian random fields in critical dimension'] There exist constants $C_1 < \infty$ and $\delta_1 \in (0, 1)$ such that 
for all integers $n \ge 1$ and all $\varepsilon \in (0, \delta_1)$,
\begin{align}
{\mathbb E}[T_\varepsilon^n] \le \left[C_1 n \varepsilon^d \Psi(\varepsilon)\right]^n,
\end{align}
where
    \begin{align}
    \Psi(\varepsilon) := (\log(1/\varepsilon))^{1-\gamma d} =
    \begin{cases} 
    f(\varepsilon) & \text{if } \gamma < 1/d, \\
    1 & \text{if } \gamma = 1/d.
    \end{cases} 
    \end{align}

