body:
[Lemma string-trajectory-cluster of arXiv:2505.16585, 'Expanded regimes of area law for lattice Yang--Mills theories'] For any string trajectory 
\begin{equs}
\Big((s_0,K_0,Q_0), (s_1,K_1,Q_1), \ldots ,(s_l,K_l,Q_l)\Big)
\end{equs}
starting at $(\ell,B,\varnothing)$, for each $0 \leq i \leq l$, we have that 
\begin{equs}
\mathrm{supp}(B-K_i)\cup Q_i \in \{\mc{C} \sse \mc{P}_{\Lambda}^+:  \mc{C} \cup \ell \text{ is connected}\}.
\end{equs}
If $s_i$ is stuck in a minimal union of connected components $\tilde{Q}_i$, we also have that 
\begin{equs}
\mathrm{supp}(B-K_i)\cup Q_i \cup \tilde{Q}_i \in \{\mc{C} \sse \mc{P}_{\Lambda}^+: \mc{C} \cup \ell \text{ is connected}\}.
\end{equs}
We call elements of $\{\mc{C} \sse \mc{P}_{\Lambda}^+: \mc{C} \cup \ell \text{ is connected}\}$ connected clusters of $\ell$.

