[Definition d:ShadowMP of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] A $\msP$-valued process~$(\rho_\bullet,\mbbP)$ with $\mbbP$-a.s.\ $\tau_\mrmn$-continuous trajectories is a \emph{distributional solution} to the \emph{shadow martingale problem~$\hmartp{}{\mssL}$} if
\begin{equation}
\widehat M^{\class{\varphi\otimes f}}_t\eqdef\ (\varphi\otimes f)^\star(\rho_t) - (\varphi\otimes f)^\star(\rho_0) -\int_0^t (\mcL'\rho_s)(\varphi\otimes f)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} s
\end{equation}
is an $\msF_\bullet$-adapted $\mbbP$-martingale for each $\varphi\in\msR_0$ and each~$f\in\msA$.

