[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2604.01701, '\bf Chung-type laws of the iterated logarithm for $m$-fold weighted integrated fractional '] Let $T:\mathcal{H}\to E$ be an operator mapping a Hilbert spaces into a Banach space and suppose that $\sum_{i=1}^{\infty} g_iTf_i$ convergence a.s. in $E$. Let $\alpha\in(0,2)$. If  
\begin{equation} e_n(T)\le c_1n^{-\alpha}, \end{equation}
then there exists two positive constants $c_2(c_1,\alpha)$ which depends only on $c_1$ and $\alpha$ such that
\begin{equation} 
-\log\pr\left(\|\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}g_iTf_i\|<\epsilon\right)\le c_2e^{-2\alpha/(2-\alpha)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

