[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] The $L^{2}$-spectral radius $\lambda_{2}(\theta\mu)$ is characterized by the following variational formula:
  \begin{align*}
    \lambda_{2}(\theta\mu) = \inf \left\{ \mathcal{E}^{\alpha}(u,u) - \theta \int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}} u^{2} d\mu : u \in \mathcal{F}^{\alpha}, \int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}} u^{2} dx = 1 \right\}.
  \end{align*}
  Hence it follows that $C(\theta) := -\lambda_{2}(\theta\mu)$.

