    By definition of $\Xi$, any point in $\Xi$ has distance $\ll \log \theta$ to a point on the boundary $\partial \cal P(\vec W)$. Thus every point in $\Xi'$ has distance $\ll \log \theta$ to a point in $\partial \cal P(\vec W) \setminus (a_X\log B - 2 A \log \log B) \Delta^s$.

