body:
[Theorem 16 (Cauchy \cite{Cauchy-1, MR2866794}) of arXiv:2609.02837, '2609.02837'] If $A \in \h_n$ and $B \in \h_m$ is a principal submatrix of $A$, then 
\begin{equation*}
\lambda_j(A) \geq \lambda_j(B)  \geq \lambda_{j+n-m}(A)
\end{equation*}
for all $1 \leq j \leq m$.

