[Lem parti-clo of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] Take any parameters $K>100$ and $0\le \delta<1$. Suppose that a particle-generated Nevanlinna function $Y$ satisfies the following conditions:
\begin{itemize}
    \item there is no pole of $Y$ in $(K,\infty)$;
    \item for any $w=x+\mathrm{i} y$ with $x\le K^2$ and $y\ge 4K^2/(1+|x|^{\delta/2})$, we have
    \[
            \left|Y(w)-\sqrt{w}\right|\leq \frac{{\rm Im}[\sqrt w]^{1-\delta}}{{\rm Im}[w]}.
    \]
\end{itemize}
Then $Y$ has infinitely many poles $x_1\ge x_2\ge \cdots$, and $|x_i-{\mathfrak a}_i|<CK^4i^{-\delta/6}$ for any $i\in \mathbb{N}$, where $C>0$ is a universal constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition pro2 of arXiv:2604.11412, 'Stability of invariant measures of the stochastic Landau-Lifshitz-Bloch equation with vani'] If (equation 1.1 of the paper) holds,  then for every
  $ \mathbf{u}_0 \in H^1({\mathbb R}^2)$,
      $\varepsilon\in [0,1]$ and $\delta\in(0,1]$, the stochastic viscous equation (equation 1.3* of the paper) admits a unique   solution $\mathbf{u}^{\varepsilon, \delta}$ in the sense of
       Definition (defa of the paper).

       Furthermore,  
 for  every $ p\ge 1$, $\varepsilon\in [0,1]$ and $\delta\in(0,1]$, 
   the  following uniform estimates hold:
\begin{equation} 
\mathrm{E}\left(\sup_{t\in[0,T]}
\| \mathbf{u}^{\varepsilon,\delta} (t, \mathbf{u}_0 )\|^{2p}_{H^1 ({\mathbb R}^2) }
\right)
\le   M_1,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
  \mathrm{E}\left(\int_{0}^{T}
\left(\|
\mathbf{u}^{\varepsilon,\delta}
(t, \mathbf{u}_0 )\|^2_{H^2 ({\mathbb R}^2) }+
\delta \| \mathbf{u}^{\varepsilon,\delta}
(t, \mathbf{u}_0 )\|^2_{H^3 ({\mathbb R}^2) } \right)dt
\right)^p
\leq M_1,
\end{equation}
