body:
[Lem lemma: single vertex pinching cancellations of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Fix a blue face $B$ with disjoint vertices and a vertex $v$ of $B$. Then 
\begin{equation}
	w_{\infty}(B) + \sum_{B'\in \AF(B,v)}w_{\infty}(B') = 0,
\end{equation}
where if $B'$ is the pair of faces $\{B'_1,B'_2\}$, then $w_{\infty}(B'):=w_{\infty}(B'_1)\cdot w_{\infty}(B'_2)$.

As a consequence, for an embedded map $M\in \mathcal{M}(s,K)$ and a vertex $v$ on a blue face $B$ of $M$ with disjoint vertices, we have that
\begin{align}
	w_{\infty}(M) + \sum_{M'\in \AM(M,B,v)}w_{\infty}(M') = 0.
\end{align}

