[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2603.26936, 'Sharp Riemannian heat kernel estimates on the cut locus and the Parabolic Anderson model'] Let the assumptions in Lemma \ref{lem: single integral bounds} prevail. The following estimates hold with the constants on the right hand side possibly depending on $\epsilon$ if the left hand side has dependence on $\epsilon'$.
    \begin{equation}
    {\sup_{x\in M}}\iint_{M^2} G^{\epsilon'}_t(d(x,y))d(y,y')^{2\alpha-d} m(dy)m(dy')\leq C,\end{equation}
