[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.04153, '\vspace*{-3cm}Smooth autonomous fast dynamo action on the three-torus'] Let $T_N:\TT^2\to\TT^2$ be a smooth, volume-preserving diffeomorphism
isotopic to the identity, and let $g\in C^\infty(\TT^2;\RR)$ be mean-free. Then there exists $n_0\geq1$ such that, for every integer $n\geq n_0$, there is a velocity field
\begin{equation}
u^{(n)}\in C^\infty_\sigma(\TT^3), \qquad
\bigl(u^{(n)}\bigr)_3>0,
\end{equation}
for which
\begin{equation}
P_{u^{(n)}}=T_N,
\qquad
\tau_{u^{(n)}}\circ P_{u^{(n)}}^{-1}
=1-\frac{g}{n}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

