[Proposition p:AndiHatPolar of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] Let~$\mbfF_n$ be as in~(equation eq:Nest of the paper) and assume that~(equation eq:QPP of the paper) holds. Then,
\begin{enumerate}[$(i)$]
\item setting~$\widehat\mbfF_n\eqdef \mbfT\times\mbfF_n$ defines an $\widehat\boldsymbol\mssE_\pi$-nest~${\big(\widehat\mbfF_n\big)}_n$;

\item the set~$\widehat\mbfM_\circ$ is~$\widehat\boldsymbol\mssW_\pi$-coexceptional.
\end{enumerate}

\begin{proof}
The family~$\left(\mbfF_n\right)_n$ as in~(equation eq:Nest of the paper) is an $\boldsymbol\mssE^\mbfs$-nest for every~$\mbfs\in\mbfT$ by Lemma~(l:Nest of the paper) (also cf.~Rmk.~(r:Nest of the paper)) and~(i:p:AndiHatPolar:1 of the paper) follows in a straightforward way.
(i:p:AndiHatPolar:2 of the paper) is a consequence of~(i:p:AndiHatPolar:1 of the paper) by~[MaRoe92].
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

