[Lemma lem:extra:4-ST of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Suppose that \((T,R_{+},R_{-},\gamma)\) is a 4-ST. Then up to orbit equivalence, there is only one semiflow \(\varphi\) satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(\varphi\) is tight.
\item \(\varphi\) contains exactly one bi-infinite flowline \(\lambda\) and \(\lambda\) is a pseudo-hyperbolic closed orbit.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:one-step-reduction of arXiv:2608.06159, 'Majority Dynamics on Resampled Sparse Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi Graphs:\\[0.5ex] Gaussian Winner '] Fix a deterministic time \(t\ge0\), condition on \(\rvy_t\), and suppose that
for some fixed \(K>K_2^{\mathrm{ER}}(b)\),
\begin{align}
\Delta_t\ge K\frac{N}{\sqrt{\log N}}.

\end{align}
Then, for any fixed \(r\) satisfying
\begin{align}
q_K<r<r_*,

\end{align}
we have, for all sufficiently large \(N\),
\begin{align}
\P\left(
|\gR_{t+1}|\le rN
\,\middle|\,
\rvy_t
\right)
\ge
1-2\exp\left(-\left(\log N\right)^2\right).

\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma l:Theta-bound of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] For any $B\in {\mathrm{SL}}(2,{\mathbb R})$ and any nonzero vector $v\in {\mathbb R}^2$, one has
\begin{equation}
\Theta(B, v)\le -\log \sin{\rm dist}([v],\mathbf{r}(B)).
\end{equation}

