body:
[Theorem thm:percolation of arXiv:2603.28161, 'Boundary four-point connectivities of conformal loop ensembles'] Let $V_0,V_2$ be defined as above. There exists a constant $C\in(0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{align*}
P^{\rm total}(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4)&= C\left(\frac{(x_4-x_2)(x_3-x_1)}{(x_2-x_1)(x_4-x_3)(x_3-x_2)(x_4-x_1)}\right)^{\frac{2}{3}}V_0(\lambda),\\
P^{(14)(23)}(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4)&= AC\left(\frac{(x_4-x_2)(x_3-x_1)}{(x_2-x_1)(x_4-x_3)(x_3-x_2)(x_4-x_1)}\right)^{\frac{2}{3}}V_2(\lambda).
\end{align*}
Here, the constant $A:=\frac{8\sqrt{3}\,\pi \sin\!\left(\frac{2\pi}{9}\right)}{135\cos\!\left(\frac{5\pi}{18}\right)}\in(0,\infty)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem QCLT of arXiv:2607.02742, 'Gaussian fluctuations for the parabolic Anderson model with L\'evy white noise'] Suppose that there exists $p \in (1,\frac{3}{2})$ such that 
\begin{equation}

m_{p}<\infty \quad \mbox{and} \quad m_{2p}<\infty.
\end{equation}
Then, for any $t>0$,
\[
{\rm dist}\left( \frac{F_R(t)}{\sigma_R(t)},Z\right) \leq  C_t R^{-(1-\frac{1}{p})}
\]
Here $C_t>0$ is a constant depending on $t$, $Z$ is a standard normal random variable and ${\rm dist}$ is the 1-Wasserstein distance, the Fortet-Mourier distance, or the Kolmogorov distance. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.00537, 'Explicit Exponential Sum Estimates and Approximate Functional Equations for the Zeta Funct'] \cite[Lemma 2]{dereyna2024approximationzetafunctiondirichlet}
    Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be continuous real functions defined in a closed interval $[a,b]$. Assume that $f$ has a non-null continuous derivative $f'(x)$ and that $\Big| \frac{g(x)}{f'(x)}\Big| $ is non-zero and monotonic. Then 
    \begin{equation}
        \bigg|\int_a^bg(x)e^{if(x)}dx\bigg|\le2\text{ max}_{a\leq x\leq b} \bigg| \frac{g(x)}{f'(x)}\bigg| 
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem-2m-recurrent of arXiv:2510.13733, 'Internal Diffusion Limited Aggregation \\ with Critical Branching Random Walks'] Assume $d=2$.
Then there exists a finite absolute constant $C_2$ 
such that for any $R>0$ and any $z\in \partial B_R$
\begin{equation}
\sum_{y\in B_R} G_R(0,y)G_R^2(y,z)\le C_2.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lm:fastmixing of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] We have
\begin{eqnarray*}
\forall f\in\mathcal {F}_1^+,\quad\forall \varepsilon\in(0,1),\quad 
{\rm t}_{\textsc{mix}}(f,\varepsilon) & \le & \frac{1+\mathrm{Ent}(f)}{\gamma\varepsilon}.
\end{eqnarray*}

