[Lemma 16 (Orbit average of quadratic form on $\su(N)$) of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] Let $\mathcal{O}^*(\Lambda)$ be the $\su(N)$ coadjoint orbit passing through $\Lambda=\text{diag}(i\lambda_1,...,i\lambda_N)$ for $\Lambda\in \su(N)$, as defined in \emph{(\ref{Eq:CoAdjointOrbitsuNIsospectral})}. For any $\Omega\in \mathcal{O}^*(\Lambda)$, consider the decomposition \emph{(\ref{Eq:ZeitlinExpansionVorticityAndStreamMatrices})}. Then we have
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathcal{O}^*(\Lambda)}\Omega_k\Omega_l dm_{\mathrm{KKS}}(\Omega)=\dfrac{\|\Lambda\|^2}{c_N(N^2-1)}\delta_{k+l, 0} \ ,
\end{equation}
where $dm_{\mathrm{KKS}}(\Omega)=dm_{\mathrm{KKS}, \mathcal{O}^*(\Lambda)}(\Omega)$ is the KKS measure on $\mathcal{O}^*(\Lambda)$ and $\| \Lambda \|^2=(\Lambda, \Lambda)=-\operatorname{tr}(\Lambda^2)$ as in \emph{(\ref{Eq:suNinnerproduct})}, and $c_N>0$ is the normalizing constant defined in \emph{(\ref{Eq:OrthogonalBasisZeitlinInnerProduct})}.

