body:
[Corollary 17 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] For each $p > 0$, there exists $C = C(p) > 0$ such that
\begin{equation*}
	\BE\!\left\lbrack D_{\Gamma_{V_r}}^{V_r}(T_r, B_r)^p\right\rbrack \le C r^{-p}
\end{equation*}
for all sufficiently large $r > 0$. In fact, for all sufficiently large $r > 0$, $r D_{\Gamma_{V_r}}^{V_r}(T_r, B_r)$ is stochastically dominated by a geometric random variable taking values in $\BN$ with a universal success probability.

[Proposition prop:productive-budget of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] If $K_F(c)=K_{\textnormal{\textsc{AR}}}(h)$, then
\begin{equation}
\boxed{h=\frac{m}{m-1}c.}
\end{equation}
For two actions, $h=2c$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

