[Corollary Cor.Jump of arXiv:2606.13442, 'Scaling limit of additive functionals for reversible non-gradient exclusion process: criti'] There exists a constant $C(c_{-},c_{+})$ such that, for any bond $b\in(\mathbb{Z}^2)^*$ and $\lambda\in(0,1)$,  we have the following uniform bound for $\pi_b\widetilde{G}_\lambda$:
		\begin{equation*}
			\norm{\pi_b\widetilde{G}_\lambda}_{L^\infty}\leqslant C m 3^{4m},\qquad\forall b\in(\mathbb{Z}^2)^*,\ \lambda\in(0,1),\quad\forall m\in\mathbb{N}.
		\end{equation*}
		\begin{proof}
			Similar to the proof for (equation eq.H1TwoScaleVar of the paper) in Proposition~(prop.H1TwoScale of the paper), we can compute $\pi_{b}\widetilde{G}_\lambda(\eta)$ exactly using the expression for $\widetilde{G}_\lambda$ and the locality of the corrector Lemma~(lem.Homogenization of the paper) (equation lem.Correctorlocal of the paper). Suppose that the bond $b= \{x,x+e_i\}$ lies in $\overline{(z+{\scaleobj{1.2}{\square}}_m)^*}$ for $z\in\mathcal{Z}_m$, then we have
			\begin{equation*}
				\pi_b\widetilde{G}_\lambda(\eta) = {\mathsf{D}}_{e_i}\overline{g}_\lambda(x)(\overline{\eta}(x)-\overline{\eta}(x+e_i))+\sum_{j=1}^{2}({\mathsf{D}}_{e_j}\overline{g}_\lambda)_{z+{\scaleobj{1.2}{\square}}_m}\pi_{x,x+e_i}\phi^z_{e_j,m}.
			\end{equation*}
			Combining (equation eq.GreenDBound of the paper) in Proposition~(prop.GreenEstimate of the paper) and (equation lem.CorrectorLp of the paper) in Lemma~(lem.Homogenization of the paper), we can obtain the desired result.
		\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

