body:
[Prop 14371 of arXiv:2606.29143, 'Comonotonic and moment matching approximations for sums of lognormal random variables'] Let $A = (a_1, ..., a_m)^{'}$ and $Q = (q_1, ..., q_m)^{'}$ be two numerical vectors with $\min(a_1, ..., a_m) \geq 0, \max(a_1, ..., a_m) > 0$ and $0 =q_0 < q_1 < q_2 < ... < q_m = 1$. Let $X$ be a continuous random variable and $X_{A, Q}$ be the step-weighted version of $X$. Then for any $p \in (0, 1)$ it holds that 
\begin{align*} 
\text{TVaR}_p[X_{A, Q}] = 
\frac{a_{l}(1 - p^{*})}{a(1 - p)}\text{TVaR}_{p^{*}}[X] + \sum^{m - 1}_{k = l}\frac{(a_{k + 1} - a_{k})(1 - q_k)}{a(1 - p)}\text{TVaR}_{q_k}[X]
\end{align*}
with $p^{*} = G^{-1}_{A, Q}(p) \in [q_{l - 1}, q_{l}]$ for some $l \in \{1, ..., m\}$ and $\sum_{k = m}^{m - 1} = 0$ by convention.

