[Thmintro ET of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a $C^0$-foliation on $M$ transverse to $\partial M$.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item (Coarse version) Assume that $(M,\mathcal{F})$ is not homeomorphic to either of the following:
        \begin{itemize}
            \item $S^1 \times D^2$ with the standard foliation by disks,
            \item $\mathbb{T}^2\times I$ with a foliation semi-conjugate to an irrational foliation.
        \end{itemize}
        Then for every $\varepsilon > 0$, there exists a positive (resp.~negative) contact structure $\xi$  which is $\varepsilon$-close to $T\mathcal{F}$ in the $C^0$ topology, and whose boundary foliation dominates a foliation $\mathcal{G} = \mathcal{G}_\varepsilon$ on $\partial M$ which is monotone equivalent to $\partial \mathcal{F}$.
        \item (Fine version) If moreover $\mathcal{F}$ has neither compact planar leaves nor $\mathbb{T}^2$-type planar minimal sets (\zcref{def:pems}), then $\mathcal{G}$ can be chosen isotopic to $\partial \mathcal{F}$ along $\partial M$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 54 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Fix constants $M,K$ satisfying \eqref{eq:costanti}. Define the sequence of real numbers $q_0, q_1, \ldots $ by, for each $i \ge 0$, setting $q_0 = \varepsilon_0$ and
\begin{flalign}

	q_{i+1}= q_i - \Delta_i, \qquad \text{where} \qquad \Delta_i = q_i^{1/3} N^{-2/3-M\delta}.	
\end{flalign}

\noindent We will always work with values of $i$ for which $q_i>0$.

