    \begin{itemize}
        \item A \textit{tree} is a simple undirected graph such that for any two distinct vertices $x, y$ there is exactly one SAW in the graph with initial vertex $x$ and terminal vertex $y$.
        \item A \textit{spanning tree} of a graph is a subgraph containing all the vertices that is a tree.
