[Lemma lem:eulerintegralrest of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] There exist polynomials $P_{i,j,\ell}$ of degree $i$
such that
\begin{multline*}
    \int_0^1 \big[B_p(u) - B_p\big] 
        \sum_{k = 1}^{n-2} 
            f^{(p)}_{j,\ell,m}(k+1-u)du 
\\
=
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2n}} 
    \frac{z^m}{n^{\ell+1/2}}
    \sum_{i=0}^{j+p-1}
        \frac{P_{i,j,\ell}(z^2/n)}{n^{i}} 
\\
+
    O\left(\frac{1}{\min (n^{j+\ell+p-m/2}, |z|^{2(j+\ell+p)-m})}\right).
 \end{multline*}

