\EE^{\frac{1}{q}} \left|
\delta\pi^{(\n)}_{xy\, \beta'}\right|^{ q} 
\lesssim \ve^{|\beta'|-\langle\beta'\rangle} |x-y|^{\langle \beta' \rangle - |\n|} \w \, .
\end{equation}

Then for all \(\gamma\) populated and not purely polynomial 

\begin{equation}
\EE^{\frac{1}{q}} \left|
(\delta\Gamma_{xy})_{ \beta}^{\gamma}
\right|^{ q} 
\lesssim \ve^{|\beta|-\langle\beta\rangle-|\gamma|+\langle\gamma\rangle} |x-y|^{\langle \beta\rangle - \langle\gamma\rangle} \w \,.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Interpolation:ProbaEffectiveDrift of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] [MR1326606]
    Let $Y^0_t$ be a weak solution of (equation eq:SDETiling2.0 of the paper) taking $\zeta=0$. Let $\dot{Y}^0_t$ be its projection into $\mathbb{T}^d$ introduced in Proposition (prop:Ergodic:InvariantMeasure of the paper). Let $\nu(\cdot;0)$ be the density of the invariant measure of $\dot{Y}^0_t$ on $\mathbb{T}^d$. Let $\bar{\mathbf{v}}$ be the effective drift as defined in (equation eq:Intro:EffectiveDrift of the paper) and $\psi(\cdot;0)$ the principal eigenfunction associated to the principal eigenvalue $\gamma(0)$ of (equation eq:Intro:EigenvalueProblem of the paper). Then,
    \begin{equation}
        \bar{\mathbf{v}}  = \int_{\mathbb{T}^d}\Big(b(x) + A(x)\frac{\nabla \psi(x;0)}{\psi(x;0)} \Big)\nu(x;0)dx.
    \end{equation}

