[Lemma 5 (Deterministic rational orthogonal perturbation) of arXiv:2608.26877, 'When Is the Sharp Covariance Envelope Tight? Feature-Only Geometry for Volume-Sampled Leas'] For every $d=4^n$, $n\geq1$, there is a deterministically specified rational
matrix $Q_d\in O(d)$ such that every square minor of $Q_d$ is nonzero and
\begin{equation}
 \lVert Q_d-H_d\rVert_{\max}<\frac18,

\end{equation}
where $H_d$ is the normalized Sylvester matrix.

