[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2609.04153, '\vspace*{-3cm}Smooth autonomous fast dynamo action on the three-torus'] Let $T: \TT^2 \to \TT^2$ be a volume preserving diffeomorphism that is isotopic to the identity, and let $g \in C^\infty(\TT^2)$ be mean free. Then, for any $n \in \NN$ large enough, there exists $u^{(n)} \in C_\sigma^\infty(\TT^3)$ with $u^{(n)}_3>0$, so that 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $P_{u^{(n)}}(x,y)=T$,
    \item $\tau_{u^{(n)}}(P_{u^{(n)}}^{-1}(x,y))=1-\frac{g(x,y)}{n}$.
\end{enumerate}

