body:
[Theorem thm:competition of arXiv:2509.16541, 'Two-stage Bootstrap Percolation'] Assume $(p,q)\to (0,0)$. Then 
\begin{itemize}
\item if $q\ll p^{2}/(\log(1/p)^2$, then $\mathbb{P}(\text{the origin is eventually in state $1$})\to 1$;
\item if $p^2\ll q\ll p^{1/2}$, then $\mathbb{P}(\text{the origin  remains in state $0$ forever})\to 1$; and 
\item if $p^{1/2}\log(1/p)\ll q$, then $\mathbb{P}(\text{the origin is eventually in state $2$})\to 1$.
\end{itemize}

