[Lemma prop:CNfailB1new of arXiv:2510.12365, 'Planted clique recovery in \\ random geometric graphs'] In $G_k(n,r)$: \\
(i) If $\mu\ll n$ then
\begin{equation}
    \Prob{\mathcal{B}_1} \leq \mu n  e^{- c_{1,d} \phi_d r^d\,(n - k + 1 + k\,O(r^d))} +o(1), \nonumber
\end{equation}
for some $c_{1,d}>0$.

\noindent (ii) If $r= (\gamma/\phi_d)^{1/d}$ so that $\mu \sim \gamma n$ for $\gamma\in (0,1)$, there exists some constant $M_0$ such that for all $M\ge M_0$, 
\begin{equation}
    \Prob{\mathcal{B}_1} \leq  M^d  e^{- M^{-d}n - k\log(1-M^{-d})}. \nonumber
\end{equation}

