[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.30570, '2608.30570'] A submanifold $\Sigma^n$ in ${\mathbb R}^{n+k}$ is a \textbf{translating soliton} for the mean curvature flow if there is a constant unit vector ${\bf T}\in {\mathbb R}^{n+k}$, such that
		\begin{align*}
			\Sigma^n_t=\Sigma^n+t{\bf T}
		\end{align*}
		is a solution to the mean curvature flow. Equivalently, it holds
		\begin{equation}
			{\bf T}^{\perp}={\bf H}
		\end{equation}
		on $\Sigma^n$ everywhere, where ${\bf H}$ is the mean curvature vector of $\Sigma^n$ in ${\mathbb R}^{n+k}$.

[Lemma lem.equivstrong of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Fix $(t_0,m_0) \in [0,1) \times \mathcal{P}_2({\mathbb R})$. Let $\big(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{F} = (\mathcal{F}(t))_{0 \leq t \leq 1}, \mathbb{P}\big)$ be any filtered probability space satisfying the usual conditions, which supports an $\mathcal{F}(t_0)$-measurable random $X_0$ with law $m_0$, and an $\mathbb{F}$-Brownian motion $(B(t))_{0\leq t \leq 1}$. Then, we have
   \begin{align}
       \mathcal{V}^{\infty}(t_0,m_0) = \inf_{\alpha} \Big\| X_0 + \int_{t_0}^1 \alpha(t) \, dt + B(1) - B(t_0) \Big\|_{\infty},
   \end{align}
   where the infimum is taken over all $\mathbb{F}$-progressive processes $\alpha$ satisfying the constraint
   \begin{align} 
       {\mathbb E} \, \alpha(t)^2 \leq 2/\pi, \quad \text{ for a.e.\ } t_0 \leq t \leq 1.
   \end{align}
   In particular, $V^{\infty} = \mathcal{V}^{\infty}(0,\delta_0)$, where $V^{\infty}$ was defined  in (equation def.vinf.intro of the paper).

