[Definition of arXiv:2608.30346, '\textbf{Classification complexity of homeomorphism group actions}'] Let \(G\) be a Polish group acting continuously on a Polish space \(X\). The action of \(G\) on \(X\) is \textit{turbulent} if
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(T1)] every orbit is meager,
        \item[(T2)] every orbit is dense, and
        \item[(T3)] every local orbit is somewhere dense, that is for any open \(U \subset X\), \( x \in U\) and open \(1_G \in V \subset G\), \(\mathcal{O}(x,U,V)\) is somewhere dense.
    \end{enumerate}

[Prop 32 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] Let $\mathbf{y},u \in E^K$ and $\vartheta \in \mathbb{R}$. Then the couple process $(\tilde{X}_t^{\mathbf{y},u,\vartheta},\tilde{\eta}_t^{\mathbf{y},u,\vartheta})_{t\in [0,T]}$ given by 
    \begin{align*}
        &\tilde{X}_t^{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta),\tau}:= \begin{cases}
            X_t^{\mathbf{y}_t^{*}}, &t \in [0,\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}]\\
             X_t^{\mathbf{y}_{\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}}^{*}}, &t\in [\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)},T]
        \end{cases}
        \\
        &\tilde{\eta}_t^{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta),\tau}:= \begin{cases}
            \tilde{\eta}_t^{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}, &t \in [0,\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}]\\
             \eta_t^{\mathbf{y}_{\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}}^{*}}- \eta_{\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}}^{\mathbf{y}_{\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}}^{*}}+\tilde{\eta}_{\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)}}^{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta),\tau}, &t\in [\tau_{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta)},T]
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    satisfies Definition \ref{Defi 317} under probability $\tilde{\mathbb{P}}^{\mathbf{y},(u,\vartheta),\tau}$.

