[Lemma trans-lem of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B}\in \mathcal{G}^\Lambda_2(\mathbb R^d)$, $m_\mathcal{A},m_\mathcal{B}\in\mathbb R^d$ be their mean vectors, and $\mathcal{J}\in\Gamma(\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B})$ be a Feller coupling of two L\'evy generators. For any $h=(\tau,\tau')\in\mathbb R^{2d}$, it holds 
	\begin{align*}
		[\mathcal{J}^- \sigma_h c_2](x,y)&= \mathcal{J}^- c_2(x,y)+ (m_\mathcal{A}-m_\mathcal{B})^\top (\tau-\tau'). 
	\end{align*}

