[Theorem 24 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Let $D$ be regular for $A$ and $\mathpzc{l}(D)<+\infty$. The  problem
		\begin{align}
			\begin{cases}
				\partial_t u(x,t)=-\Lpsi u(x,t), & x\in D,\,t>0,\\
				u(x,t)=0,& x\in D^c,\, t>0,\\
				u(x,0)=1,& x\in D,
			\end{cases}
		\end{align}
		has a pointwise solution $u(x,t)\coloneqq \mathds{P}^x(T_D>t)$.

