[Lemma lem:int_0^t e^(delta/epsilon)|A^(1/2)u|ds of arXiv:2411.02459, 'Existence and higher regularity of statistically steady states for the stochastic Coleman-'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem (thm:well-posed of the paper), let $U(t)=(u(t),\eta(t))$ denote the solution of (equation eqn:react-diff:mu of the paper) corresponding to initial condition $U_0\in\mathcal{H}^0_\mu$. Then for all $0<q\le\delta$, where $\delta$ is the constant from (equation ineq:<T.eta,eta> of the paper), there exists a positive constant $c=c(U_0,q)$ independent of $t$ and $\mu\in\mathcal{M}_\delta$ such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\int_0^t e^{qr}\|A^{1/2}u(r)\|^2_H\emph{d} r\leq\|U_0\|^2_{\mathcal{H}^0_\mu}+ c\,e^{qt}.
\end{equation}

