[Theorem general-dimensional-criterion of arXiv:2412.08400, '\vspace{-1.0cm} Characterization of Exponential Families of \\ Lumpable Stochastic Matrice'] Let $\mathcal{V}$ be a submanifold (without boundary) of $\mathcal{W}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})$ such that
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(i)\xspace] $\dim \mathcal{V} = \dim \ehull(\mathcal{V})$.
        \item[(ii)\xspace] There exists some finite dimensional (Hausdorff) topological vector space $\mathcal{U}$, a linear map 
        $$\phi \colon \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}) \to \mathcal{U},$$ 
        and $C \in \mathcal{U}$ such that 
        $$\mathcal{V} = \mathcal{W}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}) \cap \mathcal{L},$$ 
    \end{enumerate}
    where 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathcal{L} \triangleq \left\{  F \in \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}), \phi(F) = C  \right\}.
    \end{equation*}
    Then $\mathcal{V}$ forms an e-family.

