body:
[Definition $d$-admissible orientations of arXiv:2509.06273, 'Normalized Matching Property for Competing Urn Models'] For any nonnegative integer $d$, 
an orientation $O$ of $G$ is \emph{\color{darkblue} $d$-admissible} if 
\[ \text{$\outdeg_O(v_i) \geq 1$ \. and \.  \. $\indeg_O(v_i) \geq 1$ \quad   for all $i \in [d]$.} \]
For $S \subseteq X$, define
\begin{align*}
	\aM_{G,d}^{\occ}(S) \ := \ 
	\begin{array}{l}
	\text{number of $d$-admissible orientations $O$ of $G$ with  }\\[4pt]
	\text{\. $\Out_O(v_n)=\{e_j \. \mid \. j \in S\}$ \ and \  $\In_O(v_n)=\{e_j \. \mid \. j \in X\setminus S$\}.} 
	\end{array}
\end{align*}

Here the  notation 
$\occ$ anticipates its connection to the urn occupancy measure, which will be made explicit in \S(ss:proof-H-occ of the paper).
By construction,  \hskip.03cm $\aM_{G,d}^{\occ}$ \hskip.03cm is a balanced weight function for vertices of $H_X$.

