[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2506.14145, '\bf Global-in-time optimal control of stochastic third-grade fluids with additive noise'] Let $\vb$ satisfies \eqref{eqn-vb-exponential-moments} and $\gb,\boldsymbol{\psi} \in \Lrm^p(\Omega; \mathrm{L}^2(0,T; \dot{\Lb}^2(\mathbb{T}^2)))$ (for some $p>2$). Then we have
	\begin{align*}
		\Eb\left[\int_0^{{T}}(\boldsymbol{\psi}(t),\pb(t))\drm t\right] = \Eb\left[ \int_0^{{T}} (\gb(t),\mfrk(t))\drm t\right], 
	\end{align*}
	where $\pb$ is the solution of \eqref{eqn-adjoint-pi} and $\mfrk$ is the solution of \eqref{eqn-linearized-pi}.

