[Definition Definition_virtual_block of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For a block process $\vec \mathbf p$, a compatible \emph{virtual block process} is a vector $\vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon}=(\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_1,\ldots, \boldsymbol{\upsilon}_m)\in (\mathbb R_+\cup \{\varnothing\})^m$ satisfying the following conditions: for each $\ell \in \llbracket 1,m\rrbracket$,
\begin{itemize}
    \item if $\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell\neq \varnothing$, then $\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}+\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell < \min\bigl( \bigcup_{j=1}^{m+\mathbf u}\mathbf \Delta_{j,\ell}\cup \{\mathbf Q_\ell\}\bigr)$;
    \item if $\ell=1$, or $\ell>1$ and $\mathbf p_\ell(\mathbf Q_{\ell-1}-)=0$, then $\boldsymbol{\upsilon}_\ell=\varnothing$.
\end{itemize}

