body:
[Lem 6 of arXiv:2608.13374, 'Nearly Sharp Comparison Results for sliced and max-sliced Wasserstein distances'] Fix $\epsilon > 0$. For every $\theta \in \mathbb{S}^{d-1}$ and datum $(u,z,r) \in \mathbb{S}^{d-1}\times \R^d \times \R_{> 0}$ with $\rho = r\epsilon$,
\begin{equation}
    \lVert{\theta_\#(\la^{(\rho)}_{(u,z,r)}-\la_{(u,z,r)})\rVert}_{\mathrm{KR}} \leq C_{d,g} r \min\sbrac{\epsilon, \frac{\epsilon^{d+2}}{\beta^{d+1}}},
\end{equation}
where $\beta := (1 - \abrac{u,\theta}^2)^{1/2}$ and the second term in the minimum is interpreted as $+\infty$ when $\beta = 0$.

