[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Consider a pullback square of fpqc algebraic stacks
  \begin{equation*}
    \begin{tikzcd}
      \mcalY' \arrow[r,"g'"] \arrow[d,"f'"'] & \mcalY \arrow[d,"f"] \\
      \mcalX' \arrow[r,"g"'] & \mcalX.
    \end{tikzcd}
  \end{equation*}
  Assume that  \(f \colon \mcalY \to \mcalX\) is a \(BE^\sharp\)-torsor for a vector bundle \(E\) of finite rank on $\mcalX$.
  Then the base change morphism
  \begin{equation*}
    \BC_{f,g}(\cO_{\mcalY})\colon Lg^*Rf_*\cO_{\mcalY}\to Rf'_*\cO_{\mcalY'}
  \end{equation*}
  defined in \Cref{QuasiCoherentBaseChangeMorphism} is an equivalence in \(\mcalD_{\qcoh}(\mcalX')\).

