body:
[Proposition 8 (Composite profile) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] For each $M\ge0$ there are unique planar correctors
$(U_j,\Phi_j)_{1\le j\le M}$, with zero fluid data at $t=t_0$ and zero
far-field limits, such that the profile \eqref{eq:corrector-ansatz} obeys
\begin{equation*}
  \sup_{0<\eps\le\eps_0}
  \bigl(\abs{n^a}_{\cX_{s+3,T}}+\abs{u^a}_{\cX_{s+3,T}}
  +\abs{\phi^a}_{\cX_{s+3,T}}\bigr)\le C_{M,t_0,T}, 
\end{equation*}
and, for $\eps_0$ small,
$n^a\in[3n_*/4,5n^*/4]$.  Its residual satisfies
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
  &\sup_{t_0\le t\le T}
  \bigl(\norm{\cR_n^a}_{H^{s+1}}+\norm{\cR_u^a}_{H^{s+1}}
  +\norm{\cR_\phi^a}_{H^{s+1}}
  +\norm{\pa_t\cR_\phi^a}_{H^s}\bigr)
  \le C_{M,t_0,T}\eps^{2M+2}. 
\end{split}
\end{equation}
All residuals and all corrector derivatives vanish at spatial infinity.

