body:
[Corollary cor:ratio-lb-p2inf of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $2 < p < \infty$ and let $V$ be as in (thm:gradphi-large-deviations of the paper). There exists a constant $c > 0$ such that for all $h \geq 1$,
    \begin{equation*}
 \frac{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi_o = h)}{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi_o = h-1)}\geq \exp\big[-c\beta h\big] \,. 
    \end{equation*}

