{"artifact_digest":"sha256:6103cfbb451caf008a72f4e24d841ce706f38aaad3b4c61dd8c63a07e4cdbfad","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/61/6103cfbb451caf008a72f4e24d841ce706f38aaad3b4c61dd8c63a07e4cdbfad.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:797720a6ac36eb2a53380a1ad49415340812da71ecc643e3a341cc5d2dff3032","bundle_entry_key":"2509-04333-theorem-60-ratio-lb-p2inf","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_015","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_015.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2509-04333-corollary-60-ratio-lb-p2inf","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: By (lem:bd-outermost-loop of the paper), there exists $C$ such that 
    \[{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi_o = h-1) = (1+o(1)){\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi_o = h-1,\,  \mathscr{W}(\Gamma_1) \leq Ch)\,.\]
    On the latter event, consider the map $T(\phi) = \psi$ which raises the interior of $\Gamma_1(\phi)$ by 1. Then, we have 
    \begin{align*}
    -\frac{1}{\beta}\log\frac{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(T(\phi))}{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi)} &= \sum_{e \in \Gamma_1(\phi)} (\Delta_e + 1)^p - \Delta_e^p\\
    &\leq p2^{p-1}\mathscr{W}(\Gamma_1(\phi))\,.
