[Theorem thm:smallpmono of arXiv:2608.11378, 'On the most likely geodesic in last passage percolation'] Assume $d=2$. There is $p_{n} > 0$ such that if $\omega_x \sim \mathrm{Ber}(p)$ with $0 < p \le p_n$, we have for all paths $\pi,\, \gamma \in \Gamma_n$ the implication
    \begin{equation}

        \pi \succ \gamma \Rightarrow \mathbb{P}(\pi \in \Gamma^*_n ) \ge \mathbb{P}(\gamma \in \Gamma^*_n).
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, this inequality is strict unless $\pi = \gamma$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Closed blocks of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:closed_blocks}
    Let $b \in \mathbf{N}$ and let $A_0,\ldots,A_{b-1}$ be a $1$-disconnected sequence of $1$-connected sets.

    Then there exists $\ell \leq b$ and $(B_0,\ldots,B_{\ell-1}) \in \mathcal{A}(\ell)$ such that $\cup_{i \leq b} A_i \subset \cup_{j \leq \ell} B_j$ and $\cup_{j \leq \ell} \partial B_j \subset \cup_{i \leq b} \partial A_i$.

[Proposition 3 (Partial coloring \cite{Versh-Sm-3}) of arXiv:2607.12263, 'Random sets are close to low-discrepancy sets'] Let $v_1,\ldots,v_m\in\R^D$ be any vectors, and let $\varepsilon_1,\ldots,\varepsilon_m$ be independent fair signs.  For every $T>0$ there is a randomized algorithm that discards some of the terms $\varepsilon_i v_i$ so that
	\begin{equation}
		\max_{r\le m} \norm*{\sum_{i\le r\,\textrm{accepted}}\varepsilon_i v_i}_\infty\le T,
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
		\Prob{v_i\text{ is discarded}}\le \frac{\pi}{T}\norm{v_i}_2
		\qquad \text{for each } i.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

