body:
[Definition 13 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Fix~$\chi:[0,\infty) \to [0,1]$ be a smooth cutoff function satisfying
\begin{equation}
\chi(x) =
\begin{cases}
1 & x \in [0,\tfrac12], \\
0 & x \in [1,\infty),
\end{cases}
\qquad
\chi' \le 0 .
\end{equation}

For any $a, \tilde a, \epsilon > 0$, define $P : \R^d \times \R^d \to [0,\infty)$ by
\begin{equation}
P(y,z)
=
\frac12\, y^T K y\;
\chi\!\left(\frac{|y|^2}{a^2\epsilon}\right)
\chi\!\left(\frac{|z|^2}{\tilde a^2 a^2 \epsilon}\right),
\qquad y,z \in \R^d .
\end{equation}

