body:
[Lemma lemma34 of arXiv:2411.18374, 'Drawdowns of diffusions'] It holds for $\delta>0$ and $y>\delta+l$
\begin{align}

        &n^y_-\left( 1-\rm e^{-\alpha \zeta(e)}\,{\bf 1}_{\{ H_{y-\delta}(e)=\infty\}}\right) =
\begin{cases}
b_\alpha(y;\delta)& \alpha>0,\\
(S(y)-S(y-\delta))^{-1},& \alpha=0,\\
\end{cases}
\end{align}















and
\begin{align}

&    n^y_-\left( \rm e^{-\alpha H_{y-\delta}(e)}\,;\, H_{y-\delta}(e)<\infty\right)
=
\begin{cases}
c_\alpha(y;\delta),& \alpha>0,\\
(S(y)-S(y-\delta))^{-1},& \alpha=0,\\
\end{cases}
\end{align}
where $H_{y-\delta}(e)$ denotes the first hitting time of ${y-\delta}$ for a generic excursion~$e$.

