[Lemma tilt-lr of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $P_{1},P_{2}$ have densities $f_{1},f_{2}$ on $R^{2}$,
and suppose 
\begin{equation}
P_{1}\;\leq _{\mathrm{lr}}\;P_{2},  
\end{equation}
i.e.\ $\frac{f_{2}}{f_{1}}$ is coordinatewise non-decreasing. Define $\tilde{
P}_{i}$ as in Definition~(tilt of the paper). Then 
\begin{equation}
\tilde{P}_{1}\;\leq _{\mathrm{lr}}\;\tilde{P}_{2}.  
\end{equation}

