[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2609.03726, 'Inverse Scattering for Single Photons in Quantum Optics'] There exists $k_\rho>0$ such that the scattering amplitudes
\begin{equation*}
    \{A_k(\theta,\alpha) : \theta,\alpha\in\mathbb{S}^{n-1},\, \theta\neq \alpha, \, k > k_\rho\}
\end{equation*}
uniquely determine the density $\rho$.

