[Def CPS of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A \textbf{conditional probability space} (\textbf{CPS}) (relative to $\cal G$) is a map $p : {\cal G} \rightarrow \Delta(\Omega)$, which we will also write as $G \mapsto p_G(\cdot)$ for $G \in {\cal G}$, satisfying:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $p_G(G) = 1$ for every $G \in \cal G$;
\item $p_G(E) = p_G(F) \times p_F(E)$ for every $E \subseteq F \subseteq G$ with $E \in \cal F$ and $F, G \in \cal G$.
\end{enumerate}

[Defn 24 (The black-golden coupling) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] We say that the decreasing chains $\DMC$ and $\DMC'$ have the \textbf{black-golden coupling} when the dynamics of $\DMC$ (and $\DMC'$) are described for all $t\geq 0$ as follows:\footnote{We stress that here we are using a \emph{unique} set of black and golden instructions for \emph{both} chains $\DMC$ and $\DMC'$.}
    \begin{equation}
    	\DMC_{t+1} = \left\lbrace \begin{aligned}
    	& G_{\DMC_t} \qquad \text{if } \DMC_t \in \intervalleentier{5\ell}{7\ell} \text{ for some good scale $\ell$  and } B_{\DMC_t}  \in \intervalleentier{\ell}{4\ell}; \\
    	&B_{\DMC_t} \qquad \text{otherwise.}
    \end{aligned}
	\right.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, when two chains $\DMC$ and $\DMC'$ are started from $k$ and $k'$ respectively, we denote their joint law under this coupling by $\mathbb{P}_{k,k'}$.

[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] There exists $C>0$ such that for any measurable $f$ from $ \T^d\times \R^d \to \R$ and any $N\in \N^*$, it holds:

\begin{equation*}
\int_{\R^d} \int_{\T^{d}} \langle v \rangle^{2k} | \vartheta^N \ast f(x,v) |^2 \dd x \dd v \leq C\, \int_{\R^d} \int_{\T^{d}} \langle v \rangle^{2k} | f(x,v) |^2 \dd x \dd v .
\end{equation*}

