[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2609.00687, 'A unification of Euler-Maclaurin and Euler-Boole summation formulas'] Let $n,q\in\mathbb{N}$ and $m\in\mathbb{N}_{0}$. Let $\chi$ be a Dirichlet character modulo $q$. Then, for $\lambda\in\mathbb{C}\setminus\{0\}$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\sum_{k=1}^{nq}\chi(k)\lambda^{-k}k^{m}&=&\frac{\lambda^{-qn}}{m+1}\sum_{k=0}^{m}\binom{m+1}{k}(-1)^{k}\beta_{k,\chi^{-}}(\{0\}_{\chi},\lambda)(nq)^{m+1-k}\nonumber\\
&&+\frac{(-1)^{m+1}\beta_{m+1,\chi^{-}}(\{0\}_{\chi},\lambda)(\lambda^{-nq}-1)}{m+1}.
\end{eqnarray}

