body:
[Definition def:NL-MP of arXiv:2604.25851, '{Non-uniqueness of nonlinear Markov processes in the sense of McKean associated with parab'] Let $\mathcal P_0 \subseteq \mathcal P$. A \emph{(time-homogeneous)  nonlinear Markov process} is a family $\{P^\zeta\}_{\zeta \in \mathcal P_0} \subset \mathcal P(\mathcal C)$ such that, setting $\mu^\zeta_t := P^\zeta_t$ for all $(\zeta,t) \in \mathcal P_0 \times \mathbb{R}_+$,
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), font=\normalfont]
        \item $\mu^\zeta_0 = \zeta$ for all $\zeta \in \mathcal P_0$;
        \item $\mu^\zeta_t \in \mathcal P_0$ for all $t > 0, \zeta \in \mathcal P_0$;
        \item the \emph{(time-homogeneous) nonlinear Markov property} holds, i.e.,
        \begin{equation}
        P^\zeta(\pi_{t+s} \in A | \mathcal F_s) ( \cdot) = P^{\mu^\zeta_s,\pi_s(\cdot)}(\pi_t \in A)\quad P^\zeta-\text{a.s.},\quad \forall s,t \geq 0, \, \zeta \in \mathcal P_0, \, A \in \mathcal B(\mathbb{R}^d),
    \end{equation}
    where for $\zeta \in \mathcal P_0$, $\{P^{\zeta,y}\}_{y\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ is the disintegration family of $P^{\zeta}$ with respect to $\pi_0$.
    \end{enumerate}

