[Corollary 25 (Logarithmic rank from polynomial tails) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Suppose that for every compact $K\Subset\C\setminus[-b,b]$ and every $D>0$, an anisotropic local law gives a deterministic $a_n(K)\downarrow0$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{\|p\|=\|q\|=1}
 \Pp\left(
   \sup_{\zeta\in K}
   \left|\ip{p}{(\calR_{X,n}(\zeta)-\Pi(\zeta))q}\right|>a_n(K)
 \right)\le n^{-D}
\end{equation}
for all large $n$, where the supremum means that the same bound holds for every deterministic pair.  Assume that the signal frames $U_n,V_n$ are deterministic, or independent of $X_n$ so that one may condition on them.  If $r_n\le A\log n$ for a fixed $A<\infty$, then the holomorphic subspace local law holds on the signal space.

