[Theorem 30 (Monotone Density Theorem, \protect{\autocite[Theorem 1.7.2) of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] {BinghamGoldieTeugels1987RegularVariation}}]

Let \(f\) be a positive measurable function, locally bounded on
\([A,+\infty)\). Assume that \(f\) is ultimately monotone.

\begin{itemize}
\item
  If there is \(C>0\), \(\beta>0\) and a slowly varying function
  \(\ell\) such that

  \begin{equation*}{
  \int_{A}^{x}f(t)\dd t \sim_{x \to +\infty} C x^{\beta} \ell(x),
   }\end{equation*}

  then \(f(x) \sim_{x \to +\infty} \beta C x^{\beta-1} \ell(x)\).
\item
  If \(\int_{A}^{+\infty}f(t)\dd t < +\infty\) and in addition there is
  \(C>0\), \(\beta < 0\) and a slowly varying function \(\ell\) such
  that

  \begin{equation*}{
  \int_{x}^{+\infty} f(t)\dd t \sim_{x \to +\infty} C x^{\beta} \ell(x),
  }\end{equation*}

  then \(f(x) \sim_{x \to +\infty} -\beta C x^{\beta-1} \ell(x)\).
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem.decom_caonical_easy of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Given a realization $\mathbf{a}$, if $F \subseteq \mathcal{E}(\mathscr{C}_{\operatorname{bc}}^F({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}))$, then for every function $u$ satisfying Definition~(def.ConstantExtension_canonical of the paper), we have
		\begin{align}
			\forall G \subseteq F, \forall x \in {\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \setminus  \mathscr{C}_{\operatorname{bc}}^F({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}), \qquad u^G(x) = u^G([x]).
		\end{align}
		As a consequence, we have 
		\begin{align}
			\forall x \in {\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \setminus  \mathscr{C}_{\operatorname{bc}}^F({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}), \qquad (D_F u)(x) = (D_F u)([x]).
		\end{align}

