[Proposition 34 of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] Let $\tau=(k, k+1)$. Then the elements $\overline{T}_{\sigma}:=T_{\sigma^{-1}}^{-1}$ satisfy  
\begin{equation}
Y_\tau \overline{T}_\sigma=\begin{cases}
    (1-b_2)\overline{T}_\sigma+b_2\overline{T}_{\tau\sigma}\text{, if }\sigma(k)<\sigma(k+1)\\
    (1-b_1)\overline{T}_\sigma+b_1\overline{T}_{\tau\sigma}\text{, if }\sigma(k)>\sigma(k+1)\,.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

