[Proposition prop:d-ddia-derivations of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] $\textbf{CKD} \dashv \vdash \textbf{CK} + \textsf{D}_\Diamond$.
  \begin{proof}
    The following derivations prove both directions.
    \begin{center}
      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{N}_\Box$}}
      \UnaryInfC{$\Box \top$}

      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{D}$}}
      \UnaryInfC{$\Box \top \to \Diamond \top$}

      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{MP}}
      \BinaryInfC{$\Diamond \top$}
      \DisplayProof
    \end{center}

    \begin{center}
      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{D}_\Diamond$}}
      \UnaryInfC{$\Diamond \top$}

      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \UnaryInfC{$\top \to (\varphi \to \varphi)$}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{M}_\Diamond$}}
      \UnaryInfC{$\Diamond \top \to \Diamond (\varphi \to \varphi)$}

      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{MP}}
      \BinaryInfC{$\Diamond (\varphi \to \varphi)$}

      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{$\textsf{FS1}$}}
      \UnaryInfC{$\Diamond (\varphi \to \varphi) \to (\Box \varphi \to \Diamond \varphi)$}

      \RightLabel{\scriptsize{MP}}
      \BinaryInfC{$\Box \varphi \to \Diamond \varphi$}
      \DisplayProof
    \end{center}
  \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

