[Lemma lem: mass growth rate of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] If $\boldsymbol{\mu} \in \mathcal{S}^+$, then we have:
	\begin{equation*}
		\boldsymbol{\mu}_t\left(\mathbbm{R}_+ \times [0, y]\right) - \boldsymbol{\mu}_s\left(\mathbbm{R}_+ \times [0, y]\right) \leq \lambda_0(t - s) \quad \text{for all} \quad 0 \leq s \leq t \quad \text{and} \quad y \in \mathbbm{R}_+.
	\end{equation*}
	Furthermore, $\boldsymbol{\mu}_t(\mathbbm{R}_+^2) - \boldsymbol{\mu}_s(\mathbbm{R}_+^2) \leq \lambda_0(t - s)$ for all $0 \leq s \leq t$.

