[Prop 8 of arXiv:2510.21595, 'One-arm exponents of high-dimensional percolation revisited'] Let $d>6$ and $L\geq L_0$. There exist $c_2,C_2>0$ such that, for every $\tfrac{p_c}{2}\leq p<p_c$,
\begin{equation}
	c_2(p_c-p)^{-1/2}\leq\chi^{\mathbb H}(p)\leq C_2(p_c-p)^{-1/2}.
\end{equation}

