[Definition 2 of arXiv:2604.04840, 'Bounding the Gap Between Zeros of the Variable-\\Parameter Confluent Hypergeometric Functi'] The function $\Phi(a,b,z)$ is related to Whittaker's $\mathcal{M}$ function, defined as \cite{Buchholz}\footnote[2]{The normalizing factor $\Gamma(1+\mu)$ ensures that $\mathcal{M}_{\varkappa, \mu/2}(z)$ is defined even when $\mu$ is a negative integer.}

	\begin{equation}

		\mathcal{M}_{\varkappa, \mu/2}(z) = \frac{1}{\Gamma(1+\mu)} z^{(1+\mu)/2}e^{-z/2} \Phi\left(\frac{1+\mu}{2} - \varkappa, 1 + \mu, z\right)
	\end{equation}

[Proposition pr:outer of arXiv:2604.21142, 'Gaussian fluctuations for Internal DLA on cylinders'] For every $
 > 0$ there exist $C' = C'(
