[Lem muH-neg of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] \begin{itemize}
         \item For all $\mu \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M})$, we have $\mu H \leq 0$. Also, $\mu H = 0$ if and only if  $\mu \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_+)$.
         \item Since $P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_+)$ is compact, for all $\epsilon > 0$ there is a compact set $\mathcal{K} \subset \mathcal{M}_+$ such that $\mu(\mathcal{K}) \geq 1 - \epsilon$ for all $\mu \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_+)$.
