[Theorem thm: convergence of the polymer partition function of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] {}
	Let $S=(S_{n})_{n\geq 0}$ be a random walk on~${\ensuremath{\mathbb Z}} ^{d}$ satisfying the assumptions of Section~(subsec: longrange RW of the paper), and assume that $\gamma < 1+\frac{\alpha}{d}$. 
	Note in particular that it guarantees that \( V_N (a_N)^{-d}\to \infty\) as \(N\to\infty\).
	Assume also the following scaling for the parameter~\(\beta_N\): 
	\begin{equation}

	 \lim_{N\to\infty} \beta_N V_N (a_N)^{-d}= \hat{\beta} \in [0,\infty) \,.
	\end{equation}
	Then, we have the following convergence in distribution:
	\begin{equation}
	Z_N^{\omega,\beta_N} \xrightarrow[\ N\to\infty\ ]{(d)}	
	{\ensuremath{\mathcal Z}}^{\boldsymbol\zeta,\hat{\beta}} = 1 + \sum\limits_{k \, \geqslant\, 1} \frac{\hat{\beta}^k}{k!} \int_{(0,1)^k \times ({\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} ^{d})^k} \prod\limits_{j=1}^k  \boldsymbol\psi^{(k)}\big((t_1,x_1),\dots,(t_k,x_k)\big) \prod\limits_{j=1}^k \boldsymbol\zeta(\mathrm{d} t_j \mathrm{d} x_j) \,,
	\end{equation}
	where $\boldsymbol\zeta$ is a $\gamma$-stable noise on $(0,1) \times {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} ^{d}$ and \(\boldsymbol\psi^{(k)}\) is defined in~(equation eq: continuum correlation functions of the polymer model of the paper).
	This convergence holds jointly with the convergence of the discrete noise to $\boldsymbol\zeta$.
	Furthermore, for every $p \in [1,\gamma)$, ${\ensuremath{\mathcal Z}}^{\boldsymbol\zeta,\hat{\beta}}$ has a finite moment of order~$p$, and 
	$\lim_{N \to +\infty} \mathds{E}[(Z_{N}^{\omega,\beta_N})^p] = \mathds{E}[({\ensuremath{\mathcal Z}}^{\boldsymbol\zeta,\hat{\beta}})^p]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

