body:
[Theorem EHI:t:main of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy process on $\mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying (equation EHI:e:regularJumps of the paper).
    Let $j(r)$ be its jump kernel, and let $m_2(r)$ and $\lambda(r)$ be as defined in (equation EHI:e:m2def of the paper) and (equation EHI:e:lambdadef of the paper). Let $M, C, c > 0$ and $\varepsilon \in (0, 1]$, and let $(r_n) \subseteq (0, \infty)$ be a sequence of positive numbers such that $M^{-1} \leq \frac{r_{n+1}}{r_n} \leq M$ for all $n$.
    Suppose that for all $n$, we have either
    \begin{equation}
        m_2(r_n) \geq c r_n^2 \lambda(r_n)
    \end{equation}
    or
    \begin{equation}
        m_2(r_n) \leq C \left( r_n^{d+2} j(r_n) \right)^\varepsilon \left( r_n^2 \lambda(r_n) \right)^{1-\varepsilon}.
    \end{equation}
    If $r_n \to 0$, then $X$ satisfies $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}(r \leq 1)$. If $r_n \to \infty$, then $X$ satisfies $\hyperref[EHI:d:ehi]{\mathrm{EHI}}(r \geq 1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

