[Lemma K of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] If the strongly local regular Dirichlet form $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ on $L^2(X,\mu)$ satisfies (eq:HKMain of the paper) then there are constants $K \geq 1$ and $\sigma > 1$ depending only on the constants associated to $\Psi$ in (equation eq:PsiRad of the paper), the constants in (eq:HKMain of the paper) and the doubling constant of $\mu$ in (equation eq:muDoubling of the paper) such that
    \begin{align*}
        h_{x_0,R_0}(x) & \geq 2K \Psi(R_0) \text{ for all } x \in B(x_0,\kappa R_0),\\
        h_{x_0,R_0}(x) & \leq K \Psi(R_0) \text{ for all } x \in X \setminus B(x_0,\sigma R_0).
    \end{align*}
    Here $\kappa$ is the constant in (eq:HKMain of the paper).

[Proposition proposition_asymp_E_psi of arXiv:2609.00973, 'The Vlasov-Maxwell point charge system : study of the spherically symmetric case'] Let 
   \begin{equation*}
       \mathcal{E}(t,a):=4\pi^2\iiint \1_{\{\alpha\leq a\}}\gamma(t,\theta,\alpha,\ell)\mathrm{d}\theta\mathrm{d}\alpha\mathrm{d}\ell.
   \end{equation*}
   Then, there exists $\mathcal{E}_\infty\in L^\infty((0,+\infty))$ such that 
   \begin{equation}

       |\mathcal{E}(t,a)-\mathcal{E}_\infty(a)|\lesssim \varepsilon_1^2t^{-\frac{1}{4}},\qquad |\mathcal{E}_\infty(a)|\lesssim \varepsilon_0. 
   \end{equation}
   Moreover, in $\mathcal{B}_t^*$, we find
\begin{equation}

    \1_{\mathcal{B}_t^*}\left|\partial_a\widetilde{\Psi}+\frac{1}{t}\frac{m^2}{a^0a^2}\mathcal{E}_\infty(a)\right|\lesssim \varepsilon_1 t^{-\frac{6}{5}}.
\end{equation}

