[Lemma convergence of the truncated partition function with general G of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] {}
	Assume that $\lim_{N\to\infty} \beta_N V_N (a_N)^{-d}= \hat{\beta} \in [0,\infty)$.
	Then, for every $A > 0$, we have the following convergence in distribution: 
	\begin{equation*}
		Z_{N,A}^{\omega,\beta_N}(G) \xrightarrow[\ N\to\infty\ ]{(d)}
		{\ensuremath{\mathcal Z}}_A^{\boldsymbol\zeta, \hat{\beta}}(G) = \sum\limits_{k \, \geqslant\, 0} \hat{\beta}^k \int_{0 < t_1 < \dots < t_k < 1} \int_{({\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} ^{d})^k} \boldsymbol\psi_A^{(k)}\big((t_1,x_1),\dots,(t_k,x_k);G\big) \prod\limits_{j=1}^k \boldsymbol\zeta(\mathrm{d} t_j \mathrm{d} x_j),
	\end{equation*}
	where $\boldsymbol\psi_A^{(k)}\big((t_1,x_1),\dots,(t_k,x_k);G\big) := \prod\limits_{j=1}^k g_{t_j-t_{j-1}}(x_j - x_{j-1})\, \mathrm{E}[f_A({\ensuremath{\mathbf X}} ^*) G({\ensuremath{\mathbf X}} ) \mid {\ensuremath{\mathbf X}} _{t_1} = x_1, \dots , {\ensuremath{\mathbf X}} _{t_k} = x_k]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

