[Corollary cor:local_subgraph_clt_norho of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Under the same assumption as in Corollary (cor:local_subgraph_clt of the paper),
for all $\varepsilon > 0$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{d}_\mathrm{Was}\mleft(\frac{\mathsf{N}_G^{v}(X) - \mathbb{E}[\mathsf{N}_G^v(X)]}{2 \mathsf{e} p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} \varsigma_n}, Z\mright)
    \lesssim n^{-\frac{1}{4}+\varepsilon} + \delta_n.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:S6V-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] For $t \ge 1$ and
$\zeta \in \mathbb{C} \setminus \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$, the Fredholm
determinant $\mathcal{L}_{t,x,m}(\zeta)
= \det(I + K_{t,x,m})$ satisfies
\begin{align}
&(1 - b_1)
\mathcal{L}_{t,x+1,m+1}
\mathcal{L}_{t-1,x,m}
- (1 - b_2)
\mathcal{L}_{t-1,x,m+1}
\mathcal{L}_{t,x+1,m} \notag\\
&\qquad+ (b_1 - b_2)
\mathcal{L}_{t,x,m+1}
\mathcal{L}_{t-1,x+1,m}
= 0.
\end{align}

[Thm cor:boundtype2constant of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Let $r\geq 2$ an integer, $2 \leq p < \infty$, and $\mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)$ the Type-2 constant of the $\ell_p$ injective norm of order $r$ tensors (see Definition~(def:type2constant of the paper)) then
\begin{equation}
d^{\frac12 - \frac1p}\underset{r,p}{\lesssim}  \mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d) 
\underset{r,p}{\lesssim} d^{\frac12- \frac1{\max\{p,2r\}}}\log d.
\end{equation}
(The expression $f \lesssim_{r,p} g$ says that the inequality $ f \leq C_{r,p} g$ holds for some constant $C_{r,p}$ that only depends on $r$ and $p$.) (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

