[Theorem firstlem of arXiv:2605.27949, 'Yaglom limits of continuous-state branching processes in Brownian random environment \than'] For any $z>0,\lambda>0,$ we have
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E^{z}\left[\exp \left(-\lambda Z_t \right)\right]=\mathbb E\left[\exp \left(-z \xi_t(\lambda) \right)\right],
\end{equation}
and thus
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb{P}^z\left(Z_t>0\right)=1-\mathbb E\left[\exp \left(-z \zeta_t\right)\right].
\end{equation}

