[Theorem main result 4 of arXiv:2412.09850, 'Averaging principles for time-inhomogeneous multi-scale SDEs via nonautonomous Poisson equ'] Suppose that Assumptions {\rm(B1 of the paper)}, {\rm(A3 of the paper)} and {\rm(A4 of the paper)} hold. Let $\{(X_t^\varepsilon, Y_t^\varepsilon) \}_{t\ge0}$ and $\{\bar X_t\}_{t\ge0}$ be the solutions to (equation Equation of the paper) and (equation AVE22 of the paper) respectively. Then for any $T>0$, $\beta\in(0,1)$ and $\varphi\in C^4_b(\mathbb{R}^n)$, there is a constant $C_{\varphi,T,\beta}>0$ such that for all $\varepsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}\begin{split}
&\sup_{0\leqslant t\leqslant T}|\mathbb{E} \varphi(X^{\varepsilon}_t)-\mathbb{E} \varphi(\bar{X}_t)|\\
&\leqslant C_{\varphi,T,\beta}\left(1+|x|+|y|\right)\varepsilon\Big\{\int_0^{T/\varepsilon}\Big[\Big(\int^{s}_0 e^{-2\beta\alpha (s-r)}\phi^2(r)\,dr\Big)^{1/2}\Big]\,ds+\sup_{t\in [0,T]}\Lambda_\gamma(t/\varepsilon)\Big\}.
\end{split}\end{equation}

