[Lem 48 (Upper bound on the sum of remainders) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that, almost surely, for any $n_0\geq 2$, we have
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n=n_0}^{\infty} |R_n| \leq C \cdot \sum_{k=X_{n_0}}^\infty (\sttm_k)^{\frac{1}{2}-\alpha }\left(\sum_{n=\sttm_k}^{\sttm_{k+1}-1} r(n) f(T_n)\right).
\end{align*}

