[Thm 4 (Grigor'yan~\cite{grigoryan1,grigoryan2}) of arXiv:2606.02570, 'Stochastic completeness for landmark space'] Let $(M,g)$ be a geodesically complete Riemannian manifold. Suppose that, for some $z\in M$, the volumes $V(r)$ of the geodesic balls with center $z$ and of radius $r>0$ satisfy, for some $a>0$,
    \begin{displaymath}
        \int_a^\infty\frac{r\dd r}{\log V(r)} =\infty.
    \end{displaymath}
    Then $(M,g)$ is stochastically complete. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

