[Lemma lemAiry: c_1 small difference of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Suppose that $c$ solves (equation eqAiry: dc/ds ODE of the paper) on $[s_0,s_1]$. Then, for $s\in[s_0,s_1]$,
	\begin{equation}
		\lVert c_\perp(s)\rVert_{\ell^2}
		\leq
		\exp\{-\gamma(s-s_0)\}\lVert c_\perp(s_0)\rVert_{\ell^2}
		+C_A\lVert c(s_0)\rVert_{\ell^2}
		\int_{s_0}^s
		\exp\{-\gamma(s-u)\}\lvert B_q(u)\rvert\,\text{d} u
	\end{equation}
	with $C_A$ defined in (equation eqAiry: sum |A_1j|^2 of the paper). Also,
	\begin{equation}
		\lvert c_1(s)-c_1(s_0)\rvert
		\leq C \lVert c(s_0)\rVert_{\ell^2}
		\bigl(\mathcal{E}(q)^{1/2}+\mathcal{E}(q)\bigr)
	\end{equation}
	for a numerical constant $C>0$.

