[Lemma lem:abstract-gaussian-disintegration of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] With $t$ and $x^\perp$ defined in
(equation eq:abstract-slice-coordinates of the paper), $t\sim N(0,\Sigma^{-1})$ and is independent of
$x^\perp$.  Its density is
\begin{equation}
 \varphi_{H_N}(a)
 =(2\pi)^{-N/2}(\det\Sigma)^{1/2}
 \exp\!\left(-\tfrac12a^\top\Sigma a\right)>0.

\end{equation}
Consequently, for every non-negative Borel $F:X\to[0,\infty]$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E[F(x)]
 =\int_{X}\int_{\mathbb R^N}
 F(x^\perp+v_a)\varphi_{H_N}(a)\,da\,
 \mathbb P_{H_N}^\perp(dx^\perp),

\end{equation}
where $\mathbb P_{H_N}^\perp=\operatorname{Law}(x^\perp)$.

[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $C_n=Y_1+\cdots+Y_n$. Then

\begin{equation*}
\Pp_{\mathfrak a}\left(C_n\in ny_0+\mathcal L\right)=1,
\qquad n\geq1.
\end{equation*}

Consequently, the regenerative exact-time renewal mass is supported by the renewal lattice $\mathcal L_*$. If $\mathcal L_*=\Z^d$, there is no renewal-periodic obstruction. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

