[Corollary 7 (Renormalized scale derivative) of arXiv:2609.01319, 'Matched Queries for Curvature and Density at Branching Junctions'] For fixed $1<\lambda\le\lambda_{\max}$ and compact $\cQ$,
\begin{equation}
\sup_{z\in\cQ}\norm{\cD_{\sigma,\lambda}(z)-G(z)}
\le C_{\cQ,\lambda}\sigma^\alpha.

\end{equation}
Equivalently,
$G(z)=\partial_\sigma[\sigma s_\sigma(x_0+\sigma z)]|_{\sigma=0^+}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 1 (Edge case) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] Fix an integer \(\ell\ge 1\).
For \(1 \leq i,j \leq \ell \), the overlap matrix converges to the identity matrix, i.e.~$\lim_{N\to\infty}(\Omega_{i,j}^{(N)})_{1\leq i,j\leq \ell}=I_{\ell}$ (in agreement with \cite{bao2025}). Furthermore, the leading-order correction scales as $O(N^{-1/3})$ and is given by:
\begin{equation}
  N^{1/3}\bigl(\Omega^{(N)}_{i,j}-(I_{\ell})_{i,j}\bigr)\;
  \mathrel{\underset{N\to\infty}{\overset{d}{\sim}}}\;
  \begin{cases}
    \dfrac{\overline{g_i}\, g_j}{\alpha_j-\alpha_i}, & i\neq j,\\[0.6ex]
    0, & i=j,
  \end{cases}
  \qquad 1\leq i,j\leq \ell.
\end{equation}

\noindent
Here \((\alpha_i)_{i=1}^\ell\) follow the Airy$_{\beta}$ point process, and \((g_i)_{i=1}^\ell\) are i.i.d.\ standard Gaussians \(\mathcal{N}_\beta(0,1)\) independent of \((\alpha_i)\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem local curve GW universal series of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] There exist universal series $A,B_2,\ldots,B_5$ in $\epsilon_2,\ldots,\epsilon_5$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \GWargs{Z}{\mathsf{T}}{[C]} = A^{g_C -1}\prod_{i=2}^5 B_i^{\deg \cL_i} \,.
    \end{equation}
    At this stage, we do not impose the Calabi--Yau condition. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary c:cutoff_geod of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] The following holds on the event $\Omega_1$. Let $\xi \in \Xi$, and $b \in \mathcal{F}^\xi$. If for some $t \in \mathbb{R}, \tau_t^{b,L} \in \mathbb{R}$, then
    \begin{equation} 
    g_{(\tau_t^{b,L},t)}^{b,L}(s) =g_{(\tau_t^{b,L},t)}^{\xi -,L}(s) \qquad\text{for all }s \le t, 
    \end{equation}
    Additionally, if for some $t \in \mathbb{R}, \tau_t^{b,R} \in \mathbb{R}$, then
    \begin{equation} 
    g_{(\tau_t^{b,R},t)}^{b,R}(s) =g_{(\tau_t^{b,R},t)}^{\xi +,R}(s) \qquad\text{for all }s \le t. 
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

