[Definition 52 ($Tri(\mathbf{R}^3)$) of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] $Tri(\mathbf{R}^3)$ is the collection of triangles in $\mathbf{R}^3$ defined by
\begin{equation*}
Tri(\mathbf{R}^3):= \{ OAB,\ OBC,\ OCD,\ ODE,\ OEF, \text{ and } OFA \ |\  (l, m, n)\in \mathbf{Z}^3 \},
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{align*}
&O=(l,\ m,\ n),\ A=(l+1,\ m,\ n),\ B=(l+1,\ m+1,\ n),\\
&C=(l,\ m+1,\ n),\ D=(l,\ m+1,\ n+1),\ E=(l,\ m,\ n+1),\\
&F=(l+1,\ m,\ n+1), \text{ and }G=(l+1,\ m+1,\ n+1) \in \mathbf{Z}^3
\end{align*}
(Figure \ref{figure5} (a)). The elements of $Tri(\mathbf{R}^3)$ are called \textit{slant} triangles.

