body:
[Cor 24 (Round-sphere extensions) of arXiv:2609.00922, 'The Morse Index, Nullity and Jacobi Fields of Constant-Curvature 2-Spheres in Complex Proj'] Regard $S^{2m}(1)$ as a totally geodesic subsphere of $S^{2m+a}(1)$, where
$a\ge0$, and view $F_m^{(1)}$ as an immersion into the latter.  Let
$J_m^{(a)}$ denote the resulting Jacobi operator, and write
$\Ind_m^{(a)}:=\Ind_{S^{2m+a}(1)}(F_m^{(1)})$ and
$\Nul_m^{(a)}:=\Nul_{S^{2m+a}(1)}(F_m^{(1)})$.  Then
\begin{equation}

 \Ind_m^{(a)}=m(m-1)(2m+1)+am^2,\qquad
 \Nul_m^{(a)}=(2m+3)(2m-2)+a(2m+1).
\end{equation}
As real $\SO(3)$-modules,
\begin{equation}

 \ker J_m^{(a)}\simeq_{\mathbb R}\ker J_m^{(0)}
 \oplus(\mathcal H_m^{\mathbb R})^{\oplus a}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 12 (Heat evolution and jump rule) of arXiv:2607.18032, 'FRSB in the SK spin glass: convergence to full-interval support at zero temperature'] Let $u:=u^{|\cdot|,\gamma}$ solve \eqref{eq:zt-general-PDE}, let $X$ solve \eqref{eq:zt-optimal-SDE}, and define $Q$ from $u$, $\gamma$, and the density $\rho_t$ of $X_t$ as above. If $0\leq a<b<1$ and $\gamma(r)=m$ for every $r\in(a,b)$, then
\begin{equation}
 \partial_tQ(t,x)=\frac12\partial_{xx}Q(t,x),
 \qquad \forall (t,x)\in(a,b)\times\R.

\end{equation}
If $t\in(0,1)$ is a jump point of $\gamma$ and $\delta:=\gamma(t)-\gamma(t-)>0$, then
\begin{equation}
 Q(t,x)=e^{-\delta u(t,x)}Q(t-,x),
 \qquad \forall x\in\R.

\end{equation}

