[Lemma lem: prob: late points of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] {prevost2023phase}}]

    For all $\alpha_1>\alpha_0>0$ and $\beta_0>0$, there exists a constant $C=C(\alpha_0,\alpha_1,\beta_0)>0$ such that for all $N \in \mathbb{N}$ and $G\subset \mathbb{T}_N$ such that $\capacity(G) \leq \beta_0$,
    \begin{equation}

        \left|\frac{\mathsf{P}(G \subset \mathcal{L}^\alpha)}{N^{-d\alpha g(0)\capacity(G)}} - 1\right| \leq C\frac{(\log N)^{3/2}}{N^{(d-2)/2}} \quad 
         \forall\, \alpha \in [\alpha_0,\alpha_1].
    \end{equation}
    In particular, for $G=\{0\}$, we have uniformly in $\alpha \in [\alpha_0,\alpha_1]$, 
    \begin{equation}

        \mathsf{P}(0 \in \mathcal{L}^\alpha) = \big(1+o(1)\big)N^{-d\alpha}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

