\begin{itemize}

\item {\it Bounding the alternating sum  $\sum_{\nu=1}^\infty \frac{(-1)^\nu}{\nu(\nu-y)}$:}
We apply the partial fraction identity:
\begin{equation}

\frac{1}{\nu(\nu - y)} = \frac{1}{y} \left( \frac{1}{\nu - y} - \frac{1}{\nu} \right).
\end{equation}
Thus
