body:
[Lemma 12 (Linearized master equation) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Let $\zeta\notin\spec(\calX_n)$ and define
\[
   \calF_n(\zeta):=\Id_{2r_n}-\calG_n(\zeta)\calK_n.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
  \det(\zeta\Id-\calW_n)
  =\det(\zeta\Id-\calX_n)\det\calF_n(\zeta).
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
  \calE_n^*(\zeta\Id-\calW_n)^{-1}\calE_n
  =\calF_n(\zeta)^{-1}\calG_n(\zeta)
\end{equation}
whenever either side is defined.

For real $z>\norm{X_n}_{\op}$, $\calG_n(z)$ is positive definite and
\begin{equation}
  \#\{j:\sigma_j(W_n)>z\}
  =\#\left\{\lambda\in\spec\bigl(\calG_n(z)^{1/2}\calK_n\calG_n(z)^{1/2}\bigr):\lambda>1\right\}.
\end{equation}

