body:
[Proposition GWP-NS-cut-off of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Fix $a<\frac{1}{2}<2b+a$. For every initial data $u_0\in H^{2b+a}$, there exists a unique strong solution to (equation NS-cut off of the paper) in the sense of Definition (NS-def sol of the paper). Moreover, the solution instantaneously gains regularity in time and space 
		\begin{equation*}
			u\in C_t^{1/2-}C_x^{\infty},\;\mathbb{P}\text{-a.s. for every } t>0,\; x\in \mathbb{T}^3.
		\end{equation*} 
		In particular, It\^o's formula can be applied to $\|u\|_{H^{2b+a}}^2$ directly, yielding
		\begin{equation*}
			\sup_{t\in [0,T]}\|u(t)\|_{H^{2b+a}}^2 + \int_{0}^{T} \|u(t)\|_{H^{2b+a+1}}^2\,{\,\rm d} t\leq C\big(\|u_0\|_{H^{2b+a}},R,\delta,T\big),\quad \mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.}
		\end{equation*}
		where the upper bound is independent of the choice of $\{\sigma_k\}$.

