[Lemma lem:unshuffling-lemma of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $\mathbb{X}$ be a set and let $\psi$ be an $\mathbb{X}$-shuffling rule.
	If $\psi$ is $\mathfrak{S}$-equivariant, then for all $T,T'\in\trees$, ${\boldsymbol{x}}\in\mathbb{X}^T$, ${\boldsymbol{x}}'\in\mathbb{X}^{T'}$, ${\boldsymbol{\uppi}}\in\mathfrak{S}_T$, we have the equivalence
	\begin{align}
	\begin{cases}
	T'	= \bigl({\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T,{\boldsymbol{x}}}\bigr)\cdotT\\
	{\boldsymbol{x}}' = \bigl({\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T,{\boldsymbol{x}}}\bigr)_*\,{\boldsymbol{x}}
	\end{cases}
	\quad\iff\quad
	\begin{cases}
	T	=	\bigl(\overline{{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}}^\psi_{T',{\boldsymbol{x}}'}\bigr)\cdotT'\\
	{\boldsymbol{x}} = \bigl(\overline{{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}}^\psi_{T',{\boldsymbol{x}}'}\bigr)_*\,{\boldsymbol{x}}',
	\end{cases}
	\end{align}
	and if one of these equivalent conditions is satisfied then ${\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T',{\boldsymbol{x}}'}=(\overline{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T,{\boldsymbol{x}}})^{-1}$.

