[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2605.27212, '2605.27212'] Assume that, for every nonnegative \(F:\mathcal X\to\mathbb R\) with
\(\supp(F)\subseteq G\),
\begin{equation}
    \Ent_\mu(F^2)\le A\cE_P^\mu(F,F).
\end{equation}
Then every nonnegative \(f:G\to\mathbb R\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
    \Ent_{\pi_G}(f^2)\le A\cE_{K_G}^{\pi_G}(f,f).
\end{equation}

[Definition def: cycle conditon of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] A random vector $\Psi\colon \Omega \times \mathcal{N} \to \mathbb{R}$, satisfies the \emph{cycle condition} if for any sequence $(x_{0}, \cdots, x_{n})$ in $\mathbb{Z}^{d}$, with $x_{0} = x_{n}$ and $(x_{j-1}, x_{j}) \in \vec{E}_d$, $1 \leq j \leq n$, it holds that

  \begin{align}

    \sum_{j=1}^{n}\Psi(\tau_{x_{j-1}}\omega, x_{j} - x_{j-1}) \;=\; 0.
  \end{align}

[Conjecture length_spectrum_brownian_surface of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] Let $\mathbf{S}_{g}$ be the unit-area Brownian surface of genus $g$ with no boundary introduced in [bettinelli2022compact]. Define $\Upxi_g$ to be the multiset of the lengths of closed geodesics on $\mathbf{S}_g$, in the sense of shortest closed paths in their homotopy class. Then we expect
\begin{align*}
    (80 g)^{\frac{1}{4}}\,\Upxi_g \xrightarrow[g\to\infty]{\mathrm{(d)}} \mathcal{P},
\end{align*}
where $\mathcal{P}$ is the same Poisson point process on $\mathbb{R}_{+}$ with intensity $\frac{\cosh{t}-1}{t}\mathrm{d}t$ as above. In the convergence, the random multiset $\Upxi_g$ is regarded as a random point process on $[0,\infty)$.
The curious constant $(80)^{1/4}$ arises from the combination of $\alpha_2$ from Corollary~(main_corollary of the paper) with the scaling constant $c_{\mathrm{WP}} = 2 \pi /\sqrt{3 j_0}$ of  [budd2025random] or [budd2025tree], which satisfy $\alpha_2\,c_{\mathrm{WP}} = (80)^{1/4}$. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

