body:
[Lem n covering of arXiv:2609.01791, 'Minimum $b_2$ of symplectic fillings of lens spaces'] Let $\textbf{n}$ be obtained from $(0)$ through a sequence of strict blowup, with at least one of those strict blowups being a middle blowup. Then, $adjusted(\textbf{n})$ covers at least one of the following:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $(1,0^{[k]},k)$ for some $k\ge 1$;
\item $(1,k,0^{[k+1]},2)$ for some $k\ge 0$;
\item $(1,0^{[k_1]},1,0^{[k_2+1]},k_2,k_1+2)$ for some $k_1,k_2\ge 0$.
\end{enumerate}

