body:
[Lemma lm:lip of arXiv:2508.21055, 'Modern aspects of Markov chains:\\entropy, curvature and the cutoff phenomenon'] For any non-zero $f\in \mathcal {F}^+$ and any $t> 0$,
\begin{eqnarray*}
\mathrm {Lip} \log P_t f & \le & 3\log d+2\log_+\left(\frac{\mathrm{diam}(\mathbb{X})}{t}\right).
\end{eqnarray*}
Moreover, the same conclusion applies to $P_t^\star$ instead of $P_t$, with $d$ replaced by $d^2$.

