[Proposition prop:CRW-infinite-tree-CT of arXiv:2603.00705, '$L^2$-cutoff for the averaging process \\ on random regular graphs'] For all $d\ge 3$, we have
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{a\to -\infty}\liminf_{n\to \infty}n\,\mathbf{P}^{{\rm CRW}(\mathds T_d)}_{o,o}(X_{T(a)}=Y_{T(a)})=\infty\ ,
	\end{equation}
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{a\to \infty}\limsup_{n\to \infty}	n\,\mathbf{P}^{{\rm CRW}(\mathds T_d)}_{o,o}(X_{T(a)}=Y_{T(a)})=0\ .
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:HWILSU of arXiv:2507.08692, 'Some notes on higher order concentration of measure'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on ${\mathbb R}^n$ which satisfies a log-Sobolev inequality as well as $\int x_i d\mu = 0$ for any $i=1, \ldots,n$, and define $f\colon {\mathbb R}^n \to {\mathbb R}$ by $f(x) := x^TAx$, where $A=(a_{ij})_{ij}$ is a symmetric $n \times n$ matrix. Then,
    \[
    \mu(|f - {\mathbb E} f| \ge t) \le 2\exp\Big\{-c \min \Big(\Big(\frac{t}{\sigma^2\lvert A \rvert_{\mathrm{HS}}}\Big)^2, \frac{t}{\sigma^2\lvert A \rvert_{\mathrm{op}}}\Big)\Big\}
    \]
    for any $t \ge 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop p.Ntp-I-nonexistance of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Take $\gamma>2$. Almost surely, for any exceptional time $\tau \in \mathrm{ET}^\gamma$ its associated fiber, $Fib(\tau):=\pi_{\hat{t}}^{-1}(\{\tau\})\cap T^{\gamma}$, is finite. Even more, if $N$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}

        N > \frac{4}{\gamma^2-4}.
    \end{equation}
    Then, almost surely there are no exceptional times $\tau$ with at least $N$ thick points in its fiber.

