body:
[Thm small_cluster_large_deviation of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Let $d\geqslant 2$. For any $\mathfrak{p} > \mathfrak{p}_c$, the limit
		\begin{equation}
			\frac{1}{n^{d-1}} \ln{\mathbb{P}(n^d\leqslant |\mathscr{C}(0)|<\infty)}
		\end{equation}
		exists and it is a finite strictly negative real number. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm 38 (Exact constant) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $\sigma, \alpha > 0$. Every $X \in \SE(\sigma^2,\alpha)$ satisfies
\begin{align*}
    X \lecx \left(\sigma \vee \alpha\right)\Lap,
\end{align*}
and no smaller multiple of $\Lap$ dominates every member: $c^{\SE}(\sigma, \alpha) = \sigma \vee \alpha$. An extremal pair for that multiple exists exactly when $\alpha \le \sigma$, and $X \sim \mathrm{Unif}(\{-\sigma,\sigma\})$ with $f(x) = |x|$ is one. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:block-reduction-local-time of arXiv:2605.16086, 'Loop pruning and downward deviations for maximum local time of discrete-time simple random'] We have
\begin{align}
\begin{aligned}
&\big\{\xi^*(S'[0,u_n])>\Lambda_n,\,
\sup_{x\in\mathbb{Z}^d}\#\mathcal{J}_x\le M,\,N^{-1}(u_n+1)-1\le n+n^a\big\}\\
\subset&\Big\{\exists\,0\le k\le n+n^a,\,
\ell_{S_k}\big(\mathsf{Prune}(S[k,I_{i_k}^+],E)\big)
> \tfrac{\beta\alpha}{M}\log n\Big\}.    
\end{aligned}
\end{align}

[Thm thm3.6 of arXiv:2609.03751, 'Sparse bounds for maximal rough singular integrals'] {MR4245601}}]
Let \([K]=\{K_s:s\in\mathbb Z\}\) be a family of kernels satisfying
(equation equ3.1 of the paper) and (equation equ3.3 of the paper). Suppose that
\(1\leq p_1,p_2<\infty\) and
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
    C_L[K](p_1,p_2)
    :=\sup_{\mathcal Q,t_1,t_2}
    \Bigg\{
    \sup_{\substack{
        \|b\|_{\dot{\mathcal X}_{p_1}(\mathcal Q)}=1\\
        \|f\|_{\mathcal Y_{p_2}(\mathcal Q)}=1}}
      \bigl|
        \mathcal Q[K]_{t_1}^{t_2}(b,f)
      \bigr|
    +
    \sup_{\substack{
        \|f\|_{\mathcal Y_\infty(\mathcal Q)}=1\\
        \|b\|_{\dot{\mathcal X}_{p_2}(\mathcal Q)}=1}}
      \bigl|
        \mathcal Q[K]_{t_1}^{t_2}(f,b)
      \bigr|
    \Bigg\}
    <\infty,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where the outer supremum is taken over all stopping collections
\(\mathcal Q\) and all bounded measurable integer-valued truncation
functions \(t_1,t_2\). Then
\begin{equation}
    \|T_\star[K]\|_{(p_1,p_2)\text{-}\mathrm{sparse}}
    \lesssim
    \|[K]\|_{r,\star}+C_L[K](p_1,p_2).
\end{equation}
The implicit constant in (equation equ3.7 of the paper) is independent of
\(p_1\) and \(p_2\). In our application \(r=2\) is fixed. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2606.30080, 'Ergodicity of reflected stochastic reaction-diffusion equations driven by space-time white'] Assume that (S1)--(S3) and (H3) hold. Let $p>2$. Define
  \begin{align*}
    h_{+}(u):=
  \begin{cases}
    C_{b,\theta}, & u\geq 0,\\
    -\gamma u + \sup_{u\leq v\leq 0}\big(b(v) - b(0) + C_{b,\theta}\big), & u\leq 0,
  \end{cases}
  \end{align*}
where $\gamma$ satisfies \eqref{260621.1621} with $p$ replaced by $p\nu$. Let $v_{+}$ be the unique solution to \eqref{260603.1828} with $\tilde{b}=h_{+}$. If
\begin{align}
  m > \left\{\frac{\sqrt{4p}}{\pi}\left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\pi}}\right)^{\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{2}} \left(\Gamma\Big(\frac{p-2}{6p}\Big)\right)^{\frac{3}{2}} \times 2G_{\sigma}\right\}^{\frac{4p}{p-2}},
\end{align}
then
\begin{align}
  \sup_{t\geq 0}\mathbb{E}\Big[\sup_{x\in [0,1]} |v_{+}(t,x)|^p\Big] <\infty.
\end{align}

