body:
[Theorem thm5.1' of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] The reflected BSDE (equation eq7' of the paper) has a unique solution $(\{Y^i,Z^i\}_{1\leq i\leq N},K^{(N)})$ with $K^{(N)}\in \mathcal{A}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$, $Y^i\in \mathcal{S}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$ and $Z^i\in \mathcal{H}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)};\mathbb{R}^N)$ for $i=1,\cdots,N$. Moreover, there exists a constant $C$ independent of $N$, such that
\begin{align*}
    \mathsf{E}\left[|K^{(N)}_T|^2\right]\leq C.
\end{align*}

[Definition of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] A oriented embedded surface \(S\subset M\) is \emph{relatively carried by} \(\tau\) if
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(S \setminus \mathrm{int}(T_{\tau})\) is carried by the branched surface \(\tau^{(2)}\) in \(M\setminus \mathrm{int}(T_{\tau})\), and
\item each component of \(S\cap T_{\tau}\) is either a meridional disk or an annulus.
\end{enumerate}

[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.15843, 'Long-time behaviour of DLRA for SDEs'] Suppose Assumptions~(H1)--(H5) hold, and let $(U_t,Y_t)_{t\ge0}$ be the solution of Eqn.~\eqref{eq:DO} with initial condition $U_0 \in V_r(\bb R^d)$ and $Y_0 \in L^2(\Omega,\bb R^r)$. Assume further that there exists $\sigma_{Y_0} > 0$ such that $\bb E[Y_0 Y_0^\top] \succeq \sigma_{Y_0} I_r$.
For any $Q\in O(r)$, define $\al R_Q(u,y) := (Qu, Qy)$. Then, for any $t>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \scr L_{(U_t^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)},Y_t^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)})}=\scr L_{(QU_t^{(U_0,Y_0)},QY_t^{(U_0,Y_0)})},
\end{equation}
where $(U_0^{(U_0,Y_0)},Y_0^{(U_0,Y_0)})=(U_0,Y_0)$ and $(U_0^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)},Y_0^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)})=(QU_0,QY_0)$.

[Lemma lem: Bounds for M of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] Let $\beta$ be large enough. Then, the single-site marginal of $\mu_A$, which was defined in (equation def: single-site marg, diagonal elements of the paper), is bounded as follows
\begin{equation}
    \pi_A(A^c)\leq C_1 e^{-(d+1)\beta u}~~\text{and}~~\pi_A(A)\leq 1
\end{equation}
where $C_1$ is the positive constant given in Proposition (prop: Bounds A-loc. states of the paper). Moreover, the entries of the matrix $M$, introduced in (equation eq: Matrix M of the paper), can be upper bounded in the following way
\begin{gather}
    \nonumber M(1,1)\leq C_3 e^{-\beta u+t}+1,~~M(1,0)\leq C_3 e^{-(d+1)\beta u+t}\\
    M(0,1)\leq  e^{t}~~\text{and}~~M(0,0)\leq C_3 e^{-\beta((d+1)u-U)+t}+C_1 e^{-(d-1)\beta u+t}.
\end{gather}
The positive constant $C_3$ was introduced in Lemma (lem: Key Lemma of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 45 (Well-definedness and regularity of the Stein witness) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:core-target} and either kernel assumption,
\(\mathcal H^d\) is separable, the map
\(x\mapsto\xi_\pi(x)\) is strongly measurable, and
\begin{equation}
    \|\xi_\pi(x)\|_{\mathcal H^d}\le C(1+\|x\|).
\end{equation}
Consequently, \(S_\pi(\rho)\) is well defined for every
\(\rho\in\mathcal P_1(\mathbb R^d)\), and
\[
    S_\pi(\pi)=0.
\]
Additionally, under Assumption~\ref{ass:ksd-kernel}, one also has
\begin{equation}
    \|\xi_\pi(x)-\xi_\pi(y)\|_{\mathcal H^d}
    \le C(1+\|y\|)\|x-y\|.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2604.00742, 'Delayed Logistic equation as a limit\\ of long memory Markov chains'] For each $p \geq 1$ and $N \in \N$, there exists a constant $K_{N} \in (1, 1+1/N)$ such that 
	\begin{equation*}
		\E\left[\bigg(\sup_{t \in [0,T]} Z^{N}(t)\bigg)^p\right] \;\leq\; (2\mu)^p \exp\left\{pK_{N}^{p-1}T\right\}.
	\end{equation*}
	In particular,

\begin{equation*}
	\sup_N \sup_{t \in [0,T]}\widetilde{\mathfrak{m}}_p^N(t) \;<\; \infty\,,
\end{equation*}
where $\widetilde{\mathfrak{m}}_p^N(t):=\E[(Z^N(t))^p]$.

