body:
[Lemma lem:sparse-short of arXiv:2608.05123, 'A central limit theorem for the random assignment problem'] For \(1\le K\le n/2\),
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E_{\mathbb P_n^{\mathrm{ref}}}\sum_i
 \frac{\1_{\{1\le N_i\le K\}}}{N_i}\le C\frac Kn,
 \qquad
 \mathbb E_{\mathbb P_n^{\mathrm{ref}}}\sum_i\frac1{N_i^2}
 \le C\frac{\log n}{n}.
\end{equation}
Consequently
\begin{equation}
 \sum_i\frac1{N_i}\longrightarrow\zeta(2)
 \quad\hbox{in }L^1(\mathbb P_n^{\mathrm{ref}}).
\end{equation}

[Lem lem-hm-linear of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] For each $x\in \mathcal V\mathcal G$, the harmonic measure $\operatorname{hm}_{\mathcal A}^x$ is a probability measure on $\mathcal A$. 
Moreover, for each $\phi : \mathcal A \to\mathbbm R$, the energy-minimizing discrete harmonic function $h^\phi$ satisfies
\begin{equation}   
h^\phi(x)= \sum_{y\in \mathcal A} \phi(y) \operatorname{hm}_{\mathcal A}^x(y) .
\end{equation}

