[Lemma 15 (Block-pairing principle) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Let $k_i=[k_{i,n}]\in\cK_{s_i}$, $1\le i\le m$, and
$\ell_j=[\ell_{j,n}]\in\cK_{t_j}$, $1\le j\le \ell$, with
$\sum_i s_i=\sum_jt_j=q$.  Then
\begin{align}
 &\Ulim q!\ip{\Sym\bigotimes_i k_{i,n}}
                     {\Sym\bigotimes_j\ell_{j,n}}
 \notag\\
 &\qquad=
 \1_{\{m=\ell\}}
 \sum_{\substack{\pi\in\mathfrak S_m\\s_i=t_{\pi(i)}}}
 \prod_{i=1}^m
 \ip{k_i}{\ell_{\pi(i)}}_{\cK_{s_i}}.

\end{align}
Here
\begin{equation}
 \ip{k_i}{\ell_j}_{\cK_s}
 =s!\,\Ulim\ip{k_{i,n}}{\ell_{j,n}},

\end{equation}
so the full multiplicity $\prod_i s_i!$ of the matched internal legs is
already contained in the right-hand side.

[Lemma lem:third-psa of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] Consider the map $ \Phi $ as in (equation e:def-phi of the paper) with $ L [u] = u \cdot \nabla $.
For any $ 1 < \alpha  < \mathbf{a}/2 $, we can estimate uniformly
over $ \kappa \in (0, 1] $:
\begin{equ}
\mathbb{E} \bigl\| \mathcal{L}_{1}  \bigl[  \Pi^{(1)}
\Phi[X,\Phi[X,\Phi[X, Y]]]_{t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M)} \bigr] \bigr\|^{2}\lesssim (t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M))^{5} \kappa^{-2} \| \varrho_{0}
\|_{H^{- \alpha}}^{2} (\| u_{0} \|^{4}_{\mathcal{C}^{\alpha}}+1)\;.
\end{equ}

