{"artifact_digest":"sha256:1a2b689039079cd7a3e82445185a8efea6d31aa93a08f1a395cddde471b35e56","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/1a/1a2b689039079cd7a3e82445185a8efea6d31aa93a08f1a395cddde471b35e56.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:851c2716eb67a70c69c90b293ee31ed585711362db170224489def809d96c48d","bundle_entry_key":"2606-27545-lemma-2-ibp","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_059","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_059.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-27545-lemma-2-ibp","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Fix $v\in V$. Since $D_v^-g(\sigmabf)=0$ whenever $v\notin \sigmabf$ and $D_v^+g(\sigmabf)=0$ whenever $v\in \sigmabf$ we have
		\begin{align*}
			&\E_\mu\left[f(\sigmabf)\Bigl(r_v(\sigmabf)D_v^+g(\sigmabf)+D_v^-g(\sigmabf)\Bigr)\right] \\
			&=
			\sum_{\substack{\sigmabf\in\mathcal X\\ v\notin \sigmabf}}
			\mu(\sigmabf)f(\sigmabf)r_v(\sigmabf)\bigl(g(\sigmabf\cup\{v\})-g(\sigmabf)\bigr)
			+
			\sum_{\substack{\sigmabf\in\mathcal X\\ v\in \sigmabf}}
			\mu(\sigmabf)f(\sigmabf)\bigl(g(\sigmabf\setminus\{v\})-g(\sigmabf)\bigr)
		\end{align*}
		In the second sum, set $\taubf=\sigmabf\backslash\{v\}$. 
		Since
		\(
