[Lemma lem:ConvexCentreOfMass of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $C, C_0 > 0$ be constants. Then there exists some constant $c > 0$, depending only on $d,m,C$ and $C_0$, such that for all $r \leqslant C_0 \sqrt{n}$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \min_{\eta \in \mathrm{Centre}(C)} \frac{\left\lvertB(r,\eta) \cap \mathrm{Centre}(C)\right\rvert}{\left\lvertB(r,\eta)\right\rvert} \geqslant c 
    \end{equation*}
    for $n$ sufficiently large.

