[Defi app_def_pairwiseStable of arXiv:2411.16464, 'Generating social networks with static and dynamic utility-maximization approaches'] A graph $\mathcal{G}(\mathscr{I} , \alpha, C)$ is pairwise stable, iff
\begin{enumerate}
    \item for all $(i,j)$ such that $\alpha_{i,j}$ is a non-null component of $\alpha$, we have $$\forall k \in \{i,j\}, \quad U_k(\alpha, C) \geq U_k(\alpha, C)\vert_{\alpha_{i,j}=0 } $$
    \item for all $(i,j)$ such that $\alpha_{i,j}$ is null component of $\alpha$, we have $$\forall a \in (0 ,1), \forall k \in \{i,j\}, \quad U_k(\alpha, C) \geq U_k(\alpha, C)\vert_{\alpha_{i,j}=a} $$
\end{enumerate}

