[Lemma l:DiagonalEqPot of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] Assume~$\big({\mssE,\msD(\mssE)}\big)$ satisfies~(equation eq:QPP of the paper). Then, for every~$\epsilon>0$ there exists a symmetric function~$g_\epsilon=g_\epsilon^{a,b}\in \dom{\mssE^{a,b}}$ with the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}[$(a)$]
\item $0\leq g_\epsilon \leq 1$ on~$M^{\scriptscriptstyle\times 2}$;
\item $g^\diag_\epsilon \equiv 1$ $\nu$-a.e.\ on~$M$;
\item $\mssE^{a,b}_1(g_\epsilon)\leq 2^{-1/\epsilon}$.
\end{enumerate}
\begin{proof}
Note that, if~$g_\epsilon$ satisfies~(i:l:DiagonalEqPot:1 of the paper)--(i:l:DiagonalEqPot:3 of the paper), then so does its symmetrization.
Therefore it suffices to show~(i:l:DiagonalEqPot:1 of the paper)--(i:l:DiagonalEqPot:3 of the paper).
By Lemma~(l:Capacity2 of the paper) we have~$\mathrm{cap}_{a,b}(\Delta M)=0$, and the existence of such~$g_\epsilon$ follows from the very definition of capacity. 
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 41 of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Let $\xi$ and $\psi$ be associated with the multi-species model given in~\eqref{e.def H_N}--\eqref{e.def.FN.delta0}.
Let $f:\R_+\times\mcl Q^\sS_2\to\R$ be the Lipschitz viscosity solution of
\begin{align*}
\begin{cases}
    \partial_t f - \int_0^1 \xi(\partial_q f)=0 ,\qquad &\text{on }\R_+\times\mcl Q^\sS_2,
    \\
    f(0,\cdot) = \psi ,\qquad &\text{on }\mcl Q^\sS_2.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
Then, we have 
\begin{align}
    f(t,q)\leq \liminf_{N\to\infty}\bar F_N(t,q),\qquad \forall (t,q)\in\R_+\times \mcl Q^\sS_2.
\end{align}

