body:
[Lemma l.EL of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Take $(\Psi,x,t)$ sampled from $\mathcal{Q}_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma}$. The conditional law of $(x,t)$ given $\Psi$  is 
    \begin{equation}

        \nu_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma,N}(dxdt):=\frac{\exp\left(\gamma \Psi_{\varepsilon}(x,t)
        -\frac{\gamma^2}{2}\mathbb E[(\Psi_{\varepsilon}(x,t))^2]\right)
        }{\mu_{\varepsilon}^{\gamma}(D_T)}dxdt.
    \end{equation}
    And on the other hand, the law of $\Psi$ conditionally on $(x,t)$, is equal to 
    \begin{equation}

        \hat{\Psi} + \gamma \mathrm{cov}(\cdot, \Psi_{\varepsilon}(x,t)),
    \end{equation}
    where $\hat{\Psi}$ has the law of the SHEF on $Ps(D, [0,T])$.

