body:
[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2609.03954, 'Galois representations ramified at one prime via relative deformation theory'] There is a finite set $\cE_p\subset\Z$ such that
\begin{equation}
 H^2(G_{\{p\}},\Qp(m))=0
\end{equation}
for every $m\notin\cE_p$.  Moreover $H^2(G_{\{p\}},\Qp)=0$.

[Corollary cor_Ystochastic of arXiv:2603.29442, 'A compact support property for infinite-dimensional SDEs with Hölder continuous coefficien'] Suppose Assumption~(assumption1 of the paper) holds. 
    Let $i \in \mathbb{Z}$ and suppose that $X = (X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ is a continuous $\ell^1_+$-valued solution to (equation e_sdesystem of the paper). Then for every $i \in \mathbb{Z}$, $t \mapsto Y_t(i)$ is a continuous, non-negative semimartingale with representation
	\begin{equation} 
		Y_t(i) = Y_0(i) + \int_0^t (\langle X_s ,  \mathcal{L}^* h(\cdot - \underline{i})\rangle + \langle f(X_s) ,  h(\cdot - \underline{i})\rangle )ds + \int_0^t \sum_{j \in \mathbb{Z}^d \, :\, j_1 \geq i}\sigma(X_s(j))dB_s(j), \,\, t \geq 0.
	\end{equation}

