[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2604.26898, '\bf Stochastic Scaling Limits and Synchronization \\by Noise in Deep Transformer Models'] There exists a constant $\mathsf c > 0$, depending on $T$ but independent of $L$ and $N$, such that for all $i$:
    \begin{equ}
        \E\left[\sup_{0\le t\le T} |\bar X_t^i|^2\right] = 1 \quad \text{and} \quad \E\left[\sup_{0\le t\le T} |\hat{X}_t^i|^2\right] \le \mathsf c.
    \end{equ}

