body:
[Lemma EHI:l:SbmExitsNotTooFar of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t \geq 0} = (B_{S_t})_{t \geq 0}$ be a subordinate Brownian motion on $\mathbb{R}^d$. Fix $r>0$ and $s \leq r^2/2$. Let $T^{\{s\}} := \inf\{ t>0 : \Delta S(t)>s \}$ be the first time that the subordinator $S$ takes a jump of size greater than $s$. Then for all $x \in B(0, r)$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}_x \left( X_{\tau_{B(0, r)}} \notin B(0, 5 r) \Big| \tau_{B(0, r)} < T^{\{s\}} \right) \leq Ce^{-cr^2/s},
    \end{equation*}
    where $C, c>0$ are constants that depend only on $d$.

