[Lem lem-tauberian' of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $\phi$ be as in~(equation eqn-gen-func-def of the paper).
Assume that for some $c_1 > 0$, $c_2 \in \mathbbm C \setminus  \mathbbm R$, and $\nu \in (0,1)$,  
\begin{equation} 
\phi(e^{i t}) = 1 + i c_1 t +     (c_2 \mathbbm 1_{(t > 0)} + \overline c_2 \mathbbm 1_{(t < 0)} ) |t|^{1+\nu}       + o(t^{1+\nu})  ,\quad \text{as $t \to 0$}. 
\end{equation} 
Then $\operatorname{Im}(c_2)<0$ and setting $a=-\frac{\nu}{\Gamma(1-\nu)}\sec\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft(\tfrac{\pi\nu}{2}\aftergroup\egroup\originalright)\operatorname{Im}(c_2)>0$, 
\begin{equation} 
\mathbbm P[X > R] = a R^{-\nu-1}  +  o(R^{-\nu-1}) ,\quad \text{as $R\to\infty$}. 
\end{equation}

