[Proposition 87 (Uniform fixed-point estimate) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $\mathfrak K$ satisfy Definition~\ref{def:localized-smallness-class}
with bound $A$.
For every $R\ge1$ there is a nondecreasing polynomial $P_R$ such that, for
$(\Xi,y),(\widetilde\Xi,\widetilde y)\in\mathfrak K$ and
$\|Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T},\|\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}\le R$,
\begin{align}
 \|\mathscr P_{\Xi,y}Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}
 &\le C(A+A^2)+\mu_T(\Xi,y)P_R,
 \\
 \|\mathscr P_{\Xi,y}Z-
 \mathscr P_{\Xi,y}\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}
 &\le \mu_T(\Xi,y)P_R
 \|Z-\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}.

\end{align}
For simultaneous perturbations of $\Xi$ and the Cauchy data,
\begin{align}
 &\|\mathscr P_{\Xi,y}Z-
 \mathscr P_{\widetilde\Xi,\widetilde y}\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}
 \notag\\
 &\quad\le \nu_{\mathfrak K}(T)P_R
 \|Z-\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}
 +C_{A,R}\,d_T\big((\Xi,y),(\widetilde\Xi,\widetilde y)\big),

\end{align}
where $d_T$ is defined in \eqref{eq:Xi-distance}.

[Thm two_point_pointwise of arXiv:2508.18807, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation I: High effective dimension}'] If $\alpha<1$ then
 $\mathbb P_{\beta_c}(x \leftrightarrow y) \asymp \|x-y\|^{-d+\alpha}$
for every $x\neq y$ in $\mathbb Z^d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor torus of arXiv:2603.27144, 'On the critical fugacity of the hard-core model on regular bipartite graphs'] For each $C_{0}>0$ there exist $C_{1},C_{2}>0$
such that for each dimension $d\ge2$ and even $L\ge2$: The event
\begin{equation}
B\coloneqq\left\{ \min\{|\sigma_{\mathcal{E}}|,|\sigma_{\mathcal{O}}|\}>\frac{L^{d+1}}{d^{C_{0}}}\right\} \cup\left\{ \left||\sigma|-\frac{L^{d}}{2}\frac{\lambda}{1+\lambda}\right|>\frac{L^{d+1}}{d^{C_{0}}}\right\} 
\end{equation}
satisfies
\begin{align}
\mu^{\mathbb{Z}_{L}^{d}}\left(B\right)\le\frac{\zeta^{\mathbb{Z}_{L}^{d}}\left(B\right)}{(1+\lambda)^{L^{d}/2}} & \le(1+\lambda)^{-\frac{L^{d}}{d^{C_{2}}}}
\end{align}
whenever $\lambda>C_{1}\frac{\log d}{d}$.
\begin{comment}
Here are a previous version of the Corollary for torus graphs. This
version may have some advantages over what we ended up with.

\begin{cor}
There are $C,c>0$, such that for each integers
$L,d\ge2$ and $\lambda,r>0$, the following holds. ThenCan also take $d=1$
\[
\mu^{\mathbb{Z}_{L}^{d}}(\mathcal{M}>r)\le\frac{\zeta^{\mathbb{Z}_{L}^{d}}(\mathcal{M}>r)}{(1+\lambda)^{L^{d}/2}}\le(1+\lambda)^{-\frac{c}{d}r},
\]
whenever $\tilde{\lambda}>\max\left\{ \frac{C\log\left(CLd\cdot\frac{L^{d}}{r}\right)}{d},\frac{Cd}{r}\right\} $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm Informal statement of \autoref{lem:conv_muN_detailed} of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] Let $\mu^N(t)$ denote the empirical measure of the particle system and let $\mu(t)$ be the unique solution of the McKean--Vlasov equation. Then, as $N\to\infty$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{t\in[0,T]} \mathbb{E}\big[ {\mathcal W}_1(\mu^N(t),\mu(t)) \big]
\longrightarrow 0.
\end{align}
In particular, the particle system is chaotic with limit law $\mu(t)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop: ModuleRephrasingDiscriminantCondition of arXiv:2603.26932, 'On the satisfaction frequency of spectral characterization conditions'] It holds that $p \nmid \Delta_{\bM}$ if and only if it holds for all monic $\beta(x) \in \bbZ[x]$ with irreducible reduction in $\bbF_p[x]$ that, as $\bbZ[x]$-modules,  
        \begin{equation}
            \frac{\coker\bigl(\bM - x\bI)_{p,\beta}}{p \coker\bigl(\bM - x\bI)_{p,\beta}} \cong 0 
            \qquad \textnormal{ or }\qquad 
            \frac{\coker\bigl(\bM - x\bI)_{p,\beta}}{p \coker\bigl(\bM - x\bI)_{p,\beta}}  \cong \frac{\bbF_p[x]}{\beta(x)\bbF_p[x] }. 
        \end{equation}

