[Lemma appendix:numerical:iterates of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let $(a_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of non-negative reals and suppose for any $n\geq N$ it satisfies
    \begin{equation*}
    a_n-a_{n-1}\leq -\frac{a_n^\alpha}{C}\,,
    \end{equation*}
    for some positive constant $C>0$ and some $\alpha>1$. Then for any $n\geq N$ we have
    \begin{equation*}
    a_n\leq (n-N)^{-\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}\,\biggl(\frac{\alpha-1}{C}+\frac1{(n-N)a_N^{\alpha-1}}\biggr)^{-\frac{1}{\alpha-1}}\,.
    \end{equation*}

