[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2606.06231, 'Sensitivity of SDE Solutions to Perturbations of the Diffusion and Drift'] Under Assumptions \ref{assump:main_assumptions_1}, \ref{assump:h_assump1} and \ref{assump:main_assumptions_2},  suppose also that for all $t\in[0,T]$, $h_t$ satisfies a $(\sigma_{h_t},b)$-Bernstein MGF bound with respect to $\mu_{X}^*$  with $\sigma_{h_t}\in L^2([0,T],dt)$.  Then
\begin{align} 
&\log \mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(\pm c \int_0^{T} ( h(t,X_t)-E_{\mu_X^*}[h_t]) dt\right)\right]\leq    \frac{ c^2 C_*}{2(1-c C_*b)} \int_0^T \! \sigma_{h_t}^2dt\,\,\text{ for all }c\in(0,1/(C_*b)).
\end{align}

[Lemma lem:bracket_extraction of arXiv:2609.01697, 'Unique ergodicity of projective cocycles over the 2D stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] In the same setting of Lemma~(lem:vanishing_implies_orthogonality of the paper), and with $\eta_s$ given by (equation eq:eta_def of the paper), let $A$ be bracket-regular and suppose that $ \langle \eta_s, {A}^\sharp\pi_s \rangle = 0$ for all $s \in (0,T]$, $\mathbb{P}$-almost surely. Then we have:
  \begin{equation}
    \langle \eta_s, \vf{[G_{w_s}, A]}\pi_s\rangle = 0 , \qquad \langle \eta_s, {[H^k, A]}^\sharp\pi_s \rangle = 0 \qquad \text{for all } s \in (0,T] , \quad  \mathbb{P}\text{-almost surely.}
  \end{equation}

