[Maintheorem thm:conc-brw of arXiv:2411.08018, 'Last passage percolation in hierarchical environments'] As $n\to\infty$,
    \begin{align}
        \Var(L_{n}^{\mathrm{BRW}}) = \Theta(n^2).
    \end{align}
    Moreover, there exist $c, t_0>0$ such that for all $t\ge t_0$ and all $n$, 
    \begin{align}
        e^{- t^2}\le
        \mathbb{P}\left(\left|\frac{L_{n}^{\mathrm{BRW}} - \mathbb{E}[L_{n}^{\mathrm{BRW}}]}{n}\right| > t\right)
        \le e^{-c t^2},
    \end{align}
    and hence the fluctuations of $L_{n}^{\mathrm{BRW}}$ around its mean are of order $\Theta(n)$.
    Note that this combined with (equation eq:brw-mean of the paper) implies that $L_{n}^{\mathrm{BRW}}$ is concentrated around its mean. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem TH-Lp-est of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] Let   $L = (L_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a L\'evy  process with L\'evy triplet $(0,0,\nu)$ satisfying Hypotheses  (hyp-nondeg2 of the paper) with $\alpha \ge 1$. Let us consider
 \begin{align}
 \lambda v -  {
\mathscr A} v  - b \cdot Dv = f,\;\; \lambda>0,
 \end{align}
 with $b \in C_{\mathrm{b}}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^d,\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $f \in L^p(\mathbb R^d)\cap C_{\mathrm{b}}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, for some $p>1$. Let $v \in C^2_\mathrm{b}(\mathbb R^d)$ be the classical bounded solution to (equation eqn-resolvent0 of the paper).  
  Then, the following assertions hold.      
\\
1) If  $\alpha \in(1,2)$ there exists  $c = c(d,\alpha,\lambda,p,\Vert b\Vert_{\infty}) $ such that 

the solution $v$ satisfies
 \begin{equation}
 \Vert v\Vert_{H^{\alpha,p}}
  \le c \Vert f\Vert_{L^p}. 
 \end{equation}
2) If $\alpha =1$, $\beta \in (0,1)$  there exists  $c = c(d,\alpha,\lambda,p,\Vert b\Vert_{\beta}) $
 such that 
\begin{equation}
 \Vert v\Vert_{H^{1,p}}
  \le c \Vert f\Vert_{L^p}.   
