{"artifact_digest":"sha256:b9dd4acddc9f48b456254573a02f4e80ccf409f9c92058ab51e9c577784a7c78","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/b9/b9dd4acddc9f48b456254573a02f4e80ccf409f9c92058ab51e9c577784a7c78.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:e8b26850f0d779d10f34d97ec2dbeb9d43a492a8bf2de8a79bd1802224e7617f","bundle_entry_key":"2609-02610-lemma-10-wronskian-amplification","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_152","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_152.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-02610-lemma-10-wronskian-amplification","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: For nonnegative integers $r_0,\ldots,r_{N-1}$ and $z\in U$, set
\begin{equation}
    D(r_0,\ldots,r_{N-1};z)
    :=
    \det\bigl(f_j^{(r_k)}(z)\bigr)_{0\leq k,j<N}.
\end{equation}
Thus
\begin{equation}
    \cW(z)=D(0,1,\ldots,N-1;z).
\end{equation}
Repeated differentiation of \eqref{eq:W-as-D}, together with the
multilinearity of the determinant in its rows, gives
\begin{align}
    \cW^{(m)}(z)
    =
    \sum_{\substack{\alpha\in\N_0^N\\ |\alpha|=m}}
    \binom{m}{\alpha}
    D\bigl(
        \alpha_0,
        1+\alpha_1,
        \ldots,
        N-1+\alpha_{N-1};
        z
    \bigr), \quad \text{ for all } z \in U,
\end{align}
where
