[Proposition 15 (Malliavin derivative estimates) of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] Let $X$ be the unique strong solution to \eqref{eq: averaged dynamics 1}. Then $X \in \bbL^{1, 2}_T$ and there exists $C \in (0, \infty)$ depending only on $(A, \beta, T, C_{\textup{Lip}})$ such that for arbitrary $i=1,\dots,N$, 
\begin{equation*}
     \bbE\big[|D_u^i X_t|^2\big]+\int_0^t \int_0^t \bbE\big[|D_r^i X_s|^2\big]\,dr\,ds\leq C, \quad 0 \leq u \leq t \leq T.
\end{equation*}
Moreover with $Q$ as in \eqref{eq: averaged dynamics 1}, we have
\begin{equation*}
    \bbE\big[\|D^i_s Q_t\|^2_{\op}\big] \leq CN^{-1}, \quad i = 1, \ldots, N, \quad 0 \leq s \leq t \leq T.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 2 (Weak stochastic monotonicity for the Ising energy field) of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] Let $J\leq \tilde{J}$ be (edge-dependent) coupling constants, where the inequality holds pointwise for every edge. Then, for any parameter $p \le 1-\exp(-2J)$,
	\begin{align}
		\en_{J} \cap \ber{p} \domi \en_{\tilde{J}} \cap \ber{p}.
	\end{align}
	Moreover, one cannot take $p>1-\exp(-2J)$ in general. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

