[Lemma permutationBoundary of arXiv:2605.18744, 'Lattice random-field Widom--Rowlinson models'] There is $C>0$ such that, for every $m$-connected $\gamma\subset \mathbb{Z}^d$ and all $x_1,\ldots,x_k\in \gamma$ pairwise different, there is a permutation $p\colon \{1,\ldots, k\}\rightarrow \{1,\ldots,k\}$ with
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{i=2}^k\|x_{p(i)}-x_{p(i-1)}\|_1\le C| \gamma|.
\end{align*}

