[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] Let $B(R)$ be the open ball of radius $R$ centered at the origin. 
  Let $C^{B(R)}(\theta)$ be the spectral function restricted to the open ball $B(R)$,
  that is,
  \begin{align}

    C^{B(R)}(\theta) := -\inf \left\{ \mathcal{E}^{\alpha}(u,u) - \theta \int_{B(R)}^{ } u^{2} d\mu :
    u \in \mathcal{F}^{B(R)},\ \int_{B(R)}^{ } u^{2} dx = 1\right\},
  \end{align}
  where
  \begin{align}

    \mathcal{F}^{B(R)} := \left\{ u \in \mathcal{F}^{\alpha}: u = 0\ \text{$m$-a.e. on } B(R)^{c} \right\}.
  \end{align}
  Then, we have
\begin{align}
  \lim_{R\to\infty} C^{B(R)}(\theta) = C(\theta). 
\end{align}

