[Lemma lem-prelim-gap-est-very-final-rounds of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    Suppose that $\alpha > 1$, $M \in \mathbb Z_{+}$ and $\delta \in (0, 1]$ such that
    \begin{equation}{}
         1-\delta \leq \frac{\log n}{n} \,.
    \end{equation}
    Define $N_\alpha = \lceil\log_\alpha (\frac{2}{\alpha - 1})\rceil + 1$. Then, given that $(\mathbf X^{(1)}_k,\ldots,\mathbf X^{(n)}_k) \in \overline{\Omega}_n(M,\delta)$ we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb P_n^{\alpha}\left( \mathcal T \leq k+N_\alpha + 1, \mathfrak L(\mathbf X_k) = \{\mathcal W\} \right) \geq 1-\frac{1}{\log n} \,.
    \end{align*}

