[Lemma lem:lpconv of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] There exists $T_0>0$ such that 
	 for all $x\in \mathbb{R}$ and $0\leq t \leq T_0$ it holds that
	\begin{equation*}
		 \exp(-nX^n_t(x)) \rightarrow \mathbbm{1}_{X_t(x) = 0}
	\end{equation*}
in $L^q$ for $q\in[1,\infty)$ as $n \rightarrow \infty$.

