[Lemma l.cdasymptotics of arXiv:2510.07682, 'From tug-of-war to Brownian Boost: \\ explicit ODE solutions for player-funded stochastic-'] When  $\kappa$ is supposed to be at most a universal positive constant,
\begin{equation}
 c(x)  \, = \, 2 + \kappa \cdot  2 \bigg( 1 - \frac{2\big(1+(1-\rho)x^\rho \big)}{(1+x^\rho)^2} \bigg) \, + \, O(\kappa^2)
\end{equation}
 and
\begin{equation}
d(x)  \, =   \, 2 - \kappa \cdot 2 \bigg( 1 - \frac{2}{(1+x^\rho)^2} \Big( (1-\rho)x^\rho + x^{2\rho} \Big) \bigg)  \, + \,  O(\kappa^2) \, .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor RefinedRate of arXiv:2609.03762, '\vspace*{-2cm} Projected Riemannian Gradient Descent for the Bures--Wasserstein Barycenter'] Let $S_0 \in [\alpha' I, \beta' I]$ and let the iterates be generated by unit-step BW-GD projected onto the refined interval, $S_{t+1} := \mathrm{clip}_{\alpha', \beta'}[\mathrm{K}(S_t)]$.
        Then
        \begin{equation}
            f_1(S_t) - f_1(S_\star) \leq \left(1 - \frac{1}{\kappa'^{3/2}}\right)^t \left(f_1(S_0) - f_1(S_\star)\right),
        \end{equation}
        the verbatim analogue of~(Thm:UnifiedConvergence of the paper) in the refined constants, and the iteration count of~(Eq:IterationCount of the paper) improves accordingly to $\kappa'^{3/2} \log(1/\epsilon)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 27 (The anticipation martingale) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] For the survival and hazard of~\eqref{eq:surv-haz} and the hazard clock and martingale factor of~\eqref{eq:clock-mart}, the processes $\clock{\tau}$ and $\Amart{\tau}$ satisfy:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item $\clock{\tau}$ is nondecreasing with $\clock{\tau}_0 = 0$ and $\clock{\tau}_T \in [0,1]$;
\item $\Amart{\tau}$ is a nonnegative $P$-martingale with $\Amart{\tau}_0 = 1$;
\item the conditional survival satisfies $S_T = (1 - \clock{\tau}_T)\,\Amart{\tau}_T$;
\item the incremental relations are $(\clock{\tau}_t - \clock{\tau}_{t-1})/(1 - \clock{\tau}_{t-1}) = H_t$ and $\Amart{\tau}_t/\Amart{\tau}_{t-1} = P(\tau \geq t \mid \cF_t)/P(\tau \geq t \mid \cF_{t-1})$;
\item $P(\tau = t \mid \cF_t) = \Amart{\tau}_t \cdot (\clock{\tau}_t - \clock{\tau}_{t-1})$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

