[Lem Lr-bad-part of arXiv:2609.03751, 'Sparse bounds for maximal rough singular integrals'] Let \(r\geq2\) be an integer.  Then
\[
\begin{aligned}
 &\left\|
   \sum_{j\in\mathbb Z}
   \sum_{Q\in\mathfrak V_{j-s}^{n,\iota}}
   P_{j-s\kappa}
   \bigl[
     \varepsilon_{J(Q)}(T_jb_Q)
     \widetilde\chi_{J(Q)^\iota}
   \bigr]
 \right\|_{L^r(\mathbb R^d)}
 \\
 &\qquad\lesssim_d
 (r!)^{1/r}2^{-2n/r}
 \|\Omega\|_{L^\infty(S^{d-1})}
 \|b\|_{\dot{\mathcal X}_1(\mathcal Q)}
 |Q_0|^{1/r},
\end{aligned}
\]
with a constant uniform in \(s\).

