[Thm solMild of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Assume that either Hypotheses (Hyp1C of the paper) or Hypotheses (Hyp2L of the paper) holds. For every $T>0$ and $x\in E$, (equation eqFO of the paper) has unique $E$-valued càdlàg mild solution $\{X(t,x)\}_{t\in [0,T]}$. Moreover for every $t>0$ and $x,z\in E$ we have
{\small
\begin{align}
&{\left|X(t,x)\right|}_{H}\leq e^{\zeta t}{\left|x\right|}_{H}+\int_0^te^{\zeta (t-s)}\left({\left|F(Z_A(s))\right|}_{H}+2\max\{0,\zeta\}{\left|Z_A(s)\right|}_{H}\right)ds+{\left|Z_A(t)\right|}_{H},\;\; \mathbb{P}{\rm-a.s.}\\
&{\left\|X(t,x)\right\|}_E\leq e^{\zeta t}{\left\|x\right\|}_E+\int_0^te^{\zeta (t-s)}\left({\left\|F(Z_A(s))\right\|}_E+2\max\{0,\zeta\}{\left\|Z_A(s)\right\|}_E\right)ds+{\left\|Z_A(t)\right\|}_E,\;\;\mathbb{P}{\rm-a.s.}	\\
&{\left|X(t,x)-X(t,z)\right|}_{H}\leq  e^{\zeta t}{\left|x-z\right|}_{H},\;\;\mathbb{P}{\rm-a.s.}\\
&{\left\|X(t,x)-X(t,z)\right\|}_E\leq  e^{\zeta t}{\left\|x-z\right\|}_E,\;\;\mathbb{P}{\rm-a.s.},
\end{align}
where $\zeta$ is the constant defined in (equation zeta of the paper).
}

