[Lemma lem:QH-uniform of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] In the present homogeneous additive-noise setting,
\begin{equation}

  Q_{\gamma,N,H}=\frac{\sigma^2}{H}\left(1-\frac1N\right)+R_{Q,H},
  \qquad |R_{Q,H}|\le C_{Q,H}\gamma,
\end{equation}
where $C_{Q,H}$ is independent of $N$ and $\gamma$.

[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] Let~\(G=(V,E)\) be a finite graph, and let~\(\mfr{b}_1,\mfr{b}_2\subset V\) be disjoint. For any~\(p\in (0,1)\) and~\(1\leq q_\mrm{b}\leq q\),
\begin{equation*}
\qfk_{G;p,q}^{\mfr{b}_1,\mfr{b}_2;1,q_\mrm{b}}\geq_\mrm{st}
\qfk_{G;p,q}^{\mfr{b}_1,\mfr{b}_2;q_\mrm{b},q_\mrm{b}}=
\qfk_{G;p,q}^{\mfr{b}_1\cup \mfr{b}_2;q_\mrm{b}}.
\end{equation*}

