[Theorem thm:OSSS of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] Let $\mu$ be a monotonic\footnote{See [gri06] for the definition and properties of monotonic measures. A measure is monotonic if and only if it has the FKG property.} measure on $\{0, 1\}^E$ where $E$ is finite. Let $T$ be a decision tree computing an increasing random variable $f$. Then
  \begin{equation}
      \mathrm{Var}(f) \leqslant \sum\limits_{e \in E} \delta_e(f, T) \mathrm{Cov}(f, \omega(e))
  \end{equation}
  where
  \begin{equation}
    \delta_e(f, T) := \mu(e \text{ is revealed by } T)
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:upperboundLRW of arXiv:2607.10801, 'Relaxation times of non-reversible\\ Markov processes'] The lifted random walk on $\mathbb{Z}_n^d$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \overline t_\mathrm{rel} \ \leq \ 16e\max\Big(\frac{dn^2\gamma}{20},\frac{1+4d}{\gamma}\Big)\qquad\text{and}\qquad t_\mathrm{rel}\ \leq \ \frac{dn^2}{10}+\frac{1+4d}{\gamma} \,.
    \end{equation}
    In particular,
    \begin{equation*}
        \overline{t}_\mathrm{rel} \ \leq \ 16e\max\Big(\frac{dn^2\min(1,\gamma)}{20},\frac{1+4d}{\gamma}\Big)\,.
    \end{equation*}

