{"artifact_digest":"sha256:3beeee275e037ac9cecdeff08647d1256a5756163ca47d5ba6cccaa8b1db654a","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/3b/3beeee275e037ac9cecdeff08647d1256a5756163ca47d5ba6cccaa8b1db654a.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:38c1b7833ff34bd7d630ea5052ab723e03f2e228bec8d06d084de046565cfd25","bundle_entry_key":"2608-10415-theorem-224-theorem-224","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_053","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_053.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2608-10415-theorem-224-theorem-224","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The moments can be indeed computed as follows, using Theorem 8.9:
\begin{eqnarray*}
M_k
&=&\frac{1}{B(a,b)}\int_0^1x^{a+k-1}(1-x)^{b-1}dx\\
&=&\frac{B(a+k,b)}{B(a,b)}\\
&=&\frac{\Gamma(a+k)\Gamma(b)}{\Gamma(a+b+k)}\cdot\frac{\Gamma(a+b)}{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)}\\
&=&\frac{\Gamma(a+k)}{\Gamma(a)}\cdot\frac{\Gamma(a+b)}{\Gamma(a+b+k)}\\
&=&\frac{a(a+1)\ldots(a+k-1)}{(a+b)(a+b+1)\ldots(a+b+k-1)}
\end{eqnarray*}

In particular, we have the formula of $E$. Getting now to the variance, this is:
\begin{eqnarray*}
V
&=&M_2-M_1^2\\
&=&\frac{a(a+1)}{(a+b)(a+b+1)}-\left(\frac{a}{a+b}\right)^2\\
&=&\frac{a}{(a+b)^2(a+b+1)}[(a+1)(a+b)-a(a+b+1)]\\
&=&\frac{ab}{(a+b)^2(a+b+1)}
\end{eqnarray*}

