[Cor 12 of arXiv:2608.21255, 'Laws of the iterated logarithm for random Dirichlet series with general weights'] Assume that $\eta$ has a standard normal distribution. Then
\begin{equation}
        \limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{\log|\hat{Y}_n|}{\log\log n}=\frac{1}{2}\quad \text{{\rm a.s.}}
    \end{equation}
    and
    \begin{equation}
        \liminf_{n\to\infty}\frac{\log|\hat{Y}_n|}{\log n}=-1\quad \text{{\rm a.s.}}
    \end{equation}

