[Definition 2 of arXiv:2608.21607, '\bf \mbox{Subzero matrix completion for sparse data analysis:} large-scale learning of lat'] Let $\{\vec{\alpha}_i\}_{i=1}^m$ and $\{\vec{\beta}_j\}_{j=1}^n$ be sets of vectors in $\mathbb{R}^d$. We define the thresholded similarity matrix for these vectors, with threshold $\tau\!\in\!(-1,1)$, as the $m\times n$ nonnegative matrix~$\mat{S}$ with elements
\begin{equation}
S_{ij}(\tau) = \max\big(0,\vec{\alpha}_i\!\cdot\!\vec{\beta}_j - \tau\|\vec{\alpha}_i\|\|\vec{\beta}_j\|\big).

\end{equation}

