[Lemma lem:martingale of arXiv:2605.17725, 'Limit theorems for random walks with spatio-temporal drift'] a. The process
$(M_n)_{n\ge 0}$, with $M_0:=0$ and
$$
M_n:=\Phi(n)^{-1}S_n \quad \text{for $n\ge 1$,}
$$
is a martingale.

b. Assume that either $\lambda_{\min}(A)>1/2$ or $\lambda_{\max}(A)<1/2$ or $\lambda_{\min}=\lambda_{\max}=1/2$. Let $$\Delta_k:=M_k-M_{k-1}.$$ Then, a.s.\begin{align}
    \mathbb{E}[\Delta_{k} \Delta_{k}^\top \mid\mathcal{F}_{k-1}]= \Phi(k)^{-1} (\Sigma+R_{k-1}) \big(\Phi(k)^{-1}\big)^{\top}\quad\text{for all $k\ge 1$},
\end{align}
where $R_k$ is $\mathcal{F}_k$-measurable and $\|R_k\|$ converges to 0 in $L^1$.

