[Theorem thm:a0 in int of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] If $a_0\in \interior(P)$ then $U_-$ is non empty. Therefore, there exists $U\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ such that
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\mathbb{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}_0;U\right\}<\mathbb{E}\mathbb{S}\left\{\mathcal{E};U\right\}.
  \end{equation}

