body:
[Lem Lemma 2.2 of arXiv:2609.03411, 'Adjacent vertex distinguishing total chromatic number of graph products'] {\em Fix $n>2$. Let $M = [m_{i,j}]$ be a Latin square where $m_{i,j} \equiv (i + j)-1 \pmod{n}, 1 \leq m_{i,j} \leq n$, for $1 \leq i, j \leq n$. If $k,l<n$, and $M'$ is the submatrix of $M$ consisting of the first $k$ rows and the first $l$ columns of $M$, then 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item no two rows of $M'$ contain the same set of entries,
        \item no two columns of $M'$ contain the same set of entries.
    \end{enumerate}
    }

