[Lemma lem-A4 of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] There exists  a $\mathbb{P}$-full set  $\Omega^{(v)} \subset \Omega^{(iv)}$ and an infinite set $\Upsilon_{2} \subset \Upsilon_{1}$  such that
for every $\omega \in \Omega^{(v)}$ and every $T>0$,
\begin{align}
&\lim_{ \ensuremath{\varepsilon} \in \Upsilon_{2} } \sup_{t \in [0,T]}  \Big\vert \int_0^t\int_{\mathbb R^d}u_0(y)\theta(\phi^{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}_s(y)) \operatorname{div}\,b^{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}(\phi^{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}_s(y))J_s^{\ensuremath{\varepsilon}}(y)\,dyds\\
& \hspace{1truecm} -\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb R^d}u_0(y)\theta(\phi_s(y)) \operatorname{div}\,b(\phi_s(y))J_s(y)\,dyds
\Big\vert =0.
\end{align}

