[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2608.26816, '\textbf{On the existence of maximal foliations in general relativity}'] Let $g_{ij}$, $h_{ij}, H$ be the induced metric, the  second fundamental form and the mean curvature of deformation (\ref{411}) respectively.  Then  
\begin{equation} 
\begin{split}
& \frac{\partial g_{ij}}{\partial t} =2Hh_{ij},\\
& \frac{\partial h_{ij}}{\partial t} =\nabla_{i}\nabla_j H+H(h^2_{ij}-\bar{R}_{i0j0}),\\
&(\frac{\partial }{\partial t}-\triangle)H =-H|h|^{2}.
\end{split}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

