[Lemma lem:cornerdomination of arXiv:2608.11378, 'On the most likely geodesic in last passage percolation'] Let $C_k$ be the weight along the straight path $(0, n - k) \to (0, n)$ and let $L^{\mathord{\text{
\tikz[baseline=0.1ex, line join=round] {
\draw[line width=0.06em] (0,0) -- (1ex,0) -- (0,1ex) -- cycle;
}
}}}_k = L^{\mathord{\text{
\tikz[baseline=0.1ex, line join=round] {
\draw[line width=0.06em] (0,0) -- (1ex,0) -- (0,1ex) -- cycle;
}
}}}(1, n - k - 1; n)$ be a point-to-line passage time from a shifted starting point. For each $\epsilon > 0$ there is a constant $c > 0$ such that for $n$ large enough,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}(C_k \ge k \mu \ge L^{\mathord{\text{
\tikz[baseline=0.1ex, line join=round] {
\draw[line width=0.06em] (0,0) -- (1ex,0) -- (0,1ex) -- cycle;
}
}}}_k \text{ for all } 1 \le k \le n - 1) \ge e^{-n I(\mu) - c n^{1/3 + \epsilon}}.
    \end{equation}

