[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $K \in \mathcal{C}^n$ and $L \in \mathcal{B}(\R^n)$. Define $M(K,L) = \sup_{x\in K, y\in L} \langle x, y \rangle$. Then,
    \begin{equation}
    \vol(K)^{\frac{1}{2}} \vol(L)^{\frac{1}{2}} \leq \vol(\B) M(K,L)^{\frac{n}{2}}.
    \end{equation}
    If $0<\vol(L)<\infty$, then there is equality if and only if one has, up to removal of null sets, that $K$ is a centered ellipsoid and $L=M(K,L)K^\circ$.

