[Definition 10 (Fast coadjoint leafwise averaged flux) of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] We define the \emph{fast coadjoint leafwise averaged flux} as applying the leafwise averaging operator \emph{(\ref{Eq:AveragingLeafwiseCoAdjointsuN})} to the instantaneous flux \emph{(\ref{Def:FluxZeitlin:InstantaneousFluxEnergyEnstrophy:Eq})}, i.e.
\begin{equation}
\overline{\Pi}_{\mathcal{E}}(K; z)=\int_{\mathcal{O}^*(z)}\Pi_{\mathcal{E}}(K; \Omega)dm_z(\Omega) \ , \ \overline{\Pi}_{\mathcal{Z}}(K; z)=\int_{\mathcal{O}^*(z)}\Pi_{\mathcal{Z}}(K; \Omega)dm_z(\Omega) \ .
