[Corr thisgivesthat of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Given a sequence of graphs $G_n$ and a fixed graph $H$ above, set $Q_n$ by (equation eq:333 of the paper) and set $\widetilde{G}_n:=G_n/\lVert G_n\rVert_1$. Let $W^{(2)}_{\widetilde{G}_n}\in L^1([0,1]^2)$ be defined as in (equation eq:funext of the paper). Suppose the following assumptions are satisfied: 
\begin{align}
    \limsup_{n\to\infty}\,\lVert W^{(2)}_{\widetilde{G}_n}\rVert_{q\Delta} < \infty \qquad \mbox{and} \qquad \lVert W^{(2)}_{\widetilde{G}_n}-W_\infty^{(2)}\rVert_{\square^*}\overset{n\to\infty}{\to} 0, 
\end{align}
for some $q>1$ and $W_\infty^{(2)}\in L^1([0,1]^2)$. Then for any ${\boldsymbol \alpha}\in \mathbb{R}^c$, the  statistic
${\boldsymbol\alpha}^\top {\boldsymbol N}(H,G_n,{\bf{X}})$ satisfies an LDP with speed $n$ and the good rate function from (equation eq:i2 of the paper), with $G_{W_{\infty,\mathbf{1}_r}}$ replaced by $G^{(2)}_{{\infty},r}$, $1\le r\le c$ defined as
\begin{align}
    G^{(2)}_{{\infty},r}(\boldsymbol{f}):=\int_{[0,1]^v}\prod_{\{i,j\}\in E(H)} W^{(2)}_{\infty}(x_{i},x_{j})\prod_{a=1}^v f_r(x_a)\, d x_a.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

