[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] $F$ is $r$-semicontinuous if and only if the common order and uo closure of $\Ba_{F}$ is contained in $r\Ba_{F}$. Moreover, the following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is topologically semicontinuous;
\item[(ii)] The norm topology is semicontinuous;
\item[(iii)] The common order and uo closure of $\Ba_{F}$ is norm bounded;
\item[(iv)] Order closure preserves norm bounded sets;
\item[(iv')] Uo closure preserves norm bounded sets.

[Proposition prop:effective-avr of arXiv:2608.30779, 'Some uniform estimates for K\"ahler--Ricci Shrinkers'] Let \((X^n,\omega,J,f,p)\) be a  K\"ahler--Ricci
shrinker with 
\(p\in\operatorname*{argmin}_X f\). For any $\epsilon\in (0,1)$, there are \(r_0=r_0(n)\) and
\(C=C(n,\epsilon)\) such that, for
\(r\geq r_0\),
\begin{equation}
 0\leq \frac{\mathsf V(r^2/2)}{r^{2n}}
       -\omega_{2n}\operatorname{AVR}(X,g)
 \leq C r^{-1+\epsilon}.
\end{equation}

