[Lemma mgf-above-n-asymptotic of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\delta$ be a given positive real number, $n \geq 2$ be a positive integer and denote $\lambda = n-n^{1-\alpha}$ where $\alpha \in (0,+\infty)$. We have
    \begin{align}
        \frac{1}{n^\alpha \br{1-\br{\frac{\lambda}{n}}^{\frac{\delta}{\delta+1}}}} \leq 1 + \frac{1}{\delta}.
    \end{align}
    Moreover, we also have
