[Definition of arXiv:2512.09308, 'On asymptotic behavior of solutions to random fractional Riesz-Bessel equations with cycli'] [seneta2006regularly]
A function $L(\cdot)$ is slowly varying at infinity if it is real-valued, positive, and measurable on $[A,\infty)$ for some $A>0$, and satisfies the following condition for every $\lambda >0$:
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{x\to \infty} \frac{L(\lambda x)}{L(x)}=1.
\end{equation*}

[Lem 9 of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For all $p \in (0,1)$,
