body:
[Lemma L:compare_T_S of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] Let ${\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} $ be a random spanning tree with law as in (equation eq:PomegaT of the paper), and denote by $S_1, S_2, \ldots$ components chosen at random as in Section~(S:size_biased_GNP of the paper). If $t_1$ denotes the first repeat time of the process $(S_i)_{i\geq 1}$, then with $\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mathrm{P}}}_{\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} $-probability at least $1 - n^{-1}$
     \begin{equation} 
        \operatorname{diam}({\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} ) \geq \sum_{i=1}^{t_1 - 1} d_{S_i}(u_i, v_i),
    \end{equation}
    where $u_i, v_i$ are two uniform random points in $S_i$ and $d_{S_i}$ is the graph distance on $S_i$.

