[Thm 1 of arXiv:2512.02538, 'On the spectral geometry of Liouville quantum gravity'] \begin{equation}
\mu_h( \mathrm{d} z) = \lim_{\eps\to 0} \eps^{\gamma^2/2} \exp \left( \gamma h_\eps( \dd z)  \right) v_g (\dd z)
\end{equation}
exists in probability.  Furthermore the resulting measure is nonzero precisely when $\gamma \in [0,2)$, and is independent of the choice of regularisation kernel $\theta$ subject to very mild conditions. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 102 (Fixed-order moment scaling for the classical It\^o tower) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] For every integer $k\ge0$ and $q\ge2$, there is
$C_{k,q}=C_{k,q}(\Lambda,B,T)$, independent of $P$ and $s$, such that
for $s\le t\le T$,
\begin{equation}
 \left\|\sup_{s\le r\le t}
 \|\mathrm I_{s,r}^{P,(k)}\|_2\right\|_{L^q(P)}
 \le C_{k,q}|t-s|^{k/2}.
\end{equation}
For $k\ge0$ and $s\le u\le v\le T$,
\begin{equation}
 \|\mathrm I_{s,v}^{P,(k)}-\mathrm I_{s,u}^{P,(k)}\|_{L^q(P)}
 \le C_{k,q}|v-u|^{1/2}.
\end{equation}
In particular every level is a well-defined continuous Hilbert-tensor
semimartingale with moments of every fixed order.

