body:
[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2609.02423, '2609.02423'] Let $z$ solve
\begin{equation}
 z_t-i\omega(D)z=G
\end{equation}
on a time interval, and let $A$ be multiplication by a real bounded
function.  Then
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\dd}{\dd t}\ip{Az}{z}
 +\ip{i[\omega(D),A]z}{z}
 =2\operatorname{Re}\ip{AG}{z}.
\end{equation}
If $A=\tau a_*$ on a microlocal chart and
$\tau=\sgn v_\nu$ there, the principal symbol of the commutator term
on the left is
\begin{equation}
 \tau a_*'v_\nu=a_*'|v_\nu|\ge0.
\end{equation}

