[Theorem thm: distr of arXiv:2512.05896, 'T\'oth's buses and the ``detachment process'''] The random variable $\tau^{(n)}$ 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item  is almost surely finite, with a tail asymptotical with $n(n-1)/k$ as $k\to\infty$ and thus has infinite expectation;
    \item has distribution function 
\begin{align}
F^{(n)}(k)
= P(\tau^{(n)} \le k)
= \frac{\binom{k}{n}}{\binom{k+n-1}{n}},
\end{align}
using the convention $\binom{a}{b}:=0$ when $a<b.$
\end{enumerate}

