[Corollary coro_4 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $n\ge3$ be odd. Define
\begin{eqnarray}

h_n(v)=e^{\frac{v}{2}}\sum_{i=0}^{\frac{n-1}{2}}\frac{(2i-1)!!{\frac{n-1}{2}\choose i}}{(n-1)^{i}}\frac{v^i}{(v+1)^{2i+1}}.
\end{eqnarray} 

If $r,v$ are such that $h_n(v)<1$ and $r\geq nv$, then the $m_\infty$-inequality of order $k=1$ in ((case_k_1 of the paper)) is tighter than the original $m_\infty$-inequality.

