[Prop weight of corners of arXiv:2411.01104, 'Gaussian universality of $p$-adic random matrix products via corners'] Let $A^{(i)},A^{(i+1)}$ be the same as (cor: interlacing of the paper). Also, let $A^{(i+1)'}\in\Mat_{(n-i)\times n}(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ be the submatrix of $A_i$ eliminating the second row, and $A^{(i+2)}\in\Mat_{(n-i-1)\times n}(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ be the submatrix of $A_i$ eliminating the first and second row. Then we have 
\begin{equation}
|\SN(A^{(i)})|-|\SN(A^{(i+1)})|\ge|\SN(A^{(i+1)'})|-|\SN(A^{(i+2)})|.\end{equation}

