[Corollary cor:vestimate3_difference of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] Let  $K\geq 2$ be a fixed  integer number, $n,m\geq 1$ and $\zeta>0$. For any initial product measure $\mu^{\epsilon}$ satisfying (equation Ass1 of the paper), and times  $0<s<r\leq T$, there exists $\tilde\Delta>0$, such that when $r-s\leq \tilde\Delta$
\begin{equation}
\sup_{\underline{y}\in\Lambda_{N}^{m,\neq}}\sup_{\underline{x}\in\Lambda_{N}^{n,\neq}}|v^{\epsilon,m,n}_{s,r}(\underline{y}, \underline{x}|\mu^{\epsilon})-v^{\epsilon,m,n}_{s,r}(\underline{y}, \underline{x}+\underline e_1|\mu^{\epsilon})|\lesssim 
\begin{cases}
 \epsilon^{1+\zeta}(r-s)^{-1+\zeta},&n+m=2\\
 \epsilon^{1+\zeta}(r-s)^{-1/2},&n=1,m\geq 2 \\
 \epsilon^{1+\zeta}(r-s)^{-1+\zeta},& 2\leq n\leq K,m\geq 1 \\
 \epsilon^{1+\zeta},&n\geq K+1, m\geq 1
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
and when $r-s> \tilde\Delta$,   
\begin{equation}
\sup_{\underline{y}\in\Lambda_{N}^{m,\neq}}\sup_{\underline{x}\in\Lambda_{N}^{n,\neq}}|v^{\epsilon,m,n}_{s,r}(\underline{y}, \underline{x}|\mu^{\epsilon})-v^{\epsilon,m,n}_{s,r}(\underline{y}, \underline{x}+\underline e_1|\mu^{\epsilon})|)\lesssim \epsilon^{1+\zeta}.
\end{equation}
where $\underline e_1$ being the unit vector in the positive 1st-direction. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Dfn of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] [{The local Hausdorff topology}]
  We call $\lHausdMet{S}{\rho_{S}}$ the \textit{local Hausdorff metric (with the root $\rho_{S}$)}
  and the topology induced from the local Hausdorff metric the \textit{local Hausdorff topology}.

[Lem lall of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] For $L>0$, let $\mathcal S(L)$ be the set of closed geodesics on $X$ of length at most $L$. There exist
constants $0< \beta < 1$ and $c>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \liminf_{L\to\infty}
 \frac{
   \left|
     \left\{
       \gamma\in\mathcal S(L):
       N_{A,B}(\gamma)\geq\beta\,\ell_X(\gamma)
     \right\}
   \right|
 }{
   |\mathcal S(L)|
 }
 \geq c.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

