[Proposition 35 (\cite{BB23, BB24a}) of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] There is a diffeomorphism~$\Omega:\mathcal F_R\to \mathbb H^-$, such that for~$z\in \mathbb H^-$,
\begin{equation*}
F'(z;\xi,\eta)=0 \iff z=\Omega(\xi,\eta).
\end{equation*}
Moreover,~$\Omega(\xi,\eta)$ is a simple zero of~$F'(z;\xi,\eta)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop partition-function-sharpness of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Let $\beta>0$, let $\mathsf{d}/2\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}$, and assume $\mu\in L^\infty\cap\mathcal{P}({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})$.  There exist constants $c,C>0$ and $N_0\ge3$, depending on $(\beta,\mu,\mathsf{d},\mathsf{s})$, such that, for every $N\ge N_0$,
\begin{align}
{\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)
\ge C^{-1}
\begin{cases}
(\log N)^c, & \mathsf{s}=\mathsf{d}/2,\\[0.3em]
\exp\left\{c(\log N)^{2-\mathsf{d}/\mathsf{s}}\right\}, & \mathsf{d}/2<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}.
\end{cases}
\end{align}
In particular, ${\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)\to+\infty$ as $N\to\infty$ throughout $\mathsf{d}/2\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}$.

