Since $h_\mu$ is bounded, the exact one-body decomposition (equation eq:roadmapIdentity of the paper) gives
\begin{align}
{\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)
&=e^{\beta I_\mu}
{\mathbb{E}}\left[e^{-\frac\beta2W_N+\frac\beta N\sum_{i=1}^N(h_\mu(\xi_i)-2I_\mu)}\right]\notag\\
&\ge c_{\beta,\mu}Z_N,
\qquad
c_{\beta,\mu}
\coloneqq
\exp\left\{\beta I_\mu-\beta\|h_\mu-2I_\mu\|_{L^\infty}\right\}>0.
\end{align}

