[Definition $2$-cyclical monotonicity of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] A measurable set $E\subset \mathbb R^{d}\times \mathbb R^{d}$ is \emph{$2$-cyclically monotone} if for any finite sequences $\{(x_k,y_k)\}_{k=1}^N\subset E$, and any permutations $\sigma$ on $\{1,2,\cdots, N\}$, it holds
	\begin{align*}
		\sum_{k=1}^N \frac 12  |x_k-y_k|^2 &\le \sum_{k=1}^N \frac 12 |x_k-y_{\sigma(k)}|^2.
	\end{align*}

