[Proposition 30 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] Let \(f:X^{m+r}\dashrightarrow Z^m\) be an almost holomorphic fibration from a compact K\"ahler manifold onto a normal compact K\"ahler space which is not uniruled, and assume that a general fibre is biholomorphic to \(\PP^r\). Let \(\omega\) be a K\"ahler metric on \(X\) with positive scalar curvature, and let \(a:=[\omega]\cdot [L]\), where \(L\) is a line in a general fibre.  If
\begin{equation}
        \min_XS(\omega)\,a=2\pi r(r+1),
\end{equation}
then the universal cover splits holomorphically and isometrically as
\begin{equation}
        (\widetilde X,\widetilde\omega)
        \cong
        (\PP^r,a\omega_{\mathrm{FS}})\times(Y,\omega_{\mathrm{RF}}),
\end{equation}
where \(\omega_{FS}\) is the Fubini--Study metric and \(\omega_{RF}\) is Ricci-flat.

[Defi 12 (cf. \cite{FM23}, Definition 2.4) of arXiv:2608.30743, 'Perspectives on the Bott spectral sequence for Lie groupoids'] Let $G$ be a regular Lie groupoid. A multiplicative Ehresmann connection with respect to the isotropy algebroid is a distribution $E \subset T G_1$ together with a splitting $TG_1 = E \oplus (\ker(Tt) \cap \ker(Ts))$, such that the map

    \begin{center}
    \begin{tikzcd}
	E \arrow[d, shift right, "Tt" left] \arrow[d, shift left, "Ts" right] \arrow[r, hook] & T G_1 \arrow[d, shift right, "Tt" left] \arrow[d, shift left, "Ts" right] \\
	T G_0 \arrow[r] & T G_0
	\end{tikzcd}
    \end{center}

    is an inclusion of Lie groupoids.

[Lemma lem:mixed_tail_pointwise_measure_chain of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] Let $K\subseteq T$ be finite and contain $t_0$. For every
$j\in\cbr{1,2}$, there exists an admissible sequence $\mathcal T_j=(T_{j,k})_{k\ge0}$ of subsets of $K$ such that $T_{j,0}=\cbr{t_0}$ and $T_{j,k}=K$ for all sufficiently large $k$. Moreover, for every
$t\in K$,
\begin{align*}
G_{j,K}(t):=
\sum_{k\ge0}
2^{k/\alpha_j}d_j(t,T_{j,k})\le
C_{\alpha_j}^{(1)}
\rbr{\Phi_j(t)+v_j(t)},
\end{align*}
where $C_{\alpha_j}^{(1)}<\infty$ depends only on $\alpha_j$.

