[Corollary 59 (Evaluated local-to-global reconstruction) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:sharp-reconstruction}, let $K$ be
the reconstructed decoupled coefficient.  If $2\le r<\infty$, then, for
every $1\le p<\infty$,
\begin{equation}

 \norm{\cT_K^{(m)}}_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \le C_m(p+r)^{m/2}\Rec_{m,r}(\mathbf K).
\end{equation}
If the stochastic legs are labelled copies of one real Hilbert space and the
blocks come from symmetric same-field kernels, then the reconstructed
same-field coefficient, denoted again by $K$, satisfies
\begin{equation}

 \norm{I_m(K)}_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \le A_m(p+r)^{m/2}\Rec_{m,r}(\mathbf K).
\end{equation}

[Proposition 28 (Canonical/modulated identity) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] One has the exact thermal-equilibrium splitting
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb P_{N,\beta}=\mathbb Q_{N,\beta}(\mu_\beta),
 \qquad
 \D\mathbb P_{N,\beta}
 =\mathsf K_{N,\beta}(\mu_\beta)^{-1}e^{-\beta A_{N,\beta}}\,\D\mu_\beta^{\otimes N}.
\end{equation}

