[Lemma lem:firsthalfsum of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Let $a>0,b>1$, $t\in [0,1]$ and $N_n \in [\frac{n}{3}, \frac{2n}{3}-1]$. Then there exists a constant $\gamma_{a,b}$ depending on $a$ and $b$ only, such that
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{k=1}^{N_n} 
    \frac{1}{(n-k-t)^{a}(k+t)^{b}}
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 k}}
    \le
    \frac{\gamma_{a,b}}{n^a |z|^{2(b-1)}}.
\end{align*}

metadata_json:
{"artifact_digest":"sha256:42b29080805a0d17c4f873b506d6e39de229e7c18ebf1f5b58d36028ee88cbd7","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/42/42b29080805a0d17c4f873b506d6e39de229e7c18ebf1f5b58d36028ee88cbd7.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:1a22ffd94c8485f47b7a99ca1f9fbb40f01dfec7f41e595117fa6e858d418bee","bundle_entry_key":"2412-09145-lemma-4-firsthalfsum","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_127","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_127.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2412-09145-lemma-4-firsthalfsum","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Noting that $n-k-t \ge n/3$ for all $k\le N_n$, we have
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{k=1}^{N_n}
        \frac{1}{(n-k-t)^{a}(k+t)^{b}}
        e^{-\frac{z^2}{2k}}
\le
    \frac{3^{a}}{n^{a}}
    \sum_{k=1}^{\infty}
        \frac{1}{(k+t)^{b}}
        e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 (k+t)}}.
\end{align*}
For all $k\ge 1$ and any $\tau \in [0,1]$ one has
\begin{align*}
    \frac{1}{(k+t)^b}e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 (k+t)}}
    \le
    \frac{1}{(k+t)^{b}}e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 (k+t+\tau)}}
    \le
    \frac{2^{b}}{(k+t+\tau)^b}e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 (k+t+\tau)}}.
\end{align*}
