[Definition of arXiv:2608.12415, 'Sharp Phase Transition for Ellipsoid Fitting'] For any deviation vector $\eta_\tau$ such that $\tau\neq \emptyset$, 	we define $
	\mathsf{Proper} \mathcal{L}^*(w_\tau)$ to be the weighted linear combination of the following terms in the $3$-way concatenation in $\frac{1}{1-\gamma}\cdot  \mathcal{L}^*(w_\tau)$:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item Proper concatenations such that each non-trivial gadget in $A^{-1}$-path is an $\alpha$-gadget;
		\item Linearization of well-behaved intersections such that each non-trivial gadget in $A^{-1}$-path is an $\alpha$-gadget.
	\end{enumerate}
	It is important to distinguish between $\mathsf{Proper}(\eta_\tau)$ and $\mathsf{Proper}\mathcal{L}^*(w_\tau)$.

[Lemme lemma:flat_dend_morph of arXiv:2609.02346, 'Regularised double shuffle relations for planar \AZVs{}'] Let $\Omega$ be a set (resp. $(\Omega,+)$ a commutative semigroup). The map 
 \begin{equation*}
  \flaten_0:(\mathcal{PT}_\Omega,<,>)\longrightarrow(\mathcal{W}_{\Omega},\prec,\succ)\qquad(\text{\normalfont{ resp. } }\flaten_1:(\mathcal{PT}_\Omega,<,>,\bullet)\longrightarrow(\mathcal{W}_{\Omega},\prec,\succ,\cdot))
 \end{equation*}

is a morphism of dendriform algebras (resp. of tridendriform algebras).

