[Lemma comparisionprim of arXiv:2505.13382, 'The localization transition for the directed polymer in a random environment is smooth'] We set $K_1:= 2 e^{\lambda(\beta_c+1)+ \lambda(-\beta_c-1)}$.
Given $p\in (1,1+\frac{2}{d}]$ for all $u\in [0,1]$ such that $|\mathfrak{f}(\beta_c+u)|\le 2K_1$ we have
 \begin{equation}
 |\mathfrak{f}(\beta_c+u)|\le  2 \sqrt{ \frac{K_1}{p-1} \textsc{f}_{p}(\beta_c+u)}.
 \end{equation}
 Hence for any $p\in (1,1+\frac{2}{d}]$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \liminf_{u\downarrow 0}\frac{\log |\mathfrak{f}(\beta_c+u)|}{\log u}\ge \frac{1}{2} \liminf_{u\to 0+}    \frac{\log \textsc{f}_p(\beta_c+u)}{\log u}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem sum-Jn of arXiv:2604.24914, 'SPDEs with time-independent\\ L\'evy colored noise'] Suppose that Hypotheses A', B', D' and E' hold. Then $f_n^{*}(\cdot,x;t)\in \mathcal{H}^{\otimes n}$ for any $n\geq 1$ and $(t,x)\in \mathbb{R}_{+}\times \mathbb{R}^d$. If in addition,
\begin{equation}

\sum_{n\geq 1}m_2^n t^n J_n(t)<\infty \quad \mbox{for any $t>0$},
\end{equation}
then equation (equation mult-eq of the paper) has a unique solution.

