[Prop ContOUGFF of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] The process $(\Phi_{\varepsilon}(x,t))_{\varepsilon>0, x\in D, t\in \mathbb R}$ has a continuous modification (which we also identify with $\varPhi$). Furthermore, 
    for all $\alpha\in (0, 1/2)$ and $\rho, \zeta >0$, a.s. there
    exists a constant $M = M(\alpha, \rho, \zeta)$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        |\Phi_{\varepsilon}(x,t) - \Phi_{\delta}(y,s)| \leq M
        \left(\ln\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon\land \delta}\right)\right)^{\zeta}
        \frac{(|(x,t,\varepsilon)-(y,s,\delta)|)^{\alpha}}{(\varepsilon\land\delta)^{\alpha+\rho}}
    \end{equation*} 
    for all $(x,t), (y,s)\in D\times [0,T]$ and $\varepsilon,\delta \in [0,1]$ such that $1/2 \leq (\varepsilon \land \delta)/(\varepsilon\lor\delta) \leq 2$.

