[Lemma 4 (Caccioppoli-type inequality) of arXiv:2609.02732, 'Conservation of mass for solutions of Leibenson's equation on Riemannian Manifolds'] Let $\Omega $ be an open subset of $M$ and let $I$ be an interval in $\mathbb{R}_{+}=[0, \infty)$. Let $u=u\left( x,t\right) $ be a bounded
		non-negative subsolution to \emph{(\ref{dtv})} in a cylinder $\Omega\times I$. Let $\eta $ be a locally Lipschitz non-negative bounded
		function in $\Omega\times I$ such that $\eta(\cdot, t)$ has
		compact support in $\Omega $ for any $t\in I$. Fix some real $\sigma $
		such that 
		$\sigma > q(p-1)$ and set $\lambda=\sigma-\delta>1$. 
		Choose $t_{1},t_{2}\in I$ such that $t_{1}<t_{2}$. Then
		\begin{equation}
			\left[ \int_{\Omega }u^{\lambda }\eta^{p} \right] _{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}+c_{1}
			\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}
				\int_{\Omega}\left\vert \nabla \left( u^{\sigma/p }\eta \right) \right\vert
			^{p} \leq \int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}
				\int_{\Omega}\left[c_2u^{\sigma}|\nabla \eta|^{p}+pu^{\lambda}\eta^{p-1}\partial _{t}\eta\right],

		\end{equation}
		where $c_{1}, c_2$ are constants depending on $p, q$ and $\sigma$.

[Theorem thm:azuma-gtp of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a sequential gamble space satisfying Condition~(cond:usa-minimax of the paper).
  Let $\{X_t:\mathcal{Y}^T\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}\}_{t\leq T}$ be a game-theoretic supermartingale such that $|X_t-X_{t-1}|\leq c_t$ g.t.a.s.\ for all $t\leq T$ for constants $c_t\geq 0$.
  Then for all $\epsilon > 0$ we have
  \begin{align}

    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}}[X_T-X_0\geq \epsilon] \leq \exp \left(- {\epsilon ^{2} \over 2\sum _{t=1}^{T}c_{t}^{2}}\right)~.
  \end{align}

