[Lemma lem:small-jumps of arXiv:2608.28004, 'Hausdorff Dimension of the Set of Extreme Points\\ of a Random Countable Stable Zonotope'] For every \(q>0\), there exists \(C_q<\infty\), depending only on \(d\),
\(\alpha\), and \(q\), such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb E\bigl[(1+M_Q)^N V_Q^{\,q}\bigr]
    \leq C_q\,\delta^{q}
\end{equation}
uniformly over all positive integers \(n\) and all \(Q\in\mathcal Q_n\).

[Corollary COR33 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] \begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] A set $N\subset G$ is ${\mathscr E}^G$-polar if and only if it is ${\mathscr E}$-polar.
\item[(2)] Let $G_1\subset G$.  Then, $G_1$ is ${\mathscr E}$-quasi-open  if and only if it is ${\mathscr E}^G$-quasi-open.
\end{itemize}

[Theorem afixed_t of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] For every
$x\in \mathbb{C}\backslash \big((-\infty, 0] \cup [1, +\infty)\big)$
and $t\ge 0$,
\begin{align}
F(x,t;q)=\exp \left[
{-\frac 1 \varepsilon\, {\operatorname{Li}}_2(x)+\frac{1}{2} \log (1-x) + t x + O(\varepsilon)}
\right]
\;, \quad \varepsilon=-\log q \to 0^+
\end{align}
Equation (equation F1 of the paper) also holds true as $x$ approaches zero at an angle $\phi $ with the positive real axis provided that $\phi \not= \pi$.

[Corollary thm:main-upper of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] For $n\ge2$,
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}} = \lambda_2(K_{\mathrm{PF}})
 =\frac{n}{2(n+1)}.

