[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2604.26549, 'Existence and uniqueness results of a stochastic nonlinear heat equation with a constraint'] For the sequence of stopping times
			\begin{align}
				\tau^k_m:=\inf\left\{t\in[0,T]:\|u_m(t)\|_{H_0^1(\bO)} + \|u_m(t)\|_{L^p(\bO)}\geq k\right\},
			\end{align}
			where $k\in\N$, the solution of the SDE \eqref{eqn-Faedo-Galerkin} lie on manifold $\bM$, i.e., $u_m(t\wedge\tau^k_m)\in\bM$ for all $t\in[0,T]$.

[Lem sparse-giant-nearby of arXiv:2606.01627, 'The geometry of the giant component of random geometric graphs'] Fix $\beta,\varepsilon >0, \lambda_0 > \lambda_c$ and $x \in M$.      There are constants $c = c(\lambda_0,d,\varepsilon,\beta,M) > 0$ and $n_0 = n_0(\lambda_0,d,\varepsilon,\beta,M), L' = L'(\lambda_0,d,\varepsilon)$ so that if $r \leq n^{-\beta}$ and $\lambda \geq \lambda_0$ then the following holds. 
    The event
    \[
    \mathcal{C}:=
    \left\{
        \begin{array}{c}
        \text{there exists a connected component }
        \kappa \text{ of } G^-(r) \\
        \text{such that }
        \forall p \in \mathring{G}^{n}_M(r) \cap B_M(x,\delta/L'),
        \exists p' \in \kappa  \\ 
        \mbox{ such that }
        d^\lambda_r(p,u^{-1}(p')) \le \log^2 n
        \end{array}
    \right\}
    \]
    satisfies
    $\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{C}^c) \leq \exp(- c \log ^2n)$ for all $n \geq n_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lm:double-edge-integration of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] For any matrices $A,B \in \R^3$, if $Q \sim \mrm{Haar}(\mrm{SO}(3))$, then
    \begin{equs}
        \E[\mrm{Tr}(AQ)\mrm{Tr}(Q^*B)]=\frac{1}{3}\mrm{Tr}(AB)
    \end{equs}

