[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Let $\qm(X)$ be defined in \eqref{eq:qproc:defn} and assume that $X(0) = x_0\in \Cc$ is such that $\qm(x_0)>0$. Then, for $t<  \taumz\wedge \tau_{\mathcal K}$, the process $\Qm = -\ln \qm(X)$ is a continuous semi-martingale with the local martingale part 
            \begin{equation}

                d\mart{\Qm} = -2\sum_{\ccm} \frac{1}{\rcx} \sum_{k=1}^N \hcX{k} \sigma_k(X)dB_k
            \end{equation}
        and the drift giving as a sum $d\drift{\Qm} = h_1(X)dt+h_2(X)dt+h_3(X)dt$, where
            \begin{eqnarray}

	           h_1(x) &=& \sum_{\ccm} \frac{1}{(\rcx)^2}\sum_{k=1}^N\left(2(\hcx{k})^2-\rcx \sum_{\alpha\in R_+(\Cluster)}\alpha_k^2\right)\sigma_k^2(x),\\

	           h_2(x) &=& -2\sum_{\ccm} \frac{1}{\rcx} \sum_{k=1}^N \hcx{k} b_k(x),\\

	        h_3(x) &=& -2\sum_{\ccm} \frac{1}{\rcx} \sum_{\dR} \frac{\kdx \hcx{\delta} }{\xd} \/,
            \end{eqnarray}

