body:
[Lem 42 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Let $f:X\to\R$ be a function on a metric space $(X,d)$
  with $\|f\|_{\Lip^{1/2}},\|f\|_{\Lip^{1}}<\infty$.
  Then it holds that
  \begin{align*}
    \|f\|_{\Lip^{\kappa}}\leq \|f\|_{\Lip^{1/2}}^{2(1-\kappa)}\|f\|_{\Lip^{1}}^{2\kappa-1}
  \end{align*}
  for $\kappa\in [1/2,1]$.

