[Corollary corol:semigroup_taylor of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] For any $\theta\ge0$ and $H\in \mathcal{S}_\theta$, we have 
\begin{equation*}
    P_{t+\varepsilon}^\theta H=P_t^\theta H+\varepsilon \mathfrak{A}_\theta P_t^\theta H+o(\varepsilon, t),
\end{equation*}
where $o(\varepsilon, t)$ denotes a function in $\mathcal{S}_\theta$ such that $\mylim_{\varepsilon\to0}\frac{o(\varepsilon, t)}{\varepsilon}=0$ in the topology of $\mathcal{S}_\theta$. Moreover, the limit is uniform on compact time intervals. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

