[Thm eq:gauge_PDE_intro of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $R\subset \mathbb{R}^d$ and a suitable boundary function $H_b$ on $\partial R$. If $H$ is a weak solution to the differential equation 
    \begin{align}
         \text{div} (\nabla F(\nabla H)) = 0
    \end{align}
    with $H\mid_{\partial R} = H_b$, the limiting gauge flow is $\alpha = \nabla H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2608.30570, '2608.30570'] Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a closed set in a surface $\Sigma$ with connected interior $\mathring{\mathcal{A}}$ and $D\subset \mathcal{A}$ is closed subset such that
 \begin{align*}
 D\cap \mathring{\mathcal{A}}\neq \emptyset \quad \text{ and } \quad  \mathring{\mathcal{A}}\backslash D\neq \emptyset.
 \end{align*}
 Then, for any connected component $V$ of $\mathring{\mathcal{A}}\backslash D$, there holds
 \begin{align*}
 \partial V\cap \partial D\neq \emptyset.
 \end{align*}
 Moreover, there also holds
 $$\partial D\cap \mathring{\mathcal{A}}\neq \emptyset.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:DOloc of arXiv:2411.00748, '\bfseries Central limit theorems for the nearest neighbour embracing graph in Euclidean an'] For $x \in \mathbb{X}^d$, define 
\[
    R(x,\eta) := \max\{R_1(x,\eta),2R_2(x,\eta)\},
\]
where
\begin{align*}
  &R_1(x,\eta) := \max_{z \in N(x,\eta)} d(z,x),\\
  &R_2(x,\eta) := \max\{d(z,y) : z\in \eta, x\in N(z,\eta+\delta_x),y\in N(z,\eta)\}.
\end{align*}
Then for all $x \in \mathbb{X}^d$, $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$ and $k \geq d+1$, it holds that
\begin{align*}
    &D_x F_t^{(\alpha)}(\eta) = D_xF_t^{(\alpha)} (\eta \cap B(x,R(x,\eta)))\\
    \intertext{and}
    &D_x G_t^{(k)}(\eta) = D_xG_t^{(k)} (\eta \cap B(x,R(x,\eta))).
\end{align*}

