body:
[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2605.31088, 'On couplings for kinetic Langevin diffusions'] Let the Markov chain $(Z_k,\tilde Z_k)_{k\in \N}$ be given by the iterated one-shot coupling introduced in Section~\ref{sssec: iterated one-shot} applied to the Markov chains \eqref{eq: linear Markov chain}. The probability that the two chains have not met after $n$ steps is given by
    \begin{equation}

        \P(Z_n\neq \tilde Z_n)=2\Phi\br{\frac{1}{2\Theta_{n}^{1/2}}}-1,
    \end{equation}
    where 
    \begin{equation*}
        \Theta_{n}=\sum_{k=1}^n\frac{1}{\l|B_{k}^{-1}\Pi_k\Delta z\r|^{2}},
    \end{equation*}
    and $\Pi_k\coloneqq A_kA_{k-1}\dots A_1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

