[Lemma a4:lemma:2_1 of arXiv:2510.01838, 'Shadow and percolation I: discrete landscapes with independence'] Let $X : \mathbb{Z}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$ and $\mu$ be such that Assumptions (a4:a:a1 of the paper) and (a4:a:a2 of the paper) hold.
    Let $\varepsilon>0$. There exist $n_0\in \mathbb{N}^*$ and $h_0>0$ (depending on $\varepsilon$) such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \forall h\leq h_0,\ \mathbb{P}(Y_1>_h Y_2>\dots >_h Y_{n_0})\leq \varepsilon^{2n_0}.
    \end{equation*}

