[Proposition cor:second-der-ub of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Let \((X_t)_{t \in [0, T]}\) be the uniform or remasking process. Then, for \(i \in [d]\) and \(t, v > 0\),
\begin{equation}

    \frac{\partial^2}{\partial t \partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i\ ;\, X_v^{-i}) \lesssim -\left(1 + \frac{1}{1 - e^{-t}}\right)\frac{\partial}{\partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i\ ;\, X_v^{-i}).
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if \(v \geq u\) with \(v - u \leq \kappa \min(1, u)\),
 \begin{equation*}
    -\frac{\partial}{\partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i \ ;\, X_v^{-i})\biggr\rvert_{t=u} = -\left(1 + O(\kappa)\right) \frac{\partial}{\partial v} \mathrm{I}(X_t^i \ ;\, X_v^{-i}) \biggr\rvert_{t=v}.
\end{equation*}

