[Proposition prop:commut otimes odot of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $A,A'\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ and $B,B'\subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be finite sets. For every $\alpha\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}^A$, $\alpha'\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}^{A'}$, $\beta\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}^{B}$ and $beta'\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}^{B'}$, we have
  \begin{equation}
    (\alpha\otimes \beta)\odot (\alpha'\otimes \beta')=(\alpha\odot \alpha')\otimes(\beta\odot\beta').
  \end{equation}

