[Lemma lem:diff-dual of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let $\alpha,\beta \in \mathcal{S}_{\ge 0}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, and let $\mathcal{W}_{\mathcal{S}}(\alpha,\beta)^2$ denote the minimum value of the primal problem (equation posdef-prog of the paper). 
	\begin{align}
		\mathcal{W}_{\mathcal{S}}(\alpha,\beta)^2 = \sup_{A,B} \operatorname{tr}[\alpha A + \beta B], 
	\end{align}
	where the supremum is taken over all pairs of positive semidefinite matrices $(A,B)$ satisfying the matrix inequality
	\begin{align}
		\begin{bmatrix}
			A & 0 \\ 0 & B
		\end{bmatrix}
		\le \frac{1}{2}
		\begin{bmatrix}
			I & -I \\ -I & I
		\end{bmatrix}.
	\end{align}

