[Corollary cor:proto-ville of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a sequentially normalized gamble space.
  Then for all $A\subseteq\mathcal{Y}^T$ we have
  \begin{align*}
    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A = \inf\{ X_0 \mid \{X_t\in\mathbb{R}\}_t \text{ game-theoretic supermartingale}, X_T \geq \mathds{1}_A \}~.
  \end{align*}
  If $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ is scalable, then  
  \begin{align*}
    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}} A = \inf\left\{ \alpha > 0 \,\middle|\, \{X_t \geq 0\}_t \text{ game-theoretic supermartingale}, X_0 = 1, X_T \geq \frac 1 \alpha \text{ on } A\right\}~.
  \end{align*}

