[Proposition step1 of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] We have 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q^{Q_{n+1}}\right] = \sum_{k=0}^{n}c^k\left(q;q\right)_{k+1} \left(q^{-1};q^{-1}\right)_k h_{n-k}\left(1+ca_1,\dots 1+ca_{k+1}\right).
    \end{equation}
    As a consequence, 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}_{x}\left[Q_{n+1} - Q_1\right] = c \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} \sum_{k=0}^{i}c^k\left(q;q\right)_{k+1} \left(q^{-1};q^{-1}\right)_k h_{i-k}\left(1+ca_1,\dots 1+ca_{k+1}\right).
    \end{equation}

