body:
[Definition definitionvestimate of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] We fix an initial product measure $\mu^{\epsilon}$ on  $\Lambda_N$.

Suppose that the process $\{\eta_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}$ starts with $\mu_{\epsilon}$ and $\rho_{\epsilon}(t,x) $ is the solution of (equation eq:linearized of the paper). We define the space  $v$-function as:
\begin{equation}
v_{n}^{\epsilon}(\underline{x},t|\mu^{\epsilon}):=\mathbb{E}^{\epsilon}_{\mu^\epsilon}\left[\prod_{i=1}^{n}\left(\eta_{t}(x_i)-\rho_{\epsilon}(x_{i},t)\right)\right],\quad \underline{x}\in\Lambda_{N}^{n,\neq},n\geq1
\end{equation}
where $\Lambda_{N}^{n,\neq}$ is the set of all sequences $(x_1,\dots,x_n)\in \Lambda_{N}^{n}$ with $x_i\neq x_j$. For brevity, we
shall write $v_{n}^{\epsilon}(\underline{x},t)\equiv v_{n}^{\epsilon}(\underline{x},t|\mu^{\epsilon})$. When $\underline{x}=x$ then 
\begin{equation} 
v_{1}^{\epsilon}(x,t):=\rho_t^{\epsilon}(x)-\rho_{\epsilon}(x,t).
\end{equation}
and when $\underline{x}=\underline\emptyset$ is the empty configuration (i.e., no particles in the system), then 
\begin{equation}
v_0^{\epsilon}(\underline \emptyset,t)=1.
\end{equation}

