body:
[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2506.16260, 'Fractional Compound Poisson Random Fields on Plane'] The density $g_\alpha(x,t_1,t_2)=\mathrm{Pr}\{H_\alpha(t_1,t_2)\in\mathrm{d}x\}/\mathrm{d}x$, $x\ge0$, $(t_1,t_2)\in\mathbb{R}^2_+$ solves the following fractional differential equation:
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{\partial}{\partial t_1}g_\alpha(x,t_1,t_2)=-t_2\frac{\partial^\alpha}{\partial x^\alpha}g_\alpha(x,t_1,t_2),
	\end{equation}
	with $g_\alpha(0,t_1,t_2)=0$ and $g_\alpha(x,0,t_2)=\delta(x)$. Here, $\frac{\partial^\alpha}{\partial x^\alpha}$ is the Caputo fractional derivative and $\delta(x)$ denotes the Dirac delta function.

