[Definition 15 of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] For $\theta \in \bR$, the spectral function $C(\theta)$
  associated with the measure $\mu$ is defined by
  \begin{equation}

    C(\theta) = - \inf \left\{ \cE^{\alpha}(u,u) - \theta \int_{\bR^{d}} u(x)^{2} \mu(dx)
    \;:\; u \in \cF^{\alpha}, \int_{\bR^{d}} u(x)^{2} dx = 1 \right\}.
  \end{equation}

[Prop F-Borel of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] The following assertions hold:
\begin{enumerate}	
\item[\rm(1)] The set $F$ is Borel measurable.
\item[\rm(2)] The process $\check{\mathbb{X}}$ with state space $F$ is a Borel right-continuous Markov process.
\end{enumerate}

[Corollary 2-l13 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a finite subset $D$ of ${\mathbb Z}^d$. Then, there exists a finite
constant $C_0$, depending only on $D$ and the bounds (equation 2-38b of the paper),
(equation 2-84 of the paper) on the density profile, such that
\begin{align*}
& {\mathbb E}_{\nu^N} \Big[ \, \Big|\, \int_s^t \sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} G_x(r)\,
\omega_{x+D}(r) \; dr \,\Big|^\alpha\,\Big] \\
&\qquad \;\le\; C_0 \,
N^{\alpha d/2} \, |t-s|^\alpha \, \sup_{s\le r \le t} \Vert G(r) \Vert^\alpha _\infty \,
\sup_{s\le r\le t} \big( \, 1 \,+\,
H_N(f^N_r)\,\big)^{\alpha /2} 
\end{align*}
for all $1\le \alpha\le 2$, $0<s<t$,
$G\colon [0,T]\times {\mathbb T}^d_N \to{\mathbb R}$ and $N\ge 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 10 of arXiv:2608.06011, 'Strong averaging principle for multiscale time-inhomogeneous SDEs with multiplicative $\al'] A measure-valued function $\rho_t^{x}$ is said to be a $\tau$-periodic measure for the two parameter Markov semigroup $P^{x}(s,t)$ if it satisfies
    \begin{align*}
        \rho_{t+\tau}^{x}=\rho_t^{x}~~~\mbox{and}~~~P^{*,x}(s,t)\rho_s^{x}=\int_{\br^m}P^x(s,w,t,\cdot)\rho_s^x(\d w)=\rho_t^{x}.
    \end{align*}

