[Lemma lem:ito of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $X$ be a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with initial value $X_0 \sim \eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}^+_{tem})$, $p>2$, such that (equation eq:cond_x_0 of the paper) holds.
	Let $(v_s)_{s\geq 0}$ be $\mathbb{R}$-valued, absolutely continuous, monotonically increasing or decreasing, locally bounded and such that $v_0 = 0$ and let $T >0$. Then it follows that 
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{split}
			&\mathbb{E}^X\Big[\exp(-\langle V_t(\mu), X_{T-t}\rangle + v_t)\Big] = \mathbb{E}^X\Big[\exp(-\langle V_0(\mu),X_T\rangle)\Big]\\
			& \qquad  +\mathbb{E}^X\Big[ \int_0^t \exp(-\langle V_s(\mu), X_{T-s}\rangle+ v_s) \big(\langle V_s(\mu), h(X_{T-s})\rangle+ v_s'\big) ds\Big], \quad t \in [0,T],
		\end{split}
	\end{equation*}
for all finite measures $\mu$.

