body:
[Proposition 8 (Continuous stable OU persistence) of arXiv:2608.17927, 'Near-unit-root persistence of symmetric stable \\ autoregressive sequences'] Let $Y$ solve \eqref{eq:ou-sde}, with $\theta, \eta, x > 0$. Then
\begin{equation}

\PP_{x}(Y_{s} > 0,\ 0 \leq s \leq t) \sim
c_{\alpha} x^{\alpha/2} \Bigl(\frac{\alpha\theta}{\eta^{\alpha}}\Bigr)^{1/2} e^{-\alpha\theta t/2}, \quad t \to \infty.
\end{equation}
In particular, its continuous-time persistence rate is $\alpha\theta/2$.

[Thm 3 of arXiv:2608.28234, 'A note on the positivity of $Q$-curvature via the continuity method'] Let $(M, g)$ be a smooth closed Riemannian manifold of dimension $n=5$. Suppose $Y(M, [g]) > 0$ and $Y_{4}^{\ast}(M, [g]) > 0$. Assume further that there exists a conformal metric $g_0 \in [g]$ and a constant $t_0 \in (1, \frac{10}{3}]$ such that
\begin{equation}
t_0 \left(- \Delta_{0} J_0 + \frac{n-4}{2} J_{0}^2\right) + 4\sigma_2(A_0) > 0 \quad \text{and} \quad J_0 > 0.
\end{equation}
Here $\Delta_{0} := \Delta_{g_0}$, $J_0 := J_{g_0}$ and $A_0 := A_{g_0}$. Then there exists a conformal metric $\tilde{g}\in[g]$ with positive scalar curvature $\tilde{R} > 0$ and positive $Q$-curvature $\tilde{Q} > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

