[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.00813, 'Convex order, log-convexity and Moments of Averages of Random Variables'] Let $a,b\in \z_{>0}^n$ be partitions of $m$. Let $A_j = a_1+\dots + a_j$, $B_j=b_1+\dots+b_j$ and $A_0=B_0=0$. Then a necessary and sufficient condition for
\begin{align}
\sum_{\si\in S_m} \p \bigg[\prod_{j=1}^{n} \bigg(\frac1{a_j}\sum_{i=A_{j-1}+1}^{A_j} X_{\si(i)}\bigg)\bigg] \leq \sum_{\si\in S_m} \p \bigg[\prod_{j=1}^{n} \bigg(\frac1{b_j}\sum_{i=B_{j-1}+1}^{B_j} X_{\si(i)}\bigg)\bigg]
\end{align}
for all real numbers $X_1,X_2,\ldots,X_m\geq 0$ and every convex function $\p:\rp\to\r$ is that $a \maj b$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

