[Lemma lmboundekaa of arXiv:2601.09537, 'Gene genealogies in haploid populations evolving according to sweepstakes reproduction'] Suppose a population evolves according to Def.\ (hapltwo of the paper).  Then there is a constant $B > 0$ with
\begin{esplit}{egboundekaa}
 \frac{ (N)_2 }{c_N} \EE{ \frac{(X_1)_{k_1} (X_2)_{k_2} }{ (S_N)_{k_1 + k_2} } | \ensuremath{{\alpha_1}}, \ensuremath{{\kappa}} } \frac{\varepsilon_N}{ (N)_2 } \ge  \varepsilon_N \frac{B}{N^{\ensuremath{{\alpha_1}}+\ensuremath{{\kappa}} - 1} }
\end{esplit}
for all $k_1, k_2 \ge 2$.

