body:
[Lem Feller-1 of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] Assume that $F$ is closed. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm(1)] $P_F(C_0(X))\subset C_0(X)$.
\item[\rm(2)] For all $u\in C_0(X)$ we have $\lim_{\alpha\to\infty}\alpha \check{R}_\alpha u = P_Fu$, uniformly on $X$. 
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lemma-entropy-estimate of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] For every $\theta\in \mathcal{C}_0$ with $ \mathcal{I}(\theta)< \infty $, let $ g\in L^2([0,T];H)$ be the control such that $ \theta $ solves (equation PDE-SQG of the paper) weakly.
	For every $ \varepsilon>0 $ and $m(\varepsilon)\in\mathbb{N}_+$ satisfying the  scaling regime (equation scaling-m of the paper), let $\theta_{\varepsilon,m(\varepsilon)}$ and $\mu_{\varepsilon,m(\varepsilon)}$ be as in Proposition (prop-restricted-lower-bound of the paper). Then there exists a family of probability measure  $\{\pi_{\varepsilon,m(\varepsilon), \theta}\}$ on $ \mathbb{X}_{\alpha,\beta} $ that satisfies the entropy inequality
	\begin{equation}
		\limsup _{\varepsilon\rightarrow 0} \operatorname{Ent}\left(\pi_{\varepsilon,m(\varepsilon), \theta} \mid \mu_{\varepsilon,m(\varepsilon)}\right) \leqslant \mathcal{I}(\theta).
	\end{equation}

[Proposition replace-M-by-explicit-expression-in-tightness of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $\Pi$ be a fixed point of BBM with drift $\lambda > \sqrt{2}$ and $\theta \in Dom_{\lambda}(\Pi)$. Then, the family of random variables $Z_t$ given by 

\begin{equation}
  Z_t := \int_{- \infty}^0 \frac{1}{\sqrt{t}}e^{(1-\frac{\lambda^2}{2})t}e^{\lambda x}e^{-\frac{x^2}{2t}}\theta(dx) 
\end{equation}
is tight in $t\geq 1$.

