body:
[Definition 2 (Blocking Measure) of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] Let 
\begin{equation} 
    A = \{\eta\colon\Z\to\{0,1\}: \sum_{x = -\infty}^0 \eta(x) = \sum_{x = 1}^{\infty}(1- \eta(x))<\infty\}
\end{equation} denote the set of all possible configurations that can be obtained if we start with the initial condition $\eta(x) = 1_{x > 0}$ and perform a finite number of moves. Further let $$\hat{\pi} = \otimes_{x \in \Z} \text{Ber}\left(\frac{q^{-x}}{1 + q^{-x}}\right).$$
We then define the blocking measure $\pi$ to be the projection of the measure $\hat{\pi}$ to the set $A$, i.e., $\pi(\cdot)=\hat{\pi}(\cdot|A)$.\footnote{We have an explicit formula for $  \hat \pi(A)$ (see e.g. \cite{MR3765898}):
$\hat \pi(A) = \frac{1}{ \sum_{l = -\infty}^{\infty} q^{l(l+1)/2}}.
$}

[Lemma lem:SAW_bubble of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d \ge 5$.
For any $\gamma > 0$, there is a $\delta = \delta(\gamma) > 0$ such that for $z \in [z_c - \delta, z_c)$ and $\mu \in \Omega_z$,
\begin{equation}
{\sf B}^{(2\mu)}(z) \le {\sf B}^{(0)}(z_c) + \gamma .
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:homogeneous-witness of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Assume that $x_1,\ldots,x_n$ span $\mathbb{R}^d$.  An ellipsoid fit exists if and only if there are $S\in\mathsf{S}^d$ and $b\in\mathbb{R}$ such that
\begin{equation}
S\succeq0,\qquad \|S\|_{\mathrm{F}}=1,\qquad \mathcal{Q}_x(S)=b\mathbf{1},
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{Q}_x(S)=(x_i^\top S x_i-\operatorname{Tr} S)_{i=1}^n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

