[Cnj 1 of arXiv:2609.00415, 'Separation for Schr\"odinger operators. A counterexample to Simon's conjecture'] Let $V(x)=V(|x|)$ on $\R^d; d\geq 5$. Suppose
\begin{enumerate}
  \item $V\geq 0$
  \item $V$ is bounded on any closed set avoiding $0$.
\end{enumerate}
Then $H_0+V$ is closed on $\mathcal{D}(H_0)\cap \mathcal{D}(V)$. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Thm t:P0 of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] Let assumptions $\mathbf{H}^\mathrm{diss}_A$, $\mathbf{H}_{a,b,c}^{\mathrm{Lip}_b}$,
$\mathbf{H}_{\nu,p},$
$\mathbf{H}_A^{\mathrm{Lip}_+}$,
and
$\mathbf{H}_{A_x,A_{xx}}$ hold.
Then, for any $T\in[0,\infty)$, any
$p_X\in [p, p+\kappa-1)$
and any
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}

\gamma
<\begin{cases}
\frac{p(p+\kappa-1 - p_X)}{(\chi+2)(\kappa-1)+\chi p},&\quad p\leq \chi+2, \\
\frac{p+\kappa-1 - p_X}{\kappa+\chi-1},  &\quad  p> \chi+2,
\end{cases}
\end{aligned}\end{equation}
we have
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned} \sup_{t\in[0,T]}
 \mathbf{E}\|X^n_t-X_t\|^{p_X}
\leq_C  h_n^{\gamma }(1+\|x\|^{p+\kappa-1}).
\end{aligned}\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:bushre of arXiv:2606.05830, '{ Biased Random Walk on $\mathbb Z_+$ with Traps of Linearly Increasing Depth}\footnote{Su'] Fix $k\ge 2$. Then for $0<\lambda\ne 1,$ we have
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}[R_{k-1}] =
     \frac{2}{1-\lambda}\lambda^{-(k-2)} - \frac{1+\lambda}{1-\lambda},
 \end{align}
 and there exists a constant $c_1>0$  such that for all $k\ge 2$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}[R_{k-1}^2] \le c_1 \bigl(\mathbb{E}[R_{k-1}]\bigr)^2.
\end{align}

