[Lem finite-catch-up of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Suppose that Equation~(equation eq:persistent of the paper) is satisfied. Then, in the process $(\mathscr{T}_{t})_{t \geq 0}$, the set 
    \begin{equation} 
    \mathcal{P} := \left\{u \in \mathcal{U}\colon u \text{ catches up to each of its ancestors}\right\}
    \end{equation}
    is finite almost surely.

