[Lemma lemma_restriction_of_measure_good_approx of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Suppose $\alpha_{0} \neq 0$, and fix $\varepsilon < \frac{\alpha_{0}}{2}$. Let $R>\max\{R_{\overline{\mathbb{Z}}}(\varepsilon),R_{\mu_0}(\varepsilon)\}$, $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $w \in \Omega_n^{(0)}(\mu,2^{-R}\varepsilon)$. Then,
\begin{equation*}
\| \ell^{0}(w) - \mu_0 \| < \frac{6 \varepsilon}{\alpha_{0}}.
\end{equation*}

