body:
[Theorem thm.2 of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] The asymptotic expected size of the ASEP convoy of particle $0$ is of order $\sqrt{n}$ and is universal, that is, independent of $q$. More precisely,
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{n \to \infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}\mathbb{E}_x\left[\# \mathcal{C}_0^n\right] = \sqrt{\frac{4x\left(1-x\right)}{\pi}}.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, without conditioning on the speed of particle $0$, We have
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{n \to \infty}\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}\mathbb{E}\left[\# \mathcal{C}_0^n\right] = \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{4}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

