[Definition order of arXiv:2605.08624, 'On the sum-of-digits measures and Cusick's conjecture via stopped random walks'] Define two maps $L, R \colon 2\mathbb{N}+1 \to 2\mathbb{N}+1$ by
\begin{equation}
L(t) = 2t - 1, \qquad R(t) = 2t + 1.
\end{equation}
We define a partial order $"\preceq"$ on $2\mathbb{N}+1$ as follows:
 $s \preceq t$ if and only if either $s=t$, or there exists a finite sequence $w_1, \ldots, w_n \in \{L, R\}$
such that
\begin{equation}
t =w_n \circ \cdots \circ w_1(s).
\end{equation}

