[Lemma condition for rm=0 of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] If $(\lambda,C^2)\in S$, then $r_\mathcal{C}(\lambda,C^2)=0$ if and only if $\lambda\geq 0$ and

  \begin{equation*}
   C^2 = \frac{(p-1-\lambda)^2}{p^2} \frac{1}{1-\left(\frac{\lambda}{p-1}\right)^{\frac{2p-2}{p}}} \left(\frac{\lambda}{p-1}\right)^\frac{2p-2}{p}.
  \end{equation*}
  The set $\{r_\mathcal{C}=0\}$ is a smooth curve in $S^0 \subset S$ connecting $(0,0)$ to $(p-1,0)$ and $(p-1)k_m^p-\lambda=0$ along that curve.

