[Definition defn:bad of arXiv:2511.17101, 'Central limit theorem for the range of critical branching random walk'] We say a point $v\in\mathcal T^+$ is bad, if
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mathrm{dist}(v,u_0)$ is odd;
\item $\deg(v)=1$, i.e. $v$ is a leaf of $\mathcal T^\infty$;
\item $V(v)=V(\overleftarrow{\overleftarrow v})$.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:malliavin_control_bounds of arXiv:2609.01697, 'Unique ergodicity of projective cocycles over the 2D stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] For any $n \geqslant 0$ and $K, \beta >1$, the derivative $D_W h_n$ satisfies for some
    $C(K, \beta)>0$:
    \begin{equation}
      \|D_W h_n\|_{HS} \leqslant C(K,\beta) \|\vartheta_{2n}\|.
    \end{equation}
     In particular, $h_n \in \mathbb{D}^{1,2}(H_{\mathcal{C}\mathcal{M}})$.

