[Theorem thm:classical-HW of arXiv:2603.07132, 'Quadratic form of heavy-tailed self-normalized random vector with applications in $\alpha$'] If $\xi$ is centered and sub-Gaussian, then there exist universal constants $C,c>0$ such that for any $n\in \mathbb{N}$ and $u>0$, 
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{P}\!\left(\big|Q_n(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{A})-\mathbb{E}[Q_n(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{A})]\big|\geqslant u\right)\leqslant
		C\exp\!\left[-c\,\min\!\left(\frac{u^2}{K^4\|\mathbf{A}\|_{\operatorname{F}}^2},\ \frac{u}{K^2\|\mathbf{A}\|}\right)\right],
	\end{equation*}
	where $K=\|\xi\|_{\psi_2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

